hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"31063","(31063) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari with a similar hadith. Yazid, but he was not mentioned about it, and he was taken by both ends and thrown into the Fire."
"31064","(31064) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: How have you become, O Harith bin Malik? He said: You have become a true believer. He said: Every saying has a truth, so what is true? At that point, he said: I became detached from this world, so I slept at night and spent my day thirsty, as if I was looking at the throne of God. My Lord has appeared for judgment, and it is as if I were looking at the people of Paradise visiting each other in Paradise, and as if I were hearing howling The people of Hell, he said: And he said to him: A servant whose heart was illuminated by faith, and when it was known, he adhered. (Abdul Razzaq 2014, Bazzar 32)"
"31065","(31065) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, he said: Ibn Sabit narrated to us, he said: It was Abdullah bin Rawahih. He takes a group of his companions by the hand and says: Come, let us believe. Come, let us remember God and increase our faith. Come. We remind Him of His obedience, perhaps He will remind us of His forgiveness. (Ahmed 265)"
"31066","(31066) Yazeed told us, he said: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Ali, he said: Islam has three principles. Athafī: Faith, prayer, and congregational prayer. No prayer is accepted except with faith. Whoever believes, prays, whoever prays together, and whoever separates from the congregation. A hand's breadth has taken off the collar of Islam from its neck."
"31067","(31067) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Mutarrif informed us, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Imamah Al-Bahili said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Hayy and laziness are two parts of faith. (Ahmad 2698 Hakim 52)"
"31068","(31068) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, he said: We reported Medina, so we came to Abdullah bin Omar and said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, we will look into the land and meet a people who are asserting He did not decree, so he said: From among the Muslims who pray towards the qiblah. We said: Yes, from among those who pray towards the qiblah. He said: Then he became angry. I even wished I had not asked him. Then he said: If you meet those, tell them that Abdullah bin Omar is innocent of them. And they are free from it. Then he said: If you wish, I can tell you, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: Yes, and he said: We were with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A well-dressed man with a pleasant scent and a beautiful face said: O Messenger of God, what is Islam? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You establish prayer, pay zakat, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, and wash yourself from ritual impurity. He said: You have spoken the truth, so what is faith? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You believe in God, the Last Day, and the angels. By the Book and the Prophets, and by predestination, everything is good and evil, sweet and bitter. He said: You have spoken the truth. Then he departed, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Ali” with the man. He said: “So we all stood together, but we were not able to defeat him.” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted: This is Gabriel, who has come to you to teach you about your religion."
"31069","(31069) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Purity is half of faith."
"31070","(31070) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Layla al-Kindi, on the authority of Hajr ibn Adiyy said: Ali told us that purification is part of faith."
"31071","(31071) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, he said: Ablution is half of faith."
"31072","(31072) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Layla Al-Kindi, on the authority of a boy Lahjar. Hijr saw his son coming out of the stool, so he said: Boy, give me the newspaper from the window, and I heard Ali saying: Purity is half of faith."
"31073","(31073) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria told us, he said: Al-Hawari told me, that Abdullah bin Omar said: He was naked. Religion and its foundations are prayer and zakat, there is no distinction between them, Hajj to the House, and fasting of Ramadan, and among the righteous deeds is honesty. And jihad, get up and go."
"31074","(31074) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Complete The believers have the best character."
"31075","(31075) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abi Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of the stronghold of Al-Khathami, he said: A man came to Ali. And he was in Al-Rahba, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, what do you see in a woman who does not pray? He said: Whoever does not pray is an unbeliever."
"31076","(31076) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Who He established the prayer and paid the zakat, so he mediated faith."
"31077","(31077) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Who He establishes prayer, pays zakat, listens, and obeys, then faith is moderate. And whoever loves God and hates God, and gives to God and withholds from To God, faith has been perfected."
"31078","(31078) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid Al-Kala’i, who said: He took alcohol in my hand and said: O Abu Wahhab, increase the level of faith in yourself. Whoever intentionally abandons an obligatory prayer, you will be absolved of his sin. God, and whoever is freed from God’s protection has disbelieved."
"31079","(31079) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Ali said: Patience is a part of faith in His status. The head is part of the body, so if patience goes, then does faith."
"31080","(31080) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Three people who gathered them together. Faith: being fair to yourself, spending out of frugality, and extending peace to the world."
"31081","(31081) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, on the authority of Ammar: {Indeed, they have no faith} He said: There is no covenant for them."
"31082","(31082) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: No one who has even the weight of a stone in his heart will enter Hell. A mustard seed of faith. (Muslim 93)"
"31083","(31083) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Sa’q ibn Hazan, he said: Aqeel al-Ja’di narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The strongest bond of faith is love for God. And hatred for God. (Taalisi 378, Hakim 480)"
"31084","(31084) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, he said: Issa bin Asim told me, he said: Adi bin Adi told us, He said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to me: As for what follows, faith is obligatory, laws, limits, and sunnahs, so whoever completes them is complete. Faith, and whoever does not complete it has not completed faith. If you live, I will make it clear to you so that you may act upon it. She died before that, so I am not keen on your company."
"31085","(31085) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: The family must This religion is one of four things: entry into the cause of Islam, and it is necessary to have faith and belief in God and in the messengers, the first and the last. And by Jinnah and Hell and resurrection after death, and you must do good deeds, and you must know good knowledge. Your work, then he recited: {And indeed, I am Forgiver of whoever repents and believes and does righteousness and then is guided}"
"31086","(31086) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: They did not say to do something. A disbeliever man abandoned it other than prayer. He said: They used to say: Abandoning it is disbelief."
"31087","(31087) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: He was told: Some people claim that the believers They will enter Hell. He said: By your life, by God, there will be people in it other than believers."
"31088","(31088) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I heard a brother saying and a man asked him: Did you hear Ibn Masoud? He says: Whoever testifies that he is a believer, let him testify that he is in Paradise. He said: Yes."
"31089","(31089) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Waki’ bin Adas Al-Uqaili, on the authority of his uncle Abu Razin: He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The vision on the leg of a bird is as long as it does not pass, then when it passes, it occurs.\n He said: The vision is one of forty-six parts of prophecy.\n He said: And I think he said: Do not tell it except to a friend or someone with an opinion. (Ahmad 12. Hakim 390)"
"31090","(31090) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Muslim’s vision is one of forty-six parts of the prophecy.\n(Bukhari 6988 and Muslim 1774)"
"31091","(31091) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Muslim’s vision is one of forty-six parts of the prophecy. (Muslim 1774, Ahmad 495)"
"31092","(31092) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of a man who used to give fatwas. In Egypt, he said: I asked Abu al-Darda’ about these verses: {For them is good news in the life of this world} He said: No one asked me about it. Since I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: No one has asked me. Before: This is the good vision that a Muslim sees, or is shown to him, and in the afterlife is Paradise. (Tirmidhi 3106 and Ahmad 447)"
"31093","(31093) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: A Muslim’s vision is one of forty-six parts of the prophecy. (Bukhari 6987, Muslim 1774)"
"31094","(31094) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace about the good tidings of this worldly life? He said: The good vision that a Muslim sees, or it is shown to him. (Tirmidhi 3106)"
"31095","(31095) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A good vision is one of seventy parts of prophecy.\n(Muslim 1775. Ahmad 18)"
"31096","(31096) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’bad, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, removed the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and he said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of the Prophet except the good vision that the Muslim saw, or it was shown to him."
"31097","(31097) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: Indeed, prophecy has ceased and the message has ceased, so the people were embarrassed, so he said: There have remained glad tidings, and this is a part of prophecy.\n(Tirmidhi 2272 and Ahmad 267)"
"31098","(31098) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, a man does work and people love him for it? He said: This is good news for the believer.\n(Muslim 1661, Ibn Majah 4225)"
"31099","(31099) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Abu Husayn narrated to me, on the authority of Zahir al-Aslami: on the authority of His father: Abdullah used to say: A righteous and truthful vision is one of seventy parts of prophecy. (Tabarani 9057)"
"31100","(31100) Al-Qasmali narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The believer’s vision is one part of forty-six parts of Prophecy\n(Abu Ali 3417)"
"31101","(31101) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The visions Of the glad tidings, which is one of seventy parts of prophecy."
"31102","(31102) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father: {For them is good news in life. This world} He said: This is the righteous vision that the righteous servant will see. (Malik 958)"
"31103","(31103) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {For them is good news in the life of this world} He said: A good vision is seen by a Muslim, or it is shown to him."
"31104","(31104) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha al-Qannad, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Safid bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {For them Good news in the life of this world} He said: The good vision that a Muslim man sees for himself, or for his brother."
"31105","(31105) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: The Prophet of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The vision of a righteous Muslim man is one of seventy parts of the prophecy.\n(Bukhari 6989. Abu Ali 1357)"
"31106","(31106) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me. (Ahmad 472)"
"31107","(31107) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me. Indeed, Satan does not appear in my form. (Bukhari 6993 and Muslim 1775)"
"31108","(31108) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told me, on the authority of Yazid Al-Farisi, he said: I saw the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in sleep at the time of Ibn Abbas’s sight. He said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace while asleep. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Satan does not He can imitate me, so whoever sees me in sleep has seen me. (Ibn Majah 3905 and Ahmad 279)"
"31109","(31109) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir: That the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Whoever sees me in sleep has seen me. Indeed, Satan does not appear in your form.\n(Muslim 1776. Ahmad 3)"
"31110","(31110) Affan told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Mukhtar told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Anas told us, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not imitate me.\n(Bukhari 6994, Abu Ali 3271)"
"31111","(31111) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Jesus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya Al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not It is imitated by. (Bukhari 6997, Ibn Majah 3903)"
"31112","(31112) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir: A man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I saw as if my neck had been struck! He said: Why would any of you tell of Satan playing with him?! (Muslim 1776. Ahmad 383)"
"31113","(31113) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, I saw in a dream as if my head was cut off! He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at him and said: If Satan plays with one of you in his dream, he should not tell people about him. (Muslim 1777. Ahmad 315)"
"31114","(31114) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Al-Hussein, he said: Ata bin Abi narrated to me. Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I saw in a dream as if My head was hit, and I saw it in this hand! He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Satan goes to one of you and he turns to him, then in the morning he informs People! (Ibn Majah 3911 and Ahmad 364)"
"31115","(31115) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudharib: that a man saw Vision: Whoever prays the night in the mosque will enter Paradise! Then Abdullah bin Masoud came out and said: Go out, do not be deceived, for Satan has inflated you!"
"31116","(31116) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I saw in my hands two bracelets of gold, so I blew them open and put them on them. The liars: Musaylimah and Al-Ansi. (Bukhari 3421, Muslim 1781)"
"31117","(31117) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw It is as if I had two bracelets of gold in my hands. I took them apart and blew them, and they went away: broken and short."
"31118","(31118) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I saw a man emerging from the earth, and upon his head was a man with an iron clamp in his hand. Whenever he came out He hit his head and entered the ground, then he came out from another place, and he came to it and hit his head and said: That Abu Jalal bin Hisham, this will still be done to him until the Day of Resurrection."
"31119","(31119) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to Abu Bakr: I saw me being followed by black sheep, followed by Afar sheep. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, these Arabs will follow you, the non-Arabs will follow them. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Likewise The king crossed her.\n(Hakim 3951, Ahmad 455)"
"31120","(31120) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Al-Sayyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Likewise, the king made her pass by magic."
"31121","(31121) Zaid told us, he said: Sufyan bin Husayn informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I saw his shadow dripping with ghee and honey. It is as if the people were taking from it, and it was abundant and it was independent, and in between, and it was as if a reason was dropped from the heavens. So you came and took it and acted, so God exalted you, then a man came after you and took it and acted, so God exalted you, then he came A man came after you, and he took it and did it, so God exalted him. Then a man came after you and he took it, then he broke off with it, then He attained his deeds, so God exalted him.\n Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, give me permission and I will cross it. So he gave him permission and said: As for the shade, it is Islam, and as for the fat. And honey, then it is the Qur’an, and as for the cause, it is what you are upon. You rise up, and God will exalt you, then there will be a man after you upon you. Your speech will be raised, so God will raise it. Then there will be a man after you, and he will take you both, and he will raise it, and He will raise it. God, then there will be a man after you on your approach, then it will be cut off from it, then it will be connected to it, then it will rise, and God will exalt it. He said: Are you correct, O Messenger of God? He said: You were right and wrong. He said: You swore, O Messenger of God, that you would inform me. He said: Do not swear. (Bukhari 7046 and Muslim 1777)"
"31122","(31122) Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Early, on the authority of his father, he said: We delegated with Ziyad to Muawiyah, and he was not as impressed with the delegation as he was with us, he said: So he said: O Abu Tomorrow! Tell us something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: She was amazed at the beautiful vision when he asked about her - so I heard him say: I saw as if a balance had been sent down from the heavens and she was weighed. In it, Abu Bakr and I were in favor of Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr and Omar were weighed, and Abu Bakr preferred, then Omar and Othman were weighed. So Omar gave the victory to Othman, then the scales were raised to the heavens, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Caliphate and prophethood, then God gives dominion to whomsoever He wills. He said: Then he attacked us and drove us out. (Abu Dawud 4610, Tirmidhi 2287)"
"31123","(31123) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, he said: Salem told me, about a vision The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the epidemic of Medina, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I saw a black woman with a disheveled head leaving the city to go to bed, so I interpreted it as an epidemic. Medina was transferred to Maya. (Bukhari 7038. Tirmidhi 2290)"
"31124","(31124) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Badr bin Othman, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Marwan, on the authority of Abu Aisha, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us one morning and said: I just saw that you were given Scales and scales. As for the scales, these are the keys. They were placed on a palm, and my nation was placed on a palm, so they prevailed. With them, then Abu Bakr was brought and he prevailed, then Omar was brought and he prevailed, then Uthman was brought and he prevailed, he said: Then it was raised, he said: so he said He has a man: Where are we? He said: Where you have placed yourselves. (Ahmed 76)"
"31125","(31125) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Salim narrated to me, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw in sleep as if I was taking off a bucket. He was a virgin at the heart of Qalib, then Abu Bakr came and committed one or two sins, but he committed a weak sin, and may God forgive him. Then Omar ibn al-Khattab came and drew water, and it turned west. I did not see any genius among the people running away with it, until the people were told and beaten. With a curse (Bukhari 3676. Muslim 19)"
"31126","(31126) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, he said: Samurah bin Jundub narrated to us, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to his companions: Has any of you seen a vision? Then he would narrate it. God did not wish to tell the story, so he said to us one morning: “Indeed, two or two doubts came to me during the night, and they said to me: He went, and I went with them, and we came to a man lying down, and behold, another was standing over him on a rock, and behold, he He falls into the rock for his head, and it strikes his head, and the stone hits him here and takes him, and he does not return. To him until his head is healthy as it was, then he returns to him and he does to him the same as the first time. He said: I said to them: Glory be to God, what is this? They said to me: Go.\n So we set off until we came upon a man lying on his back, and behold, another was standing over him with an iron club. And behold, he was coming to him. One side of his face, so his cheeks point to the back of his face, his eyes to the back of him, and his nostrils to the back of him, then it turns to The other side, and he does the same to it, and it is not finished until that side is healthy as it was, then it returns. And he did to him as he did the first time. So I said to them: Glory be to God, what is this? He said: They said to me: Go, go.So we set off until we came to someone like someone who builds an oven. He said: I think he said: We heard confusion and noises therein. So we looked up, and behold! Therein are naked men and women, and when a flame comes to them from below them, then when that flame comes to them, they become disturbed. He said: I said to them: Who are these? He said: They said to me: Go, go.\n He said: So we set off until we came to a river - I thought he said red - like blood. In the river, behold, a man swimming. On the shore of the river there was a man who had gathered many stones, and behold, that swimmer swam as long as he swam, then he came. He is the one who gathered stones, and his mouth opened for them, and he threw a stone at him, and he went and swam what he swam, then Then came the one who, whenever he returned, had his mouth wide open and he threw a stone at him. He said: I said: What is this? He said: They said: To me: Go, go.\n He said: So we set off, and we came upon a man who hated a mirror as much as you hate seeing a man who hates a mirror, and lo, he was by a fire. He filled it and ran around it. He said: I said to them: What is this? They said to me: Go, go.So we set off until we came to a meadow that was dark with all the light of the spring, and behold, between the two sides of the meadow was a man. He is so tall that I can hardly see his head so tall in the sky. And when around him was a man of the most beautiful sons I have ever seen and the best of them, he said: I said: Lama: What is this? And what are these? He said: They told me: Go.\n So we set out, and we came to a great staircase. I had never seen a stairway greater or better than it. He said: They said to me: Rest in it. So we ascended it and came to a city built with bricks of gold and bricks of silver. He said: So we came to the gate of the city. So we inquired about it and it was opened for us, so we entered it and there we met men of a half of their creation, like the best of you. You are a smart seer. As ugliest as you can see. He said: They said to them: Go and fall into that river. He said: And behold, an obstructing river was flowing. As if its water was pure white. He said: So they went and fell into it, then they returned to us, and the evil had gone away from them and they had become In its best form.\n He said: They said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and this is your abode. He said: So he directed his sight upwards, and when he turned short, like The white lords. He said: They said to him: This is your abode. He said: I said to them: May God bless you both. So let him enter him, he said: They said to me: But now no, and you will enter him.He said: I said to them: You saw a wonder this night, so what is this that you saw? He said: They said: As for us, we will inform you. As for the first man whom you came to who had his head cut off with a stone, he was a man who had taken The Qur’an and sleeps without the obligatory prayers. As for the man upon whom you came whose mouth, eyes, and nostrils are spread out to the back of his head, then he is a man coming from his house. So he lies, the lie reaches all horizons. As for the naked men and women who are like those building an oven, they are adulterers and harlots. As for the man who swims in the river and throws stones, he is a usurer. As for the man who is near the Fire and hates the mirror, then he is Malik, the keeper of Hell. As for the tall man in the meadow, he is Abraham, and as for the children around him, every child who died was Al-Fitra, he said: Then some Muslims said: O Messenger of God, and the children of the polytheists? He said: And the children of the polytheists.\n As for the people of whom half is like the ugliest thing you have seen and half is like the best thing you have seen, then they are a people who have mixed good deeds. And others were bad, but God overlooked them. (Bukhari 1386, Muslim 1781)"
"31127","(31127) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdaliya, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Kharsha bin Al-Hurr said: I came to Medina and sat with the sheikhs in the mosque, the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then an old man came, leaning on a staff, and the people said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look. To this, he said: So he stood behind a pole and prayed two rak'ahs, and I stood up to him and said to him: Some people said such-and-such. He said: Paradise is God’s and He may enter it whomsoever He wishes. And I saw a vision at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I saw as if a man was coming, and he said to me: Go, so I went with him, and he took me on a great path, so I appeared to him. A path to my left, so I wanted to take it, but it was said: You are not one of its people. Then a path was shown to me on my right. So I followed it until I came to a slippery mountain. He took me by the hand and let me in. When I was at its peak, I neither descended nor descended. I was holding on to you, and behold, there was an iron pillar with a gold ring at its top. He took it in my hand and pushed me until I took hold of the loop.\n He said: Hold on to it, and I said: Yes, so he struck the pillar with his foot and held on to the handle.\n So I narrated it to the Messenger of God, and he said: I saw good. As for the great approach: the gathering, and as for the path that turned away from... Your left path is the path of the people of Hell, and you are not of its people. As for the path that turned away from your right, it is the path of the people of Hell. Paradise, and as for the slippery mountain: it is the abode of the martyrs, and as for the robe that you held on to: it is the robe of Islam, so hold on to you. With it until you die.\n He said: I hope to be among the people of Paradise. He said: Then he is Abdullah bin Salam. (Bukhari 3814, Muslim 148)"
"31128","(31128) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: I saw as if I was in the house of Uqba bin Rafi’ and we were brought with dates from Ibn Taab’s dates, so I interpreted: The superiority is for us in This world, and the consequences in the Hereafter, and that our religion is good. (Muslim 1779. Abu Dawud 4986)"
"31129","(31129) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I saw as if I was wearing a fortified shield, and I saw a beheaded cow, so I interpreted: The shield is the city. And the cows are a group. (Dharmi 2159, Bazar 2133)"
"31130","(31130) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: I saw, as the sleeper saw, as if I was flanking a ram, and as if the lion of my sword had been broken, so I interpreted. I will kill the writer of the book. Affan said: There was something after this, I don’t know what it was. (Bazzar 2131. Tabarani 2951)"
"31131","(31131) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath bin Abd al-Rahman al-Jarami told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub: A man said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I saw as if I had been given a bucket of Heaven, then Abu Bakr came and took some of its Iraqis and drank a drink that was weak, then Omar came and took some of its Iraqis and drank until He sat down, then Othman came and took some of her Iraqi food and drank until he sat down. (Abu Dawud 4413. Tabarani 6965)"
"31132","(31132) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw in a dream as if irrigation was running between my fingernails, or My nails, they said: What did you explain? He said: Knowledge. (Bukhari 3681, Muslim 1859)"
"31133","(31133) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan, so if one of you sees something He hates it, let him blow off his veil three times, and let him seek refuge in God from its evil, for it will not harm him."
"31134","(31134) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If one of you sees a vision that he hates, let him spit on his left side three times, and seek refuge. By God, from Satan three times, and let him turn away from the side he was upon."
"31135","(31135) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Visions have a universe, and they have names, so they created them with their names and expressed them with their names, and visions are for the first time. Passing by\n(Ibn Majah 3915; Abu Ali 4117)"
"31136","(31136) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Suhayb passed by Abu Bakr and he turned away. He said: Why did you turn away from me? Did I tell you something that you hated? He said: No, by God, only a vision that you saw that you hated. He said: And what did you see? He said: I saw your hand tied to your neck at the door of an Ansar man called: Abu Al-Hashr! Then Abu Bakr said to him: What you saw was excellent. It has fulfilled my debt until the Day of Judgment."
"31137","(31137) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab: that Aisha said to her father: I saw During sleep, it was as if the moon had fallen into my room until she mentioned three times, and Abu Bakr said to her: If your visions come true, he will be buried in Your House is the best people on earth: three. (Tabarani 127)"
"31138","(31138) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi: That a man came to Abu Bakr and said: I saw in a dream It is as if I am urinating blood. He said: I see you having intercourse with your wife while she is menstruating. He said: Yes. He said: So fear God and do not transgress."
"31139","(31139) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man came to Abu Bakr and said: I saw in a dream It is as if I was luring a fox. He said: You are a lying man, so fear God and do not repeat it."
"31140","(31140) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Aisha said to Abu Bakr: I saw in a dream Cows are being slaughtered around me. He said: If your vision comes true, a group will be killed around you!"
"31141","(31141) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d. Al-Ghatafani, on the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha al-Amari: Omar bin Al-Khattab said on the day of Friday prayer, or he delivered a sermon on the day of Friday prayer, He thanked God and praised Him, then said: O people! I saw a red rooster that pecked me twice, and I do not see that as anything other than the presence of my life. \n(Muslim 397. Ahmad 48)"
"31142","(31142) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Jariyah bin Qadamah Al-Saadi, he said: Hajj was the year in which Omar was injured. He said: Then he got engaged and said: I saw as if a rooster pecked me two or three times."
"31143","(31143) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Harith Al-Khuza’i, who said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying in his sermon: Yesterday I saw a rooster pecking me, and I saw people removing it from me. He only stayed for three days until Abd al-Mughirah, Abu Lulu’a, killed him. (Bayhaqi 232)"
"31144","(31144) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem informed me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a dream, and I saw him not looking at me, so I said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with me? He said: Aren't you the one who kisses while you are fasting? I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not kiss her after that while I am fasting."
"31145","(31145) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: More than one person narrated to me: that a judge from the people of Syria Omar bin Al-Khattab came and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I saw a vision that frightened me. He said, “What is it?” He said: I saw the sun and the moon fighting, and the stars were divided into two halves. He said: Whichever of them you were with, he said: With the moon over the sun. Then Omar said: And We made the night and the day as signs, so We erased the signs of the night and made the signs of the day visible. He said: So he set off. By God, you will never do anything for me."
"31146","(31146) Surayj bin Al-Nu’man narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of His father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab addressed the people, and he said: I saw in my dream a red rooster who pecked me on the knot of my garment three times. Clicks, so Asma bint Umays interpreted them, and she said: If your visions come true, a non-Arab man will kill you."
"31147","(31147) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Hamza narrated to me, on the authority of Yazid bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abi Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al Ashja’i, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The visions are of three types: Among them is the fear of Satan to make the son of Adam sad, and among them is the matter that he speaks to himself in the wake of the day and he sees it in A dream, including forty-six parts of prophecy. (Ibn Majah 3907. Ibn Hibban 6042)"
"31148","(31148) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: There are three types of visions: good news from God, self-talk, and fear from Satan. If one of you sees a vision that he likes, let him tell it if he wishes, and if he sees something that he dislikes, let him tell it to no one and let him He prays. \n(Bukhari 7017 and Muslim 1773)"
"31149","(31149) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: Abdullah said: There are three visions: the presence of Satan, the man talking to himself during the day and then he sees God, and the visions that Visions"
"31150","(31150) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Hilal bint Waki`, on the authority of Uthman’s wife, she said: Uthman fell asleep, and when he woke up he said: The people are killing me. I said: No, Amir. The believers. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar. He said: So they said: Break your fast with us. The night, or he said: You break your fast with us the night."
"31151","(31151) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: that Uthman became He spoke to people, saying: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a dream that night, and he said: O Uthman, break your fast with us. Then he fasted in the morning and was killed that day."
"31152","(31152) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I like shackles in a dream. And I hate deception. The bond is steadfastness in religion, and Abu Hurairah said: Milk in a dream is the sign of unbreakable nature."
"31153","(31153) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: You saw me on a hill It was as if cows were being slaughtered all around me, and Masruq said: If you can not be her, then do so. He said: So you have been afflicted with that. May God have mercy on her."
"31154","(31154) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, that she killed an offender, so she was brought as the sleeper saw, and it was said to her: By God, you killed a Muslim. She said: Why did the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, enter upon me? It was said to her: He does not enter upon you unless you have your clothes on. So she became terrified and ordered twelve thousand, and they were sent to the God"
"31155","(31155) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khattimi, on the authority of Amara ibn Khuzaymah bin Thabit, on the authority of his father: He saw in a dream as if he was prostrating on the forehead of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The spirit To meet the spirit, or he said: The spirit to meet the spirit. Yazid doubted, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, convinced him and gave him his head, then ordered him to do so. So he prostrated behind him on the forehead of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"31156","(31156) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid and Abu Imran al-Junai told us: Samura ibn Jundub said to Abu Bakr: I saw in a dream as if I was unwinding a ribbon and placing it next to me and a coin. We ate it. He said: Marry a woman who has a child and he will eat your earnings. He said: And I saw a bull come out of a hole, but he was not able to get back into it. He said: This great bone came out from the man’s mouth, but it did not. He can turn it back. He said: And I saw as if it was said: The Antichrist is coming out, so I started to storm the walls, and he turned around behind me. Then the earth opened for me, so I entered it. He said: A calamity will strike you in your religion, and the Antichrist will soon be upon you."
"31157","(31157) Abdullah bin Bakr told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: I saw what the sleeper sees as if Abdullah bin Omar was eating dates, so I wrote to him: I saw you eating dates, which are the sweetness of faith, God willing. Come on"
"31158","(31158) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Ziyad Al-Adawi said: In my sleep, I saw as if I was seeing an old man with one blind eye and the other almost gone. It was adorned with emeralds and some amazing jewellery. He said: I said: What are you? She said: The world. I said: I seek refuge in God from your evil. She said: If it pleases you that God protect you from evil, then hate dirhams."
"31159","(31159) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Fudail bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I asked him about drinking, and he said: Between a drinker and a deserter."
"31160","(31160) Affan told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: It was said to Muhammad bin Sirin: So-and-so is laughing, he said: And why? He does not laugh, for someone better than him laughed. It was narrated that Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. And he was safe from a vision that was told to him by a man who laughed. I have never seen him laugh at anything more intense than this. Muhammad said: And I knew what The vision, and what is its interpretation. He saw as if his head had been cut off. He said: So he went to follow it, for the head was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the man wants to join his work with the work of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he does not overtake you."
"31161","(31161) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik: that Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, or Anas, said: I saw in a dream as if I had taken a large number of horses and ridden them until they reached a mountain. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on top of the mountain, with Abu Bakr beside him and gesturing with his hand towards Omar. So I said: To God we belong, and to Him we shall return. He died, and God is Omar, so I said: Don’t you write it to Omar? He said: I was not referring to Omar. Himself"
"31162","(31162) Husayn bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’: that Ibn Umar saw a vision: as if he was an angel. He was taken to the Fire, and another angel met him and shook him, and he said: You are not alarmed. This is an excellent man if he were to pray from The night, he said: After that he used to prolong the prayer into the night, he said: He ended up with me in Hell and I say: I seek refuge in God From the Fire, and behold, it is narrow like a house, its bottom is wide and its top is narrow, and behold, there are men from Quraysh whom I know. They are crossed with their feet.\n(Bukhari 1156, Muslim 1928)"
"31163","(31163) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymimi say: The only thing that brought me to this gathering of mine was that I saw as if I was dividing perfume among the people, so I mentioned that to Abraham. Al-Nakha'i, and he said: Basil has a bitter appearance and taste."
"31164","(31164) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shibl, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And you taught me of interpretation. Hadiths} He said: Expressions of visions."
"31165","(31165) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad: He heard a people mentioning a vision. While he was praying, when he left, he asked them about it, but they concealed it. He said: The interpretation of Joseph’s vision came after forty. Meaning: Sunnah."
"31166","(31166) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: A man asked Muhammad, he said: Did you see it as if I was eating something special during prayer? He said: Khubays is permissible, but it is not permissible for you to eat it during prayer. So he said to him: Do you kiss your wife while you are fasting? He said: Yes. He said: Do not do that."
"31167","(31167) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: He was in the midst of Yusuf’s visions. And its interpretation takes forty years."
"31168","(31168) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abdullah bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: When he saw... One of them did not hate it. He said: I seek refuge with what God’s angels and His Messenger have sought refuge with from the evil of what I saw in my dream. Something happens to me that I hate in this world and the hereafter."
"31169","(31169) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Sirin and he was asked about A man saw in a dream that he had a sharpened sword with him, and he said: A boy was born. He said: The sword struck, he said: He will die.\n He said: Ibn Sirin was asked about stones in sleep, and he said: Hardening.\n He was asked about wood during sleep, and he said: Hypocrisy."
"31170","(31170) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He was asked about a man who saw a light in the middle of the night, and he said: If this were good, the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, would look at it."
"31171","(31171) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: Salah bin Ashim said: I saw in my sleep as if I was in a group, and there was a man behind me who had a sword, pointing it at him. He said: Whenever he came upon one of us, He hit his head and fell, then he sat down and went back to the way he was. He said: So I set to wait when he would come to me and do that to me. He said: Then he came to me and hit my head and it fell, and it was as if I was looking at my head when I took it, shaking the dust from my lips, then I took it and returned it as it was."
"31172","(31172) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: He said: I saw Abu Rifa’ after He has never been afflicted with sleeping on a fast camel, while I was on a camel with dried dung, and I was following it. He said: So he turned it to me. So I say: Now let me hear the voice, so he released it, and I follow in his footsteps. He said: So I interpreted my visions of him taking the path of Abu Rifa’ah and I. I work harder after that. (Hakim 432)"
"31173","(31173) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit: Abu Thamer saw what a sleeper sees: Woe. For the fat women who have lost their bones on the Day of Resurrection."
"31174","(31174) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul-Malik said: A brother of Al-Hajjaj entered and said: What is your name? He said: The prince did not send for me until he knew my name. He said: I want to seek your help in some of my work. He said: He said: But I am afraid. You have my soul, so he asked for his pardon and he pardoned him. He said: When he left him, he stood up and said: This is how he lives. He said: So he said: Pilgrims: Help the Sheikh, Help the Sheikh."
"31175","(31175) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, who said: Ibn Awsat sent Ash-Sha’bi to Al-Hajjaj and he was working on Al-Ray, he said: Then he entered upon Ibn Abi Muslim, and the one between him and him was kind. He said: So Ibn Abi Muslim treated him, And he said: I will introduce you to the prince, but if he laughs in your face, do not make you laugh. He said: So I will introduce you to him."
"31176","(31176) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of a sheikh from Nakha, on the authority of his grandmother, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr was concealed. At the time of your father, the pilgrims, your father took it in a box to Mecca."
"31177","(31177) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Al-Walid ibn Uqba said while he was giving a sermon: O people of Kufa, I am determined that the one who fattened me felt blessed when he stood up. Udayy was embarrassed by his resolve, so he stood up and said to him: It is He is the one who mourns you and says: I am the one who named you. Ibn Aoun said: And he was the one who named you."
"31178","(31178) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, he said: They were talking. He said: Then Ali came out. He passed by, and with him was Aqeel. He said: And with Aqeel was a ram. He said: Then Ali said: He bit one of us with his penis. He said: Then Aqeel said: As for me? And Kabshi, no."
"31179","(31179) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of a scholar, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla entered the presence of al-Hajjaj and said: To those sitting with him: If you want to look at a man cursing the Commander of the Faithful Othman, then this is with you - meaning: Abdul Rahman - Then Abdul-Rahman said: May God forbid, O prince, that I should curse Othman, for he would have restrained me from that for three verses in The Book of God, God said: {For the poor immigrants who were expelled from their homes and their wealth, seeking bounty from God. and satisfaction, and they help Allah and His Messenger. Those are the truthful. He said: Then Othman was among them. He said: Then he said: {And those who repented. abode and faith before them,” and he was one of them who refused: “And those who came after them say, “Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers.” Those who preceded us in faith} So I was one of them. He said: You have spoken the truth."
"31180","(31180) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Wahhab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali: Who are you from? He said: I said: from a people whom people hate: from Thaqif."
"31181","(31181) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi said to Ali: Write to These two men are on their promise to Kufa and Basra, meaning Al-Zubayr and Talha, and he wrote to Muawiyah With his return to the Levant, he will be pleased with you for that. He said: Ali said: I would not give this worldly life in exchange for my religion. He said: After that, the raider met Muawiyah, and Muawiyah said to him: Are you the one who spoke? He said: Yes. He said: Or, by God, no one can protect her from evil except God."
"31182","(31182) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Ziyad wrote to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers: From Ziyad bin Abi Sufyan, hoping that you would write to him: Ibn Abi Sufyan, he said, so I wrote to him: From Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, to Ziyad, her son."
"31183","(31183) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Ali, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: I have never sat with the family of His house is like this: meaning: Ali bin Hussein."
"31184","(31184) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: A man said to Al-Hasan: O Abu Saeed, by God, I never see you composing. He said: My nephew, you have preceded the tune."
"31185","(31185) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Asbahani, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Asbaani narrated to me. Shaddad, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Don’t you like me? He said: One day I was at home and I took my bed, according to the one who said it, when it was said: A man at the door. He said: I said: This one did not come. This is the hour, except for a need. Come in. He said: Then he entered. He said: I said: Do you have a need? He said: When will that man be sent? I said: What man? He said: Ali. He said: I said: He will not be resurrected until God resurrects those in the graves! He said: He said: You say what these fools say! He said: I said: Take this away from you."
"31186","(31186) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, who said: Al-Sha’bi found two men who were backbiting him and falling into him, so he said:\nBlessed and well-pleased, free from the disease of intoxication, for Your honor is one of our honors as long as they have become lawful"
"31187","(31187) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, who said: When Sa’id bin Jubayr entered upon al-Hajjaj, He said: You are Al-Shaqiy ibn Kusair. He said: No, I am Saeed ibn Jubayr. He said: I will kill you. He said: If you kill me, you will kill me. My mother used my name."
"31188","(31188) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aisha: Indeed, a man Of the freedmen, he pledges allegiance to him - meaning: Muawiyah - she said: O my son, do not be surprised, this is the kingdom of God, which He will give to whomever Yessssssssss"
"31189","(31189) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Uqba: He said: There was no prophecy except that there was a kingdom after it."
"31190","(31190) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab: That a man from Quraysh, called Thumama, was On Sana'a, when he came to him when he killed Uthman, he wept for a long time, and when he woke up, he said: Today the prophecy - or its successors - has been taken away. Prophethood - from the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she became a king and a tyrant. Whoever conquers something will eat it."
"31191","(31191) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Al-Hasan said to me: Aren’t you surprised by Sa’id bin Jubayr? He came to me and asked me about the fight between Al-Hajjaj and some of the leaders with him, meaning: the companions of Ibn Al-Ash’ath."
"31192","(31192) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, who said: I heard Mu’awiyah say during his illness that he died. Therein, he lowered his arms as if they were branches of palm trees, and said: By God, I wish I had not disgraced you above... Three, and they said: May God have mercy and forgive him, and he said: It is what God wills that he should do, even if he disliked it, he would have done something different.\n Ibn Bishr added: Is there anything in this world except what we know and have experienced?!"
"31193","(31193) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Qais, he said: Qais bin Rumanani narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: He said: Muawiyah: She did not fight Ali except on the orders of Uthman."
"31194","(31194) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: A young man from Quraysh entered upon Mu’awiyah and treated him harshly, so he said: He said to him: O nephew, forbid you from authority, for the authority becomes as angry as a boy and becomes as angry as a lion."
"31195","(31195) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, he said: Ziyad said: The Commander of the Faithful has not defeated me. With any kind of politics, except for one matter. I employed so-and-so, and he broke his tax, and he was afraid that I would punish him, so he fled to the Commander of the Faithful. So he wrote to her: This is bad manners for those before me. So he wrote to me: It is not appropriate for you or me to touch people. One policy, that we should be all too soft so that the people would fall into disobedience, and not that we should all be too harsh so that we would force the people to commit sins. Your fates, but I will be for severity, harshness, and harshness, and I will be for gentleness, compassion, and mercy."
"31196","(31196) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, he said: Aamir told us, he said: I heard Mu’awiyah saying: You have not dispersed. He has never been a mother except that the people of falsehood prevail over the people of truth except this mother."
"31197","(31197) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Suwayd, he said: Pray with us. Mu'awiyah led the gathering with palm trees in the morning, then he addressed us and said: I did not fight you so that you would pray, nor fast, nor perform Hajj, nor That you may be pure, and I know that you do that, but I only fought you to conspire over you, for God has given me that. And you hate it."
"31198","(31198) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Huzayl bin Shurahbil, he said: He addressed them. Mu'awiyah, and he said: O people! You have come and pledged allegiance to me, obediently, and if you had pledged allegiance to a renewed Ethiopian slave, I would have come and pledged allegiance to him with you. He said: Then when He came down from the pulpit and Amr ibn Al-Aas said to him: Do you know what I brought today?! You claimed that the people pledged allegiance to you willingly, and if they had pledged allegiance to an obedient Ethiopian slave, you would have come and pledged allegiance to them. He said: So he stood up. Mu'awiyah went to the pulpit and said: O people! Was there anyone more deserving of this matter than me?"
"31199","(31199) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: Mu’awiyah said: There is no dream except Experiments"
"31200","(31200) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, who said: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me: That Hussein bin Ali entered upon Muawiyah and said: I will reward you with a reward that I have not rewarded anyone before you, and I will not reward anyone after you. Arabs, so he granted him four hundred thousand, so he accepted it."
"31201","(31201) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, he said: Abdullah bin Buraida narrated to us, he said: I entered And my father refused to speak to Muawiyah, so he made my father sit on the bed and brought the food and he fed us. He brought a drink and he drank. Then Muawiyah said: What is the matter? There is something I used to enjoy when I was young and I take it today except milk, so I take it as I used to take it before today. And the good hadith."
"31202","(31202) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhallim Al-Hamdani narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man came to Muawiyah. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have promised you what you promised me. He said: What did I promise you? He said: That you increase my giving by a hundred. He said: I did not. He said: Yes. He said: Who knows that? Al-Aswad, or Ibn Al-Aswad, said: What does this say, O Ibn Al-Aswad? He said: Yes, I have increased it, so he commanded her to do so, then Muawiyah struck his hands, one of them against the other, and he said: What is the matter? I added a hundred to a man, but because of your neglect, I added a hundred to a man from among the immigrants. Then he forgot about it, so Ibn al-Aswad said to him: O Commander of the Faithful! So he believed in her? He said: Yes, he said: By God, I have not increased anything for you, but no man calls me to something good that befalls him from someone of authority, but I bear witness. He has it, and I do not turn away any evil from him except that I bear witness to it."
"31203","(31203) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told me, on the authority of Wahhab bin Kaysan, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah says: When it was the year of the Jama’ah, Mu’awiyah sent Busr ibn Arta to Medina to sell its people to Ali. Their banners and their tribes. Then when the Ansar came to him, and Banu Salamah came to him, he said: Is Jabir among them? They said: No. He said: Let them return, for I will not pledge allegiance to them until Jabir comes. He said: So he came to me and said: I appealed to you by God except for what You set off with us and pledged allegiance and shed your blood and the blood of your people. If you do not do so, our fighter will be killed and our children taken captive. He said: So I waited for them until the night, and when evening came, I went to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I informed her. The news and she said: O son of my brother, go and pledge allegiance and spare your blood and the blood of your people, for I have ordered my nephew to go. So he pledges allegiance."
"31204","(31204) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, who said: A man from the people of Iraq to Ibn al-Zubayr when he was sold out: Peace be upon you, for I praise God to you, there is no god but Him. As for what follows: For the people who obey God and for the people of goodness there are signs by which they are known and which are known about them: from enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong. And work in obedience to God, and know that the example of an imam is like a market: he will come to him as he was in it, and if it is righteous, then his family will come. Righteousness is due to righteousness, even if he is an immoral person, he will recompense the people of immorality for their immorality."
"31205","(31205) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahhab, he said: I was with Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, and it was said to him: Al-Mukhtar claims that it was revealed to him, so he said: He spoke the truth, then he recited {Shall I inform you? On whom do the devils descend? On whom do all the evil creatures descend?"
"31206","(31206) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Anas, who said: There will be kings, then The tyrants, then the tyrants."
"31207","(31207) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, he said: We used to narrate that the children of so-and-so were afflicted by A severe killing, and when that happened, four of them fled to the Romans, so they brought the Romans against the Muslims."
"31208","(31208) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem told me, he said: When they wanted to pledge allegiance to Yazid Bin Muawiyah, Marwan stood up and said: The Sunnah of Abu Bakr al-Rashidi al-Mahdi. Then Abdul Rahman bin Abu Bakr stood up and said: He is not of the same age as Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr left his family, clan, and origin, and joined a man from the Banu Adi bin Ka`b saw that he was worthy of that, so he pledged allegiance to him."
"31209","(31209) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Aamir, who said: Muhammad ibn Al-Ash’ath said: Every thing has a state, even Indeed, foolishness has its effect on dreaming."
"31210","(31210) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem informed me, on the authority of his father: that when Omar removed Sharhabeel bin Hassani said: O Umar, did you turn away from my anger? He said: No, but we saw someone stronger than you, so we were embarrassed by God to leave you, even though we saw someone stronger than you. Then Sharhabeel said to him: Excuse me. Omar stood up on the pulpit and said: We used Sharhabeel bin Hasna, then we removed him. Other than his displeasure, I found it against him, but we saw someone stronger than him, so we were embarrassed by God to acknowledge him, and he had We saw someone stronger than him, so Omar looked from the evening at the people as they sought refuge with the worker who had been employed. And Sharhabeel Muhtab was alone, so Omar said: As for this world, it is enough."
"31211","(31211) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, on the authority of Muhammad Al-Kateb: that Omar used to say: This matter is not appropriate. Except for severity other than arrogance, and softness other than weakness."
"31212","(31212) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, he said: My father told me, he said: Ali said: By the One who split the grain and brought forth the breeze, removing mountains from their place is easier than removing a deferred king."
"31213","(31213) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak bin Salama, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Asma, he said: I was with Aisha when a messenger from Mu'awiyah came to her with a gift and said: The Commander of the Faithful has sent this, so she accepted. I guided him. When the Messenger came out, we said: O Mother of the Believers, are we not believers while he is our commander? She said: You are believers, God willing, and he is your commander."
"31214","(31214) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Uthman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Tamim ibn Hudhalam, who said: The first day of the salaam Ali, the prince of Kufa, said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba left the palace, and a man from Canada came to him and greeted him. He asked him about the woman, and he said: What is this? I am but one of them. I left it for a while, then he continued it after that."
"31215","(31215) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: I entered upon Al-Hajjaj did not greet him."
"31216","(31216) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: It has reached Ibn Umar that Yazid ibn Muawiyah Allegiance was given to him. He said: If it is good, we will be satisfied, and if it is evil, we will be patient."
"31217","(31217) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qays, he said: I witnessed Abdullah bin Masoud come. Saad was receiving the dirhams he had given him from the treasury, so he said: Return this money. Saad said: I think you will meet evil. He said: He returned this money, he said: Then Saad said: Are you Ibn Masoud except a slave of the tail? He said: Then Abdullah said: Are you anyone but Ibn Humaynah? He said: Then his nephew Saad said: Yes, you are both companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, people look up to you both! Then Saad raised his hands and said: O God, Lord of the heavens and the earth, and Ibn Masoud said: Woe to you, speak a word and do not curse. He said: So he said Saad: Or, by God, had it not been for the fear of God, I would have made a supplication against you that would not cause you error. He said: So Abdullah departed as he wished."
"31218","(31218) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ziyad, he said: When Uthman wanted to flog the newborn, He said to Talha: Get up and flog him. He said: I was not one of the executioners. So Ali got up and flogged him, and the newborn started saying: Perhaps Ali: I am the owner of a place. He said: I said to Ziyad: Who is the owner of a place? He said: A woman he was talking to."
"31219","(31219) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Marwan was with Talha on the day of the camel, and when they clashed War. Marwan said: I will not seek revenge after today. He said: Then he shot him with an arrow and he hit his knee, and the blood did not ooze. Until he died, he said: And Talhah said: Call him, for it is an arrow sent by God."
"31220","(31220) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Bakra al-Mughirah ibn One day, in the middle of the day, he was wearing a mask, and he said: Where do you want to go? He said: I want a pilgrim. He said: The prince is visited, but he does not visit."
"31221","(31221) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: It has reached me that Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bi was appointed governor. The season, and he heard that a prince was approaching him, so he arrived on the day of Arafah, so he made it the day of sacrifice."
"31222","(31222) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Qays bin Saad bin Ubadah was with Ali. On his introduction, and with him were five thousand who had shaved their heads after Ali died. When Al-Hassan entered into the pledge of allegiance to Muawiyah, Abu Qays wanted to enter, so he said to his companions: Whatever you wish. If you wish, I will fight with you forever until the calf dies, and if you wish, I will take You have security. So they said to him: Take security for us. So he accepted for them that they will have such-and-such and that they will not be punished with anything. A man among them, and he did not take anything for himself, so when he journeyed towards Medina and went away with his companions, he made a sacrifice for them. Every day he was steadfast until he reached the age of"
"31223","(31223) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: That Ali informed him on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bi. Something, and he said: If you took it, its stones would follow you."
"31224","(31224) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Jafar: So-and-so testified with Omar, but he rejected his testimony."
"31225","(31225) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard my father narrating: That he heard Amr bin Al-Aas said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf died, he said: Bring your belly to Ibn Awf, do not bother with it at all.\n(Ibn Saad 1361, Tabarani 263)"
"31226","(31226) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: Ibn Sirin heard a man cursing Al-Hajjaj, so Ibn Sirin said: God is a just arbiter, and He takes recompense for Al-Hajjaj from one who has wronged him, just as He takes recompense from one who has been wronged by Al-Hajjaj."
"31227","(31227) Abu Asama told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Jahaf told me, he said: Mu’awiyah bin told me Tha'labiyah, he said: I came to Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, and I said: The Messenger of the Chosen One came to us inviting us, he said: So he said to me: Do not fight. I do not hate to blackmail this mother about her affairs, or have sexual intercourse with her without her right."
"31228","(31228) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Azdi, who said: Ibn Al-Hanafiyy said: May God have mercy on the richest person. He restrained his hand, restrained his tongue, and sat in his house, having what he desired, and he was with those he loved."
"31229","(31229) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Radha Ibn Abi Aqeel, on the authority of his father, who said: We were at the door of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. among the people, and a son of his - who had two wolves - came out and said, O people of the Shiites, my father is offering you his greetings. He said: It is as if There were birds on their heads. He said: My father says: We do not like the cursing, nor the negligent, nor those who hasten with destiny."
"31230","(31230) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: If only Ali This matter of ours has overtaken you, this was the place of his journey, meaning: the people."
"31231","(31231) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The Hour will not come until thirty liars emerge, including Al-Ansi, Musallamah, and Al-Mukhtar.\n(Abu Ali 6786. Bazzar 3376)"
"31232","(31232) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Musa bin Umair, on the authority of His father, he said: Al-Hussein ordered a caller and he called out and said: Do not accept a man with me who is in debt. Then a man said: My wife is in charge. My religion, and he said: A woman! What is a woman's guarantee? He said: And he called out in the evening: “It has informed me that a man who has left no loyalty will not be killed without entering Hell.”"
"31233","(31233) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, he said: Abraham said to me: Beware of To be killed with temptation."
"31234","(31234) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Mis’ar mention, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir: That it was stolen. He used to ride his mule every group of people and put me behind him, so he would bring a group of people in the desert and carry them. Ali is his mule, then he says: The world is beneath us."
"31235","(31235) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Humaid bin Abdullah Al-Asam mentioning on the authority of Umm Rashid, his grandmother, that she said: I was with Umm Hani’ and Ali came to her and she called for food for him. She said: I went down and met two men in the spacious area, so I heard One of them says to his friend: Our hands have pledged allegiance to him, but our hearts have not pledged allegiance to him. He said: So I said: Who are these two men? They said: Talhah and Al-Zubayr. I said: I heard one of them say to his friend: You pledged your allegiance to him, but you did not pledge allegiance to him. Our hearts, and Ali said: (So whoever breaks it is only breaking it against himself, and whoever fulfills what he has covenanted with God, he will repay it.) A great reward.)"
"31236","(31236) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, he said: He narrated to me Ibn Abbas, he said: Ali sent me to Talha and Al-Zubayr on the Day of the Camel, he said: So I said to them: Your brother will teach you Peace be upon you, and He says to you: Did you find that I was unfair to you in a ruling, or in deprivation of a category, or such-and-such, or In such and such? He said: Al-Zubair said: No, not even in one of them, but with fear comes the intensity of ambitions."
"31237","(31237) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, on the authority of Alim Al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, said: This house will be burned at the hands of a man from the Al-Zubayr family."
"31238","(31238) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I have never seen a man more cursing than him. Meaning: Ibn Al-Zubayr."
"31239","(31239) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: I said to Amir: People claim that Al-Hajjaj is a believer? He said: And I bear witness that he is a believer in the tyrant and a disbeliever in God."
"31240","(31240) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I never saw Abu Wa’il insult any animal, except for Al-Hajjaj once. One, for he mentioned some of his good deeds, and said: Oh God, feed the pilgrims with food from a cow that does not make him fat and does not make him hungry. He said: Then they turned to her after that and said: If that is more beloved to you, then I said: Do you have doubts about Al-Hajjaj? He said: Do you consider that a sin?"
"31241","(31241) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard my father saying, he said: Ali bin Abu Talib narrated that Talhah said: I pledged allegiance while the clouds were at my back, so he sent Ibn Abbas and asked him. He said: Asama said: As for the deep seas? On his back, no, but he pledged allegiance even though he was unwilling. He said: Then the people jumped on him to the point that they almost killed him. He said: So Suhayb came out while I was beside him. He turned to me and said: I learned that Umm Awf is coming to you."
"31242","(31242) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: We entered upon Ibn Abi Al-Dhail, and he said: They killed Uthman, then They came to me, and I said to him: Do you make yourself suspicious?"
"31243","(31243) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antarah, who said: I heard Abu Ubaidah say: How, I hope. The testimony after I said: Did you see your father rebuking the Bedouins?"
"31244","(31244) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antarah, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Hanzali, he said: We brought Ubayy ibn Ka’b Let us talk to him. When he got up to walk, we got up to walk with him. Omar caught up with him and raised a pearl over him, and said: O Commander of the Faithful: I know what you are doing. He said: What you see is a temptation for the one who is followed and a humiliation for the one who follows."
"31245","(31245) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: He came A man went to Ka'b ibn Ajra and started mentioning Abdullah ibn Ubayy and what was revealed about him of the Qur’an and criticizing him, and he was Between him and him were sacred things and relatives, and Ka’b was silent. He said: Then the man went to Omar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, have you not seen? I mentioned what was revealed about Abdullah bin Ubayy, but it was not from Ka’b. So Omar met Ka’b and said: Was I not informed that Abdul Allah ibn Ubayy was mentioned to you but he was not of you. Ka’b said: I heard what he said, but when I saw him it was as if he deliberately went out to meet you. I hated to help him with my evening, he said: Then Omar said: I wished I had hit his nose, or I wished I had broken him. His nose"
"31246","(31246) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair: Al-Ashtar and Ibn al-Zubayr met, and Ibn al-Zubayr said: I only hit him once until he hit me five or six times, then he said: So he threw me to my feet, then said: By God, had it not been for your closeness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would not have left a member of you with his companion. He said: And Aisha said: And the names are bereft. He said: And when it was yet to be given to him who gave her good tidings, he was alive ten thousand."
"31247","(31247) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I did not know. No one took a break from Shurayh except a Bedouin. Shurayh said to him: Your tongue is longer than your hand. The Bedouin said: You are Asamaru, so no. Tams, Shurayh said to him: Come before your command, he said: That is what I did to you, he said: When he wanted to get up, Shurayh said to him: I did not rebuke you with what I said. He said: Nor did I rebuke you."
"31248","(31248) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya: that Ibn Mikhnaf Al-Azdi sat next to Ali, and said: So Ali said to him: Read, so he recited Surah Al-Baqarah, and he had not finished it until he became distressed for Ali. He said: So he sent him to Asbaan. He said: So he took what he took and carried the rest of the money to Muawiyah."
"31249","(31249) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn Yazid Al-Hamani said: I heard Ali on this pulpit saying: O people, help me take care of yourselves. The city was to be repaired by the seven, but if it is necessary for you to separate it, then come until I divide it among you. When the people settle with the people, they will turn their faces away from their town."
"31250","(31250) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Ibn Umar passed by Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah said: The companions of the Messenger of God sat May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. There was no one among them who did not give him part of his religion except this man."
"31251","(31251) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Sa’d ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Mina, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, He said: I heard Omar, and one of my fingers was in this wound, or he was saying: O people of Quraysh, I am not afraid of people. On you, I only feared for you for the people, and I have left among you two things that have not departed well as long as you have stuck to them: justice in Judgment and justice in oaths, and indeed I have left you in a state like one with which blessings are withheld, except that a people should crook and then crook Why? (Bayhaqi 134)"
"31252","(31252) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: We passed by Abu Dharr about Al-Rabadhi. So we asked him about his residence. He said: I was in the Levant and I read this verse: {Those who hoard up gold and silver and do not We spend it in the way of God.} Then Mu’awiyah said: It is only for the People of the Book, so I said: Indeed, it is among us and within them. So I wrote to Uthman, and he said: Then Uthman wrote to me: To come, and when I came, the people rode on me as if they had never seen me before. That, so I complained about it to Othman, and he said: If I were to isolate myself and be near, and stay at this place, I would not ignore his statement, even if They appointed an Ethiopian slave over me."
"31253","(31253) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Ibrahim said: Sufficient is he who doubts about Al-Hajjaj because of his beard. God"
"31254","(31254) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah: that Omar bin Abdul Aziz had a smar, and his mark was what was between him. And between them he may say to them: If you wish."
"31255","(31255) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Whenever Abraham was mentioned to Ibn Sirin, he would say: I have seen A young man whose cervix is covered with white. As for Al-Sha’abi, I have seen him. Meaning: in the time of Ibn Ziyad."
"31256","(31256) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Mu’adh was a young man who looked up and made his double chins clear, and whenever he sat with the Companions of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. They saw for him what they see for the elderly."
"31257","(31257) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Furat, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, he said: When some of camel, and headed to Siffin. The Nakha'is gathered until they entered Al-Ashtar, and he said: Is there anyone in the house except a Nakha'i? They said: No. He said: This nation intended to do good to her and killed him, and we went to the people of Basra, a people with whom we have pledged allegiance. So We were victorious over them by breaking them, and you will march to the people of the Levant, a people over whom you have no pledge, so let him see. Where does one of you put his sword?"
"31258","(31258) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, it was said to Omar: Write to Juanan, he said: And what Jawanan. They said: The best of the boys. He said: Write to the worst of the boys. (Abdul Razzaq 19855)"
"31259","(31259) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla beaten by al-Hajjaj. He stopped him at the door of the mosque and said: They started saying to him: Curse the liars, so he started saying: May God curse the liars, then He was silent when he was silent, then he said: Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr and Al-Mukhtar bin Abi Ubaid, so I knew When he remained silent, then he began to introduce them to them, saying that he did not want them."
"31260","(31260) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I was sitting with Abu Al-Bakhtari Al-Ta'i and Al-Hajjaj was giving a sermon, and he said: The likeness of Othman in the sight of God is like Jesus, son of Mary, he said: So he raised his head. Then he groaned, then said: {Indeed, I will cause you to die and raise you to Me} according to His saying: {And I will place those who follow you above those who disbelieve. On the Day of Resurrection} He said: Abu Al-Bakhtari said: He is a disbeliever by the Lord of the Ka’ba."
"31261","(31261) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Kinanā told us, he said: I was driving with my horse so that you would return. On the authority of Othman, he said: Al-Ashtar met her and struck her face with his mule until she turned and said: Return me, do not expose me to this.\n(Ibn Saad 128)"
"31262","(31262) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Abi Salih, who said: When Sa’id bin Jubayr came from Mecca to Al-Kufa to be taken to Al-Hajjaj to Wasit. He said: So we came to him as a group of three or four, and we found him. In the wood floor, we sat next to it, and one of us cried, and Sa`id said to him: What makes you cry? He said: I make you cry for the one who The matter has befallen you, and he said: Do not weep, for it has already occurred in God’s knowledge that this will happen. Then he recited: {Whatever befalls calamity in the land, nor in yourselves except that it is in a Book, before We exonerate it. Indeed, that is easy for God."
"31263","(31263) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, he said: Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abbad, he said: Al-Mukhtar Ali bin Abi Talib brought money from Al-Mudain, and his uncle Saad bin Masoud was in charge of it. He said: So he put the money in his hands. And on it was a red cloth. He said: So he put his hand in and took out a bag containing about fifteen hundred pounds. He said: This is one of the wages. The prostitutes, he said: Then Ali said: We have no need for the wages of the prostitutes, he said: And he ordered the money of the debtors to be taken to the treasury, he said: When He turned away. Ali said to him: May God kill him. If his heart had been hardened, he would have found it full of love for Al-Lat and Al-Uzza."
"31264","(31264) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Zubair ibn Al-Awwam: In This verse: {And beware of temptations that will not afflict those who do wrong among you alone.} He said: It was revealed, and we do not know who will replace it. He said: Some of them said: O Abu Abdullah, why did you come to Basra? He said: Woe to you! We see, but we do not have patience."
"31265","(31265) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Qadamah bin Attab, he said: I saw Ali He was giving a speech, and someone came to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, meet Bakr bin Wael, for Banu Tamim has beaten her with sweepers. Ali said: Haha, then he proposed to you, then another came to him and said the same thing, so he said: Ah, then the third came to him. Or the fourth, and he said: Bakr bin Wael overtook you, and Banu Tamim struck her with sweepers, so he said: Now Sunn has told me the truth. Your firstborn, Shaddad? Approach Bakr bin Wael and Banu Tamim and cast lots among them."
"31266","(31266) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim, the client of Sakhir, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Al-Hajjaj sent for me, and I presented to him the Ahwaz. He said to me: What do you have of the Qur’an? He said: I said: I have it as long as I follow it. Enough for me. He said: I want to seek your help in some of my work. He said: I said: If you force me, I will force you, and if you put me with me. Other than me, the linings of evil will be diminished. He said: Then Al-Hajjaj said: By God, if you say that, then the linings of evil will spoil the man. He said: I said: I still will. I have been lying in bed since night, fearing that you will kill me. He said: Why should I kill you? But, by God, if you say that, I will kill the man for something that was feared before me to kill someone like him."
"31267","(31267) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Muhammad bin Hilal Al-Qurashi told us, he said: My father informed us, he said: I heard Abu Huraira said to Marwan and he delayed the gathering: You should stay with the daughter of so-and-so and she will fan you and give you cold water to drink. And the children of immigrants are being boiled in the heat. I thought I would do it and I will do it. Then he said: Listen to your commander."
"31268","(31268) Hammad bin Osama told us, he said: Tell them?? Hammad bin Zaid, he said: Abu Naama told us Amr bin Issa, he said: Aisha said: Oh God, realize your fear of Othman and convey Retaliation against Muthammam and remove the nakedness of a man from Banu Tamim, Abu Imra’at Al-Farazdaq."
"31269","(31269) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Nadhri told us: Rabi’a spoke Talha in the mosque of Banu Salamah, and she said: We were in the enemy’s throat when she came to us. I sold this man to you, and now you are fighting him. Or as they said, so he said: I was brought into the garden and ice was placed on my neck, so it was said: pledge allegiance or we will kill you. He said: so I pledged allegiance, And I knew that she had sold him astray. Al-Taymi said: Walid bin Abdul-Malik said: A hypocrite among the hypocrites of the people of Iraq is Jabala bin Hakim. He said to Al-Zubayr: You are I have pledged allegiance. Al-Zubair said: The sword was placed on my neck and I was told: Pledge allegiance or we will kill you. He said: So I pledged allegiance."
"31270","(31270) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: that people They were at Aisha’s Fustat, when Othman passed by and saw that man in Mecca. Abu Sa’id said: Not one of them remained except that he cursed her, or He was reviled by others, and there was a man among them from the people of Kufa, so Othman was more daring towards the Kufais than he was towards anyone else. He said: O Kufi, are you insulting me? He approached the city, as if he was approaching it. He said: Then he approached the city, and it was said to him: You have to shoot him. He said: So he set off. Talhah was with him until he came to Uthman. Uthman said: By God, I will flog you a hundred times. Talhah said: By God, you will not flog a hundred unless you He is an adulterer. He said: I will deprive you of your gifts. He said: Then Talha said: God will provide for him."
"31271","(31271) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Omar bin Jawan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, he said: We presented Medina, and we wanted to perform Hajj. Al-Ahnaf said: So I set out and went to Talhah and Al-Zubayr, and I said: Who do you command me to do? And His satisfaction with me? I do not see this man except that he was killed, meaning Uthman. They said: We command you to take care of Ali. I said: Do you command me to do so and are satisfied with me? They said: Yes, he said: Then I set off on Hajj until I reached Mecca, where we were there when the killing of Othman came upon us, and Aisha, the mother of The believers, so I met her and said: Who do you command me to pledge allegiance to? She said: Ali. I said: Do you command me to do so and approve of it for me? She said: Yes, so she passed by Ali in Medina and pledged allegiance to him, then returned to Basra, and I see that the matter has settled.\n While I was like this, someone came to me and said: This is Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and Talha and Al-Zubayr have encamped beside me. Al-Khuraibi, he said: So I said: What brought them? They said: They sent to you seeking your victory over the blood of Othman. He was killed unjustly. He said: Then the most horrific thing that had ever come to me came to me. He said: I said: Indeed These people, along with them the Mother of the Believers and the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, let me down severely.The killing of the cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after they ordered me to pledge allegiance to him was very severe.\n He said: When I came to them, they said: We have come to seek your help for the blood of Othman, who was killed unjustly. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you. By God, I said to you: Who do you command me to command? You said: Ali, and I said: Do you command me to command him and are satisfied with him? I said: Yes? She said: Yes, but he changed it, so I said: O Zubayr, the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, O Talha, I appealed to you by God: I told you: whom do you command me to do? You said: Ali, so I said: do you command him and are pleased with him? So you said: Yes? They said: Yes, but he changed it.\n He said: I said: I will not fight with you and with you is the Mother of the Believers and the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor will I fight the cousin of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. You commanded me to pledge my pledge of allegiance. Choose one of three characteristics from me: Either you open the door of the bridge for me. Then I will join the land of the non-Arabs until God decides what He has decreed, or I will join Mecca and I will be there until it is done. God has decided what He has decreed, or withdraw and I will be near. They said: We will conspire, then we will send to you. They conspired, so they said: We will open for him. The bridge door is joined by the one who separates and the one who abandons,Or he will join Mecca and attack you among the Quraysh and tell them your news. This is not according to my opinion. Leave it to him. Behold, we are near, where you shall tread on its earbuds and behold it.\n So he withdrew from Basra with Al-Jalha'i and about six thousand with him, then he met the people, and the first people killed were Talha and Ka'b. Ibn Sur, who had the Qur’an with him, reminding these people and that people until he was killed among them, and Al-Zubayr reached Safwan near Basra. Like the place of Al-Qadisiyyah among you. Then Al-Na’ar, a man from Majashi, met him and said: Where are you going, oh disciples of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? May God bless him and grant him peace? To me, you are under my protection and no one can reach you. So he went with him, and a person came to Al-Ahnaf and said: This Zubair has joined Safwan. He said: What is safe? He gathered the Muslims together until some of them struck each other's eyebrows with swords, then he went home to him and his family.\n He said: Then Umair bin Jarmuz heard him, and he was tempted by the temptation of Banu Tamim, and Fadalah bin Habis, and Nufay’, so they rode on. They asked him to force him with the camel, and Umair bin Jarmouz came to him from behind him, riding a weak horse, so he stabbed him slightly. Al-Zubair was carried on him while he was riding a horse of his own, and it was said to him: the one with the veil, and even if he thought that he had achieved it, he called his companion. O Nafi`, O Fadalah, so they attacked him until they killed him."
"31272","(31272) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, joked He greeted Abu Qatada and said: I will shear your camel, and he said to him: You have her place as a captive, so he said to him after that: Honor her. So he used to walk with her."
"31273","(31273) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Al-Hasan: that Abdullah ibn Ja’far He married his daughter, and he was alone with her, and he said to her: If death befalls you, or any of the affairs of this world is terrible, receive it with You say there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\n Al-Hasan bin Al-Hasan said: Al-Hajjaj sent for me, so say?? To behead you, and I have already arrived and no one among your household is more honorable to me than you. Ask me what you need."
"31274","(31274) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr said to Ubaid ibn Umair: These people spoke to the people of the Levant, hoping that he would return them. Al-Hajjaj heard that and sent to them: Raise. Your voices, so do not listen to anything from him. Then Ubaid said: By God, do not be like those who said: “Do not listen to this man.” The Qur’an, and they have negated therein that you may overcome."
"31275","(31275) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali said: Oh God, you know that I am not theirs. With an imam."
"31276","(31276) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: A sheikh from the people of Kufa told me, He said: I saw Ibn Umar in the days of Ibn al-Zubayr. He entered the mosque and saw a weapon. He started saying: You have made this world great! Until he received the stone."
"31277","(31277) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Abd al-Ala narrated to us. Al-Jafifi, he said: Al-Hajjaj sent for Suwayd bin Ghafali and said: Do not lead your people, and when you return, blame Ali. He said: I said: I heard And obedience."
"31278","(31278) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, saying: Abraham mentioned that he was sent to him at the time of Al-Mukhtar bin Abi Ubaid, he said: He painted his face with paint, and drank medicine, but he did not come to them, so they left him."
"31279","(31279) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Aisha wrote to Muawiyah: As for what follows, whoever acts out of God’s displeasure will be considered one of the people who praise Him and condemn him. (Hamidi 266. Ibn Hibban 277)"
"31280","(31280) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Hijr bin Adiy and he He says: Haha! I have pledged my pledge of allegiance and I will neither dismiss it nor resign it, listening to God and the people. What he means by saying “al-Mughirah”"
"31281","(31281) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbā bin Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murā, On the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote about the shame of Othman, and they said: Who will take him away? To him, and Ammar said: I am, so he took it to him, and when he read it, he said: May God force your nose, so Ammar said: And to his father’s nose. Bakr and Omar, he said: Then he got up and had intercourse with him until he fainted, he said: and there was dirt on him.\n He said: Then he sent Al-Zubair to him and asked him to go, and they said to him: Choose one of three: either you pardon, or you take the damages, or To retaliate, he said: Ammar said: I will not accept anything from them until I meet God.\n Abu Bakr said: I heard Yahya bin Adam, he said: I mentioned this hadith to Hassan bin Salih, and he said: What happened to Othman? More than what he did."
"31282","(31282) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I said to Abraham: Indeed, the Scriptures come before... Qutaybah contains falsehood and lies, so what should I do if I want to speak to my companion? He said: No, but listen."
"31283","(31283) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Israel, he said: A man said to Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas: You have lost the world. And the last one, he said: What is that? He said: You have wealth that you give in charity and receive from it, but we do not have wealth. He said: For a dirham that one of you took. So what he puts in a rightful place is better than ten thousand which one of us took just from an abundance and could not find any touch for it."
"31284","(31284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: It was clear Khalid bin Al-Walid and Saad had a conversation. He said: Then a man had a meal with Khaled at Saad’s, and Saad said: “Ma, what happened between us has not reached the end.” Our religion"
"31285","(31285) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, he said: Someone who heard Salem narrated to me, he said: Umar used to forbid the people. About something, he gathered his family and said: I have forbidden the people from such-and-such, and the people will look at you with disdain. From birds to meat, and by God, I do not find any of you doing that except that I will double his punishment for him."
"31286","(31286) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Sabah ibn Thabit, who said: My father used to hear the servant cursing the tea, and he would say: You curse a sheep and drink its milk."
"31287","(31287) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who heard him say: Salem bin Abdullah said: He said to him: Omar bin Abdul Aziz: Write to me about Omar’s age. He said: I said: If you do what Omar did, you are better than Omar. He is not You have a lifetime like the past, and there are no men like the men of my lifetime."
"31288","(31288) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Waqid, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying while he was prostrating in The Kaaba towards the stone and he says: I seek refuge in You from the evil of what you do."
"31289","(31289) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told me, he said: Omar bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abu Iyas Muawiyah ibn Qurayh told me, saying: I was staying with Amr ibn al-Numan ibn Muqrin, and when Ramadan came, he came to him. A man with two thousand dirhams from Musab bin Al-Zubayr, and he said: The prince greets you and says: We have not left an honorable reader except A favor has come to him from us, so seek help from these people at the expense of this fellow of yours. Amr said: Convey your greetings to the prince. And say to him: By God, we have not read the Qur’an with the intention of this world, but it has been returned to him."
"31290","(31290) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: While I was sitting in The Sacred Mosque, and Ibn Omar was sitting on one side of it, and his two sons were on its right and left, and Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf was addressing the people. He said: Ibn al-Zubayr broke the book of God, God broke his heart, so Ibn Umar said: Indeed, that is not in your hand, nor With his hand, Al-Hajjaj remained silent for a moment - if you wish, you can say long, and if you wish, you can say not long - then he said: Indeed, God has Teach us and every Muslim and you, O Sheikh, that it is of benefit to you. He said: Then Ibn Umar started laughing and said to those around him: But I have abandoned the one in which there is merit: to say: I lied."
"31291","(31291) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Kamil bin Habib, who said: Al-Abbas was the closest earlobes to the heavens."
"31292","(31292) Qubaisa narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Aizar, he said: While Amr Ibn Al-Aas was in the shade of the Kaaba, when he saw Al-Hussein Ibn Ali coming and said: This is the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of the heavens."
"31293","(31293) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman, who said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr: You are coming. Al-Hajjaj: Look at what you say. Do not say what makes your blood permissible. He said: I am only asked by an unbeliever or a believer. I would not incite disbelief against myself when I do not know whether I will be saved from it or not."
"31294","(31294) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man, who said: Omar wrote to Muawiyah: Stick to the truth and the truth will stick to you."
"31295","(31295) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ubaid, who said: Omar said: We seek help from his strength. The hypocrite and his sin is upon him."
"31296","(31296) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, he said: I heard Al-Farzadq saying: Ibn Hattan was one of the most poetic people."
"31297","(31297) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: When I met Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah It is as if I will cause a sea to explode with it."
"31298","(31298) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hamza Abi Amara, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz said to Ubaid Allah bin Abdul God: What is the matter with poetry? He said: Is the source able to do anything but spit it out?"
"31299","(31299) Affan told us, he said: Sulaym bin Akhdar told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Muslim bin Yasar was the highest Al-Hasan was with the people of Basra, until he became weak with Ibn Al-Ash'ath and the other was restrained, but Abu Sa'id did not falter in his height and fell. The other"
"31300","(31300) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed me, he said: Umair ibn Hani told me, He said: A savior, Al-Hajjaj’s companion, told me: When Al-Hajjaj killed Sa’id bin Jubayr, he stayed for three nights, saying: I have nothing to do with Sa’id. Ibn Jubayr."
"31301","(31301) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Muradi, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, On the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, he said: There was a poet among us on the day of Siffin who sang a satire for Muawiyah and Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: And Ammar. He says: Stick to the elderly. He said: Then a man said: Glory be to God. You say this while you are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and Ammar said to him: If you want to sit, then sit, and if you want to go, then go."
"31302","(31302) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Al-Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar used to say: May God have mercy on Ibn al-Zubayr, he wanted the dinars of the Levant, may God have mercy on Marwan, he wanted the dirhams of Iraq."
"31303","(31303) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ziyad wrote to Al-Hakam bin Amr Al-Ghifari. And he is in charge of Khurasan: The Commander of the Faithful has written: That the yellow and the white be chosen for him, and that he should not divide gold among the people. Nor silver, so he wrote to him: Your letter has reached me. You mention that the Commander of the Faithful wrote that the white women should be chosen for him. And the bile, and I found the Book of God before the Book of the Commander of the Faithful, and by God, if the heavens and the earth were He granted a slave a ransom, then he feared God. God made a way out for him, and peace be upon you. Then he said to the people: Convey your money to me. So they left in the morning, and he divided it among them."
"31304","(31304) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali, who said: Ali said: Al-Zubair is still It is as if he was a man from among us, the Ahl al-Bayt, until his sons overtook Abdullah and turned him away from us."
"31305","(31305) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Sharia, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, who said: They mentioned the poets of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is mentioned in this world, he is mentioned in the hereafter: He will bear the standard of poetry on the Day of Resurrection in Hell, or he said, in Hell."
"31306","(31306) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hunaidah ibn Khalid Al-Khuza’i, who said: The first head of sacrifice was given in Islam: the head of the foolish son."
"31307","(31307) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah Al-Jarami, who said: I was among those who went to the people of the Levant that day. Al-Khazir, so we met, and the wind blew upon them, and they turned back, so We killed them, our evening and our night, until morning. He said: So he said: Abraham Meaning: Ibn al-Ashtar: Yesterday I killed a man and I smelled a pleasant scent from him, and I only saw him as Ibn Murjaniya. his feet and his head to the west, or his head to the east and his feet to the west. He said: So I set off and behold, by God, it is him."
"31308","(31308) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala’ ibn al-Manyal al-Ghanawi narrated to me, saying: Abu al-Jahm narrated to me. Al-Qurashi, on the authority of his father, said: Something reported to Ali about me, so he whipped me, then he was informed after that that his companion He wrote to her, and he sent two men to search his house. They found the letter in his house, and he said to one of the men: From the clan: You are from the clan, so cover me up. He said: So they went to Ali and told him. He said: Then Ali rode and my father rode. He said to my father: When we searched for it, we found it to be invalid. He said: Whatever he strikes me with, I will nullify it."
"31309","(31309) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: Whoever heard Umar narrated to me When he saw Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, he would say: Woe to you, O Mughirah, by God, I have never seen you except in fear."
"31310","(31310) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan, he said: Ibn Sinan came out to us. Masoud, while we were in the mosque, he said: O people of Kufa, I lost a hundred thousand from Malik’s house last night that did not come to me. With it is a letter from the Commander of the Faithful."
"31311","(31311) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, saying: Mundhir Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali Ibn The Hanafi, he said: Beware of this temptation, for no one is honored by it unless it is snuffed out by it. Indeed, these people have a term. And for a long time, if all those on earth were to agree to remove their kingdom, they would not be able to do that until God is the one who The call to prayer is given in it. Can you remove these mountains?!"
"31312","(31312) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba narrated to me, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra. He said: Sa'd sent me to divide land between Al-Zubayr and Khabab, and they ran into each other by the gondal. I returned and told Sa'd about that. He laughed until he stamped his foot and said: There is on earth like this mosque, or at least what is more than it. He said: So why not? I replied to them."
"31313","(31313) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, Sa’id bin Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim. He was presented with fresh meat, and he said: Eat it, eat it."
"31314","(31314) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When the pledge of allegiance was given to Ali, he came to me and said: Indeed, A beloved man among the people of the Levant, and I have appointed you over them, so go to them. He said: I mentioned kinship and I mentioned in-laws, so I said: As for what follows, by God, I will not pledge allegiance to you. He said: Then he left me and left. After that, Ibn Umar came to Umm Kulthum and greeted her. Ali and headed to Mecca, so he came to Ali, may God have mercy on him, and he was told: Ibn Omar has headed to the Levant, so the people mobilized. He said: If a man was in such a hurry that he threw his cloak around the neck of his camel, he said: And Umm Kulthum came and informed me, So she sent a message to her father: What is this that you are doing? The man came to me, greeted me, and headed to Mecca, so the people retreated."
"31315","(31315) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to be proud of the people in four things: With our jurist, storyteller, muezzin, and reciter. Our jurist: Ibn Abbas, our muezzin: Abu Mahdhuriya, and our storyteller: Ubaid bin Umayr, and our reciter: Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib."
"31316","(31316) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn al-Zubayr agreed on Destroying it, we left for Mina, awaiting the torment, meaning the demolition of the Kaaba."
"31317","(31317) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, who said: Ibn Umar entered the mosque, and Ibn Al-Zubair was crucified, so they said to him: These are the names, so he came to her and reminded her and admonished her, and said: The corpses are not anything. “But souls are with God, so be patient and seek reward.” She said: “What prevents me from being patient, and the head of Yahya bin Zechariah went to one of the prostitutes of the Children of Israel."
"31318","(31318) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: I was given names after he was killed. Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, and she said: I was informed that they crucified Abdullah upside down and hung him as a cat. By God, I wish I had not I will die until it is handed over to me, so I wash him, embalm him, and shroud him, then bury him. They did not stay long before the letter of Abd came to him. The king was to be handed over to his family. He said: Asmaa brought him, washed him, embalmed him, shrouded him, then buried him."
"31319","(31319) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Zubair and I entered The names of ten nights before Abdullah was killed, and the names of his pain. Abdullah said to her: How do you find yourself? She said: He was in pain. He said: Indeed, in death there is recovery. She said: Perhaps you rejoice in my death, so you wish for it? So do not do it, for by God I do not desire to die until one of your two parties attacks me. Either you are killed and I seek reward for you, or It appears and pleases my eyes, so beware lest a mistake be presented to you that does not agree with you, and you accept it with the hatred of death. He said: But Ibn al-Zubayr told him that he would be killed and that would make her sad."
"31320","(31320) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of his father, he said: My father told me: When Al-Hajjaj killed Ibn Al-Zubayr, he brought him. He went to Minna and crucified him at the same time in the valley, then he said to the people: Look at this! This is the worst of the mothers. He said: I saw Ibn Umar coming to get his mule and he went to approach her by the trunk, and she started to flee. So he said to his master: Woe to you, take her bridle and bring her closer. He said: I saw him approaching her, so Abdullah bin Omar stood and said: May God have mercy on you, if you are a regular faster, and your mother has succeeded, you are the worst of her."
"31321","(31321) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, he said: The mail that came told me: With the head of Al-Mukhtar to Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, he said: When I placed it in his hands, he said: Ka’b did not narrate to me a hadith except I saw his credibility other than this, for he told me that a man from Thaqif would kill me. He showed me that I was the one who killed him."
"31322","(31322) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, Ali bin Harmala, who said: Al-Hajjaj spoke on the day he was recognized. At Arafat, he spoke at length, and Abdullah bin Omar said: Today is a day of remembrance. He said: So Al-Hajjaj continued his sermon. He said: So Abdullah repeated it twice, or three times, then he said: O Nafi’, call for prayer, so Al-Hajjaj descended."
"31323","(31323) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, Qais told us, he said: Omar said: Don’t you tell me about your two houses? These two, and despite this, I am asking you both, and I can see in your faces which of the two places of stay is better. He said: So he said to him. Jarir: I am telling you, O Commander of the Faithful, as for one of the two places: the nearest black palm tree to the land of the Arabs. The last dwelling: the land of Persia, its land, its neighbourhood, and its baqqa. Meaning: Al-Mada'in. He said: So Ammar told me a lie, so he said: I lied, so Omar said: You are lying, then Omar said: Don't you tell me about Is this your prince sufficient? I said: By God, he is not sufficient, nor sufficient, nor knowledgeable in politics, so he removed him and sent Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah."
"31324","(31324) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: It was between Ibn Masoud and Al-Walid ibn Hassan followed him, saying: Then Saad called for them and said: Oh God, let them be together. Then one of them was saying to his friend: He has Saad was answered among us."
"31325","(31325) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The princes were mentioned in the presence of Ibn Abbas, Then a man appeared among them and became so tall that I did not see anyone in the House taller than him, so I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Oh Hazzaz, no. You make yourself a temptation for the wrongdoers, so you shrink back to the point that you have not seen anyone shorter than he."
"31326","(31326) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn al-Muhallab Abu Kudayna informed us, on the authority of al-A’mash, he said They mentioned, according to Ibn Omar, the caliphs and people’s love for their change. Ibn Omar said: If the people’s ruler was the companion of this woman, they would not be satisfied. With it Meaning: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan."
"31327","(31327) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, On the authority of Ali, he said: The fever is like the fever of a scorpion, so if that is the case, join your blind palm tree. It means: blackness."
"31328","(31328) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali: That he said: There will be Akra"
"31329","(31329) Muhammad ibn Kunasa narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Mus’ab ibn al-Zubair came. Abdullah bin Omar was walking around between Safa and Marwa, and he said: Who are you? He said: Your nephew, Musaab bin Al-Zubair. He said: The owner of Iraq? He said: Yes, I came to you to ask you about a people who threw off their obedience, shed blood, and exacted money, but were killed and defeated. They entered a palace and fortified themselves. Then they asked for security and were given it, then they were killed? He said: How much is the iddah? He said: Five thousand. He said: Ibn Omar said: Subhanahu wa Tasbih at that, and said: May God bless you, O Ibn al-Zubayr! If a man brought cattle to Zubair and slaughtered five thousand of them in the morning, would you consider him extravagant? He said: Yes, he said: So you see extravagance with livestock that do not know what God is, and you consider it permissible for one day from those whom God has glorified?"
"31330","(31330) Muhammad bin Kannasa told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Sa’id, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah bin Omar Abdullah came Ibn Al-Zubair, and he said: O Ibn Al-Zubair, beware of atheism in the sanctuary of God, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: A man from Quraysh will commit atheism therein. If his sins were weighed by the sins of the two heavyweights, they would outweigh him. So look and do not neglect it.\n(Ahmad 1368 Hakim 388)"
"31331","(31331) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of al-Muthanna bin Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr addressed us. He said: Indeed, we have been tested with what you may see, so whenever we command you to do a matter for God in which it is obedient, then it is upon you to listen and obey. And whenever We command you to do a matter for which there is no obedience, we have no obedience upon you for it, nor any blessing in kind."
"31332","(31332) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali: He delivered a speech and then said: Your nephew, Al-Hasan bin Ali, has collected money and he wants to divide it among you. Then the people came, and Al-Hasan stood up and said: I collected it for your poor. Then half the people stood up, and then the first one to take it from him was Al-Ash’ath ibn Qais"
"31333","(31333) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani, on the authority of Ali, he said: Al-Hussein will certainly be killed unjustly, and I do not know the soil of the land in which he will be killed: close to the Fire. (Tabarani 2824)"
"31334","(31334) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murā, on the authority of Amr bin Murā as Al-Salami, who said: He came Al-Ash'ath ibn Qais sat next to Ka'b ibn Ajra in the mosque, and he placed one of his legs on the other, and Ka'b said to him: Put it away, for it is not suitable for humans."
"31335","(31335) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Khaled, he said: I came to Omar, so he preferred The people of Syria are ahead of us regarding the reward, so we said to him, and he said: O people of Kufa, are you sure that I have been favored over you? People of the Levant in the reward, because of your disunity, I have preferred you to Ibn Umm Abd."
"31336","(31336) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Mundhir, who said: I was with Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. Then I saw him turning on his bed and blowing his nose, and his wife said to him: What troubles you about the matter of your enemy? This is the son of Al-Zubair? He said: By God, this enemy of God, Ibn al-Zubair, is not the fault of him, but what he will do in his sanctuary tomorrow. He said: Then he raised his hand. To the heavens, then he said: Oh God, you know that I was more knowledgeable than what you taught me, that he would emerge from it dead and floated around. With his head in the cities, or in the markets."
"31337","(31337) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Shu’ab bin Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Abi Hafsa narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Majlaz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, said: I went out to Medina in search of honor and knowledge, and a man wearing robes arrived. Beautiful, so he placed his hands on Omar’s shoulders, so I said who is this, and they said: Ali bin Abi Talib."
"31338","(31338) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, he said: When Othman was besieged, and Talhah came to Ali while leaning his back against the cushions in his house, and said: I adjure you by God when you turn away the people from Commander of the Faithful, and Talhah said: Until they are given the right from themselves."
"31339","(31339) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahhab, or his nephew Abd al-Rahman: that he heard Al-Mukhtar, and he says: Nothing remains of Ali’s turban except two crops until he comes. He said: I said: Why are you leading people astray? He said: Let me talk to them."
"31340","(31340) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to me, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Jabir, he said: I heard Talha ibn Ubaidullah say on the Day of the Camel: We had attacked Uthman in the matter of Uthman, so we found no alternative. Exaggeration"
"31341","(31341) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When There was peace between Al-Hasan bin Ali and Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan. Al-Hasan wanted to leave - meaning: to Medina - Then Muawiyah said to him: You are not the one who goes to address the people. Al-Sha’bi said: I heard him on the pulpit, thank God. He praised him, then said: As for what follows, the most intelligent is piety, and the most incapable is immorality, and this is the matter. The matter about which Mu’awiyah and I disagreed is a right that I had and left to Mu’awiyah, or a right that belonged to someone who had more right to it than me. But I did this to spare your blood. {And if I knew, perhaps it would be a trial for you and an enjoyment for a while}."
"31342","(31342) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Oh God, I I disavow before you the change and clarification."
"31343","(31343) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of al-Sumait, on the authority of Ka`b, who said: For all times there have been kings, so if If God wants good for a people, He sends among them those who reconcile them, and if God wants evil for a people, He sends among them those who are well-off."
"31344","(31344) Ibn Fadl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra, who said: The boy used to pass by, or The slave girl is among those whom the pilgrims take out into the darkness and say: Who is your Lord? So he says: God, and he says: Who is your prophet? Then he says: Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then he says: By God, there is no god but Him, I do not find anyone who fights. Al-Hajjaj unless Al-Hajjaj fights with him."
"31345","(31345) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari: He saw a man taking the side, so he said: Free. Fire is more intense than the heat of the sword."
"31346","(31346) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla exhorting the people. The days of skulls."
"31347","(31347) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-A’la, who said: They said to Mutarrif: This is Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ash’ath. He accepted, and Mutarrif said: By God, he has come to a dispute between two matters. If he appears, no debt will be established for him, and if he appears, no debt will be established against him. You will continue to be humiliated until the Day of Resurrection."
"31348","(31348) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: More than one person told me: That a judge from among the people of Damascus: Omar came and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I saw a vision that frightened me. He said: What did you see? He said: I saw the sun and the moon fighting, and the stars were with them in two halves. He said: Whichever of them you were with, he said: I was with the moon. On the sun, and he said: Omar: {And We made the night and the day as signs, so We erased the signs of the night and made the signs of the day visible} So go, and by God, you will never do anything for me again.\n Ata’ said: I was informed that he was killed with Muawiyah on the day of Siffin."
"31349","(31349) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Two Eids gathered one day, and the pilgrims stood up for the first Eid, and he said: Whoever wants to gather with us, let him gather, and whoever wants to leave, let him leave, and there is no harm. Abu Al-Bakhtari and Maysara said. : What is the matter with God who killed him? Where did this come from?"
"31350","(31350) Abu Usama told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Wasil Al-Ahdab, he said: Ibrahim saw the prince of Helwan passing by. With his animals in the crops of a people, Abraham said: Being unjust in the way is better than being unjust in religion."
"31351","(31351) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Zaydah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Umayr narrated to us, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Amr bin Al-Aas said: If Abu Bakr and Omar had left this money and it would be permissible for them to have any of it We have been foolish and their opinion has been lacking, and may God forgive them. They were not foolish, nor deficient in their opinion, and if they were two women it would be forbidden. We have been destroyed by this wealth that befell us after them. By God, the illusion came only from us."
"31352","(31352) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Ali bin Abi Talib, Qays bin Saad, was the Emir of Egypt. He said: Then Mu’awiyah and Amr bin Al-Aas wrote to him in a letter, and they treated him harshly. And he cursed them and made enemies of him, so he wrote to them in a gentle letter, approaching them and making them feel good about himself. He said: Then when He gave them the letter. They wrote to him with a soft letter, mentioning his virtue and seeking reassurance regarding what they had received. So he wrote to them. With the answer to their first letter, he was harsh to them, and he did not leave anything without saying it, so one of them said to the other: No, by God, we cannot bear it. Qais bin Saad, but come, let us discuss it with Ali. He said: So he sent his first letter to Ali. He said: Then his family said to him: Al-Kufa: An enemy of God, Qays bin Saad, so he deposed him. Then Ali said: And he rules. I, and God knows best, and God is one of them. They refused to remove him, so he removed him, and he sent Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, and when he came to Qais bin Saad, he said to him: Qais: See what I command you to do. If Mu’awiyah writes to you with such-and-such, then write to him with such-and-such, and if He did this, then do that, and beware of disobeying what I commanded you to do. By God, it is as if I am looking at you if you do that and you will be killed. Then it was put into the belly of a donkey and burned with fire. He said: So he did that to it."
"31353","(31353) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: I did not know that Ali He was accused of killing Othman until he was sold out, but when he was sold out, the people accused him."
"31354","(31354) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Qays bin Saad said: Ibn Ubadah: If a man had not plotted to break the dawn, I would have plotted against the people of Syria, and they would have been in turmoil day until night."
"31355","(31355) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Abu Maadan, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who said: I witnessed Al-Hasan and Malik bin Dinar. Muslim bin Yassar and Sa`id were ordered to fight Al-Hajjaj with Ibn Al-Ash'ath, and Al-Hasan said: Al-Hajjaj is a punishment that came from the heavens. Let us accept God’s punishment with the sword."
"31356","(31356) Abu Sufyan Al-Himyari told us, he said: Khalid bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Marwan said: Whoever wants to take a slave girl for pleasure should take her as a barbarian, and whoever wants to take her for children Let him take her as a Persian, and whoever wants to take her to serve let him take her as a Roman."
"31357","(31357) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Ghani narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, who said: Muawiyah said: I am the first of the kings."
"31358","(31358) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Malik Ibn Umayr, he said: Mu’awiyah said: What I have been coveting the caliphate ever since the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Muawiyah, if you rule, do well.\n(Tabarani 850, Bayhaqi 446)"
"31359","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:\n(31359) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bailili saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his sermon in the year of the Farewell Hajj, said: God has given every person his due. There is no bequest to an heir."
"31360","(31360) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sheep, on the authority of Amr bin Kharijah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: No will is made to an heir."
"31361","(31361) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He has no heir. His commandment"
"31362","(31362) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, who said: A man asked Ibn Omar, and he said: O Ibn Omar, what do you think of him? A will for an heir? Then he turned to him and said: Is the free-blood approaching? So he said: It is not permissible to make a bequest to the heir."
"31363","(31363) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: An heir has no will unless he wishes. Heirs"
"31364","(31364) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: It is not For an heir - a will."
"31365","(31365) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man makes his will to an heir, then he permits The heirs before he died, then the heirs returned after his death, so they are in charge of their affairs, and if it is for someone else An heir in excess of a third, then the same is true. If it belongs to someone other than an heir, and there is something between him and the third, then it is permissible."
"31366","(31366) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If a man asks permission from his heirs to And he bequeathed more than a third, and they were pleased with him. So when they shake their hands from his grave, they are on his head. Command them, if they want, they allow it, and if they want, they do not allow it."
"31367","(31367) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked him? He said: They are on top of their affairs."
"31368","(31368) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: They will return if they wish."
"31369","(31369) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bequeathed more than a third of the heirs’ consent, so when They denied that. He said: It is permissible for them."
"31370","(31370) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ used to say: It is permissible. They have given the adhan."
"31371","(31371) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad: He said: Concerning a man who bequeaths more than a third, he will reward him. The heirs, then they return to it? He said: They do not have the right to return, and the arbiter said: If they wish, they can return therein."
"31372","(31372) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If a man makes a will that exceeds a third, then he asks for permission. His son during his life, so he gave him permission, and when he died, he returned to his son. If he wanted, he would allow him to do so, and if he wanted, he could reject him."
"31373","(31373) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman: That a man asked for permission During his illness, his heirs allowed him to bequeath more than a third, so they gave him permission. When he died, they returned, and Ibn Masoud was asked about that. ? He said: That is for them, that is not permissible."
"31374","(31374) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amer On the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, he said: If a man bequeaths more than a third of more than a third to no heir during his illness, Or to an heir, so the heirs gave permission, then he died and they had the right to return."
"31375","(31375) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid Abi Khaled Al-Dalani, who said: I heard Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah narrates, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah: He said; Regarding a man who bequeaths more than a third, the heir allows it, but then he does not allow it after his death. He said: That is reprehensible. It is permissible"
"31376","(31376) Abdul-Ala, or Hushaym, narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he made a will, then he made a will. By the other after it, he said: It is taken by the other of them."
"31377","(31377) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Abu al-Sha’ath’i, they said: He shall be taken for another. His commandment"
"31378","(31378) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan: That a man made a will, so he called people, and said: I call you to witness. If so-and-so’s servant did anything to me then he was free. So they left him and it was said to him: I freed so-and-so and left so-and-so and he was better. affliction, so he said: Return the evidence to me. I bear witness that you have returned to free so-and-so, and that so-and-so belongs to his other servant if it happened to me. Something happened and he was free, then the man died, so the first said: I am free, and the other said: I am free, so they disputed with Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and he responded. He freed the first and permitted the second to be freed."
"31379","(31379) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man makes a will, then breaks it, then The other, and if he does not cancel it, then they are both permissible together in a third of it in shares."
"31380","(31380) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib: That Ibn Abi Rabi’a wrote to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: Concerning a man who makes one will and then makes another will. He said: The last of them took possession of them."
"31381","(31381) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a man who made a will for another man and the one who died A will was made to him before she came to him. He said: This is for the heirs to whom the will was made."
"31382","(31382) Hafs told us, he said: I asked Omar about it, he said: Al-Hasan used to say: It is for the heirs to whom it is bequeathed."
"31383","(31383) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he made a will for a man who was dead On the day a will is made for him, then the will returns to the heirs of the testator, and if he makes a will for a man and then he dies, then the bequest For the heirs to whom the will is made."
"31384","(31384) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: There is no will for a dead person."
"31385","(31385) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no will for a dead person."
"31386","(31386) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: Concerning a man who makes a bequest, then the one to whom it was bequeathed dies. Before the one who made a will, he said: He has nothing, because he made a will while he was dead."
"31387","(31387) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a man who makes a will, and the one to whom he bequeaths dies before that. He made a will, he said: It becomes invalid, and if the one who made a will dies, then the one to whom it was made a bequest, it belongs to his heirs."
"31388","(31388) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who bequeathed to another man a third of his wealth, and he benefited from wealth before If he dies and then he dies, he said: He gets one-third of what he bequeathed to him, and he gets one-third of what he benefited."
"31389","(31389) Hafs told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khallas, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a man who bequeathed a third of his wealth and was killed. Wrongly, he said: The third is included in his blood money."
"31390","(31390) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He has a third of his wealth, and a third That's it"
"31391","(31391) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bequeathed a third of his wealth and was killed by mistake. He said: A third of the blood money is included in a third of his wealth."
"31392","(31392) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: The people of the will are partners in the will, whether it is more or less. It decreased. He said: So I told Ibn Sirin about it, and he liked it."
"31393","(31393) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ibn Layya, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz: Concerning a man who made a will for another man, and then money came to him or he gave money, he said: It does not count."
"31394","(31394) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man bequeaths to another man fifty dirhams, it will be given to him in advance. The eye, and if he bequeaths a third or a quarter, it is for the eye and the debt."
"31395","(31395) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bequeaths to another man fifty dirhams of his wealth, he said: He hastens. He has what is between him and a third of an eye."
"31396","(31396) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ata’ and his followers. On the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who made a will for his cousins, men and women. They said: “The male’s portion is like the female’s portion, except that it be He said: {For the male is the equivalent of the portion of two females}."
"31397","(31397) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Al-Alam Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: That a man recommended For the widows of Banu Hanifa, and Al-Sha’bi said: It is for men and women who left the Hanifa clan."
"31398","(31398) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who says: To the son of so-and-so. Such and such. He said: It is for the rich and the poor of them, and for the male and female of them."
"31399","(31399) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about a man He had dwellings, so he bequeathed a third of each dwelling to him? He said: He will go out until he is in one dwelling."
"31400","(31400) Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who bequeathed a third of his wealth and other things besides that. And he left a house that was one-third of it, and he gave it to the bequestor for one-third. He said: No, but he will be given a share of the money and the house."
"31401","(31401) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: He was asked about a man, and he said: two-thirds. Three hundred dirhams: a hundred for so-and-so, a hundred for so-and-so, and the remaining two-thirds; So it is for so-and-so. He said: To so-and-so a hundred, and to such-and-such a hundred, and whatever remains is so-and-so, and if nothing remains, then it is nothing."
"31402","(31402) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: Concerning a man who made a will. He said: Two-thirds is for so-and-so, and if he dies, it is for so-and-so. He said: It is for the first."
"31403","(31403) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: It is for the first."
"31404","(31404) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: It is conducted as He said"
"31405","(31405) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, the same."
"31406","(۳۱۴۰۶) حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ الْوَہَّابِ الثَّقَفِیُّ ، عَنْ یَحْیَی بْنِ سَعِیدٍ ، قَالَ : بَلَغَنِی أَنَّ صَفِیَّۃَ أَوْصَتْ لِقَرَابَۃٍ لَہَا بِمَالٍ عَظِیمٍ، وَکَثِیرٍ مِنَ الْیَہُودِ کَانُوا وَرَثَتَہَا لَوْ کَانُوا مُسْلِمِینَ فَوَرِثَہَا غَیْرُہُمْ مِنَ"
"31407","(۳۱۴۰۷) حَدَّثَنَا وَکِیعٌ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنَا سُفْیَانُ ، عَنْ لَیْثٍ ، عَنْ نَافِعٍ : أَنَّ صَفِیَّۃَ أَوْصَتْ لِقَرَابَۃٍ لَہَا Jews"
"31408","(31408) Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A man’s will is permissible, whether he is a non-Muslim or someone else."
"31409","(31409) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say: The will. It is permissible for the Jew, the Christian, the Magian, and the Mamluks."
"31410","(31410) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’: that a woman from the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace She made a bequest to a relative of hers who was Jewish."
"31411","(31411) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: There is no harm in making a will to a Jew. And the Christian."
"31412","(31412) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders: {Unless you do to your friends kindness} He said: Your guardians are from the People of the Book. He says: There is no will or inheritance for them."
"31413","(31413) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He heard him being asked about a will for his family. Shirk? He said: There is no harm in it."
"31414","(31414) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar: That Omar made a will to Hafsa."
"31415","(31415) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Janab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi: That a man made a will to his wife, so he permitted That is clear."
"31416","(31416) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Amr Al-Azdi, who said: My aunt, who was Ibrahim’s wife, narrated to me. She said: He made some of his wills to Abraham."
"31417","(31417) Abdă told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A woman cannot be a guardian, for if he does so, he should look to a man. He trusts him, so this was attributed to him."
"31418","(31418) And I heard a woman saying: Sufyan said: To be a guardian. Perhaps a woman is better than a man."
"31419","(31419) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ikrimah: Concerning a man who made a testament. For those in need, he said: It is included in the relatives, and if they are not, then for the relatives, and if they are not, then for the neighbors."
"31420","(31420) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Muammar said in The will: Whoever names him: We will place it where he is named, and whoever says: Where God has commanded: We will place it in his relatives. (Abdul Razzaq 14430)"
"31421","(31421) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who makes a will for the far-off and abandons the relatives. He said: You make His will is three-thirds: two-thirds for the relatives, and one-third for the distant ones. As for Muhammad bin Ka’b, he said: It is only money. God gave it to him and placed it where he liked."
"31422","(31422) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Place it where he commanded it."
"31423","(31423) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam: That his leader was asked about a man who left a will for someone other than his kin? He said: Salem, Suleiman bin Yassar, and Ata used to say: It is for the one to whom it was entrusted."
"31424","(31424) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said: I will give a will to a person for the sake of God, and in The poor, and did he leave behind a gift for those in need? He said: His will is as he enjoined it."
"31425","(31425) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: He commanded them to do a matter. They disagreed, it is permissible and miserable is what they did, and Ata’ said: The relative has more right to it."
"31426","(31426) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man gets a third of it, and he throws it into the sea if I wish"
"31427","(31427) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who makes a will for the far-off and abandons the relatives. He said: You make His will is three-thirds: two-thirds for relatives, and one-third for distant people."
"31428","(31428) Al-Dahhak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: He would not see the successor except For those with kinship, the people of poverty. If he bequeathed it to others, it would be taken from them and returned to them. If not, Among them are poor, so for the people of poverty whatever they are, even if he names its people those to whom he has entrusted."
"31429","(31429) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Maimounah, he said: I asked Al-Ala’ ibn Ziyad and Muslim bin Yassar on the authority of the will? So he called for the Qur’an and recited: {If he leaves behind good, he will make a bequest to the parents and relatives} They said: It is for relatives."
"31430","(31430) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Abd al-Malik ibn Ali, who said: You respond to kinship"
"31431","(31431) Hafs told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas: that Abu Talhah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Messenger of God, I have made my wall for God, and if I could hide it I would not show it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it among the poor of your family. (Muslim 2851, Abu Dawud 1686)"
"31432","(31432) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Concerning a man if he gives advice regarding his illness, then He was healed and did not change that will until he died. He said: He will be taken according to what is in it."
"31433","(31433) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ali: Concerning a man He made a will during his illness, then he left it until he died. He said: It is permissible."
"31434","(31434) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: Amer was asked about a man who died and left behind three sons. And he bequeathed the equivalent of the share of one of them? He said: It is a fourth, for him is a quarter."
"31435","(31435) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour and Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a man abandons Three sons and he bequeathed the equivalent of the share of one of his sons, saying: Add one and make it out of four."
"31436","(31436) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Add one and make it out of four."
"31437","(31437) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left behind two sons. And two parents, and he bequeathed the equivalent of the share of one of the two sons. He said, “It is out of eight.”"
"31438","(31438) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left Six sons, and he bequeathed the equivalent of the share of some of his sons. He said: Mansour said: He is one of seven, and he will enter with them, and he said Mughirah: It is diminished and not completed, like the share of one of them."
"31439","(31439) Abu Muawiyah told us, Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Ibrahim told me, and he said: What do you say about a man who made a will? Half, a third, and a quarter. He said: I did not have anything on it, so he said: Abraham, take money that has a half and a third. And a quarter: twelve, so take half of it as six, and a third as four, and a quarter as three, then divide the money among thirteen, so what He who struck six was the owner of the half, and whoever struck four was the owner of a third, and whoever struck three was the owner of a quarter."
"31440","(31440) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They disliked that a man bequeath a similar share. One of the heirs, even if it is less."
"31441","(31441) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Ubad al-Siddalani narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas: He commanded The same as the share of one of his children."
"31442","(31442) Waki’ narrated to us, Zaydah Abu Qutaybah Al-Hamdani narrated to us, on the authority of Yasar bin Abi Karib, on the authority of Sharih : He made a ruling concerning a man who bequeathed to another man an arrow of his wealth, but he did not poison it. He said: The arrows are removed, and the legatee has an arrow."
"31443","(31443) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the people of Khurasan, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He does not have Something, this is unknown."
"31444","(31444) Affan told us, he said: Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ata’. And Yaqoub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sayyib, on the authority of Ikrimah: Concerning a man who bequeathed to another man an share of his wealth. He said: It is nothing. He did not explain it."
"31445","(31445) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Iyas ibn Muawiyah, he said: It was The Arabs say: He has one-sixth."
"31446","(31446) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Al-Huzayl: A man made an arrow for another man. He did not have his money and did not poison it, so Abdullah said: He has one-sixth."
"31447","(31447) Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid: Did Adiy ask Ayas? He said: The arrow in the speech of the Arabs is one-sixth."
"31448","(31448) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, that a woman was told: He made her sick: He recommended such-and-such, he recommended such-and-such, so she nodded her head, but Ali bin Abi Talib did not reward him."
"31449","(31449) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Abu Rabi`ah, or Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi`ah, said: I said to Omar: Something that the people of Yemen would do. A man makes a will, then changes his will. He said: To change whatever he wants of his will."
"31450","(31450) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: A man has not freed a slave during his illness. It is a will that if he wishes, he can revise it."
"31451","(31451) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man can change his will as much as he wants, except to free him."
"31452","(31452) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Every successor, if he wishes, may return it. There is nothing other than emancipation."
"31453","(31453) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a man makes a will By bequests, and he freed a boy of his if death occurred to him. He said: There is no recourse to the matter of emancipation. Emancipation is not like any other will."
"31454","(31454) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man makes a will, then he changes his will as he pleases. It was said to him: The emancipator, he said, the emancipator and not the emancipator, but only the last of it is taken."
"31455","(31455) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Tawus: He did not see. It is unfortunate for a man to take back his freedom."
"31456","(31456) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Al-Aliya fell ill, so he freed one of his slaves. They mentioned to him that he was behind him. The river, and he said: If he is alive, then I will free him, but if he is dead, then I will free him. And he mentioned these verses: {And he has descendants. Weak}"
"31457","(31457) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: They used to make wills, so the man would write in his will: Something happened to me before I changed this will, so if he decides to change it, he can change the emancipation and change it if he wants. If he did not make an exception in his will, he could change any of it as he wished other than emancipation."
"31458","(31458) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ruh Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: He used to swear to him. An oath, that the man who has been emancipated leaves behind a will, and that a man has the right to change his will as he pleases."
"31459","(31459) Sa’id bin Khathim narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The master who manages it returns whenever he wishes."
"31460","(31460) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Aisha said: Let the man write in His will: If something happened to me before I changed this will."
"31461","(31461) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr: that Ibn Masoud made a will So he wrote in his will: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Ibn Masoud recommended: If something happened to him during his illness. This"
"31462","(31462) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: They used to make wills, and the man would write in his will: If Something happened to me before I changed this will."
"31463","(31463) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Khaldi, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, he said: I recommended twelve Once upon a time, I was given a time. If the time came, I would have a choice."
"31464","(31464) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Umair, Al-Harith bin Umair, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He stipulated: If something happened to me before this book of mine was changed."
"31465","(31465) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus: That a man from the people of Yemen made a will, and he said: So-and-so is free. And so-and-so is free - and he has not been named - if he dies during this illness, and the man is healed, then his dispute is taken by his kings to the judge of the soldiers, So he consulted Tawoos about that, and Tawoos said: They are slaves, but his intention was: If anything happens to him, something bad happens to him."
"31466","(31468) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He was asked about a man who bequeathed his female servant to his brother’s son, then He had intercourse with her? He said: He spoiled his will."
"31467","(31467) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he bequeaths to them, then it is a third of them. Meaning: Hajj and zakat."
"31468","(31468) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he recommended Hajj but there was no Hajj, then from a third."
"31469","(31469) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: From a third."
"31470","(31470) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is from all the wealth."
"31471","(31471) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Tawus: Concerning a man who performs the Hajj of Islam and it is on him. Zakat on his wealth? They said: These two are in the position of religion."
"31472","(31472) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who dies and is instructed to perform Hajj. On his behalf, or should alms be given on his behalf as the expiation of Ramadan, or the expiation of the right month? He said: From a third."
"31473","(31473) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man has something obligatory for him, then it is of all Money"
"31474","(31474) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: It is from all the wealth."
"31475","(31475) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Salih ibn Khawat, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr: Omar ibn Abdul Aziz He wrote: It is not permissible for a person to be made a will or a gift except with the permission of his master."
"31476","(31476) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The one who has been granted will neither be freed nor granted except by permission. His Lord"
"31477","(31477) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is it permissible for a fool and a possessed person to make their will if They achieved the truth while they were weak in their minds? He said: I do not think it would be appropriate for them to bequeathed to you."
"31478","(31478) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah: Concerning the will of the insane person, he said: If He was right, he was right."
"31479","(31479) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: It is not permissible to make a will. There is no divorce except within reason."
"31480","(31480) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, who said: If he was named Al-Ghazai: He was given Al-Ghazai. Otherwise: obey God: His way."
"31481","(31481) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Habib, on the authority of Abu Darda’: Concerning the man He recommended something for the sake of God, he said regarding the Mujahideen."
"31482","(31482) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas Ibn Sirin: A woman bequeathed thirty dirhams. For the sake of God, when the time for separation came, I said to Ibn Umar: A woman bequeathed thirty dirhams for the sake of God. Should we give it to her during Hajj? He said: But it is from the way of God."
"31483","(31483) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd: That a man died. And he left money and bequeathed it for the sake of God. He mentioned that bequest to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said: Give it to God’s servants. He said: What are the workers of God? He said: Pilgrims to the House of God."
"31484","(31484) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, who said: A man asked Mujahid about a man, and he said: Everything is for me. For God's sake? Mujahid said: The path of God is not one, every good thing he does is in the path of God."
"31485","(31485) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin: That a man recommended something for the sake of God, and he said: Ibn Omar: Hajj in the name of God."
"31486","(31486) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i: that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about a man who gave his money in charity. All of it is owed to someone other than an heir, then he withheld it until he died, returning that to a third."
"31487","(31487) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever does anything with his wealth will not implement it. Until death comes to him: he is on his way."
"31488","(31488) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: A man came to Al-Hasan with a sealed will to bear witness to it. Al-Hasan said: Why do you find among these people two men whom you trust and testify to this book of yours?!"
"31489","(31489) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I see it on the authority of Abraham: about a man who seals his will and says to the people: : They bear witness to what is in it. He said: It is not permissible unless it is read to them, or it is read to him and he acknowledges what is in it."
"31490","(31490) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi: Concerning a man who writes a will. And he says: Bear witness to what is in this document. He said: No, until it is known what is in it."
"31491","(31491) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, who said: I went with Hafs bin Asim. To Salem, who had sealed his will, and said: If anything happens to me, then bear witness to it."
"31492","(31492) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ali Qadi Basra: In a man who writes his will, then seals it, then says: Bear witness to what is in it. He said: It is permissible."
"31493","(31493) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, He said: There was a boy from Ghassan in Medina, and he had heirs in Syria, and he had an aunt in Medina, so when he came, she came Omar bin Al-Khattab, so she mentioned that to him and said: Is he a guardian? He said: Have you had a wet dream yet? He said: I said: No, he said: Falus, he said: So he bequeathed to her some palm trees, so I sold them to her for thirty thousand dirhams."
"31494","(31494) Abu Issam told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: that Uthman approved the will of Ibn Ash-Isha Sunnah"
"31495","(31495) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: that Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz permitted the will of a boy."
"31496","(31496) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that Abdullah bin Utbah was asked about the will of his neighbour. They belittled and despised her? He said: Whoever does the truth will be rewarded."
"31497","(31497) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, who said: A son made a will for my father. Moses was a young boy who received a will, and his brothers wanted to reject his will, so they went to Shurayh, so he approved your will. The boy"
"31498","(31498) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible to make a will on a child. His wealth is in the third or less."
"31499","(31499) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I said to him: Is his will permissible? He said: It is permissible."
"31500","(31500) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ammarah, he said: I heard Abu Amr bin Al-Ajda’, saying: He disputed with Ali. Zahir was a boy, so Ali ordered that we free him, so we freed him."
"31501","31501) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: That he said regarding the boy’s will: Whoever of the testator makes a right and does what is right, he will reward."
"31502","((31502) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of his father: A boy made a will for his servant. From the people of Al-Hira for forty dirhams, so Shurayh rewarded him."
"31503","(31503) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If the boy is pious Al-Rakki, if he falls into it, his will is permissible."
"31504","(31504) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is not permissible for a boy or a female servant to be a will even He prays."
"31505","(31505) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not permissible to emancipate a child, nor to make his will, nor to make a will. Neither selling him, nor buying him, nor divorcing him."
"31506","(31506) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible for a boy to be a guardian until he has had a wet dream, nor for a male slave. She even menstruates."
"31507","(31507) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Your will is not permissible except what is not obscene. Nope"
"31508","(31508) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I heard him say: If he reaches The boy is fifteen, his will is permissible."
"31509","(31509) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible to make a will."
"31510","(31510) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Mustamir ibn Al-Rayyan, who said: I attended Jabir ibn Zayd in the Jami’ Mosque, and he said to him: Zurara bin Awfa - who was at that time in charge of judgment: A boy was brought before me who had freed a slave of his, but the saints disapproved of that. So I decided to return that, and then the boy would lead, until the boy grows up and loves money, so if he wants to go, I will go. And if he wants to be rejected, he will be rejected."
"31511","(31511) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, who said: Hisham bin Hubaira witnessed a case concerning a man who made a will for his sister. Upon his death, he was given the share of two of his sons, and the deceased left behind sons and daughters. The legatee wanted to make She was in the same position as the male, but the heirs refused to make her except in the female position, so he ruled that she was in her position. If you do not make it clear."
"31512","(31512) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Awf Al-Arabi, on the authority of Hisham bin Hubaira: That he decreed Concerning a man who willed to another man the share of one of his children, and he has a male and a female, that he shall have the share of the female. Abu Bakr said: Waki’ said: Sufyan said: He has a female share."
"31513","(31513) Omar told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: Concerning a man who bequeathed to another man a horse and named it, and said: A third of my money goes to so-and-so. And so-and-so, and the horse was enough to support a third of his money. Al-Zuhri said: We think that a third of his money should be divided among their shares."
"31514","(31514) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He said about a man who bequeathed a dirham and a sixth. And the like: they all share one another."
"31515","(31515) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He did not see any harm in a man making a will. A hundred dirhams for his slaves, and two hundred dirhams if the saints are satisfied, and if he gives him anything of a third of it, then it is on his neck."
"31516","(31516) Hafs told us, he said: I asked Omar about a man who makes a will for his servant? He said: Al-Hasan used to say: If he had bequeathed a loaf of bread to him, I would have freed him."
"31517","(31517) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Jundub, who said: Taman asked Ibn Abbas: Should I recommend The slave? He said: No."
"31518","(31518) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: A man’s will is wherever he made it, unless he is orphaned. His will"
"31519","(31519) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: The executor is in the position of the father, and if The guardian was accused and deposed, or someone else was appointed with him."
"31520","(31520) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar, who said: If there is a will and a freed man, they are equal."
"31521","(31521) Hafs and Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If she is a freed woman and a legatee. He began with emancipation."
"31522","(31522) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath and Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to begin with emancipation."
"31523","(31523) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who recommends the emancipation of his servant during his illness, and entrusts with him. With bequests, he said: He begins with the emancipation of the slave before the bequests, so if he bequeaths that he purchase a slave for him, then she will be emancipated: it was Nasmah is like every other commandment."
"31524","(31524) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say: He begins with emancipation, even if that comes to him. The whole third"
"31525","(31525) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to say about a will, “There shall be in it.” Emancipation is more than a third. He said: The third is between them in shares."
"31526","(31526) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Masruq: He said regarding freeing people and bequests, he said: It begins with the will."
"31527","(31527) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said about the shares."
"31528","(31528) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It begins with emancipation."
"31529","(31529) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He only begins with emancipation if he names him a slave. With her eyes"
"31530","(31530) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan said: If he bequeaths certain things, and says: Manumit me, then by shares, and if He gave a will, and said: So-and-so is free, he began by emancipating you."
"31531","(31531) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It begins with emancipation."
"31532","(31532) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: With quotas."
"31533","(31533) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, he said, It begins with emancipation."
"31534","(31534) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who died and left behind two thousand dirhams and a slave whose value was a thousand dirhams. And he bequeathed to a man five hundred and freed a slave. He said: The slave will be freed and the will will be invalidated."
"31535","(31535) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: In his saying: {And when the two people are present, turn away. Relatives, and orphans, and the needy, so provide them with it.} So he narrated on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of his servants: He appointed a successor, so he commanded With a sheep, it was slaughtered, and he prepared food for the sake of these verses, and said: Were it not for these verses, this would have been part of my wealth."
"31536","(31536) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, in his saying: {And when the people who are divided are present, they will be of kin. And the orphans and the needy, provide for them from it.} He said: Whenever a people divided the inheritance and these were witnesses, He would submit to them. Of the inheritance, and if they are absent and one of them is a witness, then if he wishes, he can give from his share, otherwise he will say to them a known word. He said: He says: You have a right to it."
"31537","(31537) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah and Al-Hasan, they said: They submit. And they say a kind word."
"31538","(31538) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man was dividing an inheritance, and he said to its owner: No. There will come to us a verse from the Book of God that has been dead, so he divided among them from his share."
"31539","(31539) Zayd ibn Harun, Anusfyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: In his saying: {And when The relatives and the orphans have attended the portion. They said: It is confirmed. So when she attends and these people attend, they will be given some of it and he will submit. Oh God!"
"31540","(31540) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: In his saying: {And when the people who are divided are present, they will be of kin} Indeed. Arbitrated"
"31541","(31541) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, he said: I heard Yunus bin Jubayr narrating on the authority of Hattan, on the authority of Abu Moses: In these verses: {When the people of the relatives and the orphans and the needy are present, provide for them from it and say to them: A well-known word. He said: Abu Musa decided it."
"31542","(31542) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah: that Urwah divided an inheritance His brother Musab, so he gave to those around him and his sons were young."
"31543","(31543) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa And Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr: They used to give gifts to whomever of them were present."
"31544","(31544) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr: {And when he is present Those who are relatives, and the orphans, and the needy, provide them with it.} He said: If they are old, they will submit, but if they are young, Apologize to them, for that is his saying {a well-known word}"
"31545","(31545) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: My father’s guardian An inheritance, so he ordered a sheep to be slaughtered and prepared. When he divided that inheritance, he fed them, and said: For those who do not inherit, it is fair."
"31546","(31546) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik: The verse of inheritance abrogated it."
"31547","(31547) Ibn Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not decisive. Abrogated."
"31548","(31548) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’bi say in the mosque that he passed by: I heard a hadith that remains Someone heard him except me. I heard Amr bin Shurahbil say: Abdullah said: You people of Yemen are among the people most deserving of death. A man, and he does not leave his relatives, let him put his money wherever he wants. Al-Amash said: So I said to Ibrahim: Al-Shu’abi said such-and-such. Ibrahim: Hammam bin Al-Harith narrated to me, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah, similar to him.\n(Saeed bin Mansour 217)"
"31549","(31549) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubaidah about a man who did not Is he in possession of a contract but not a family member, and will he bequeath all of his wealth? He said: Yes."
"31550","(31550) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; He was asked about a man who died and left no freed slaves or heirs? He said: His wealth is wherever he puts it. If he did not bequeath anything, then his wealth is in the Bayt al-Mal."
"31551","(31551) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who befriended another man and greeted him with greetings. He said: If he wishes He bequeathed all his wealth."
"31552","(31552) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah: that Abu Al-Aaliyah bequeathed his inheritance to Banu Hashim."
"31553","(31553) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father: that Abdullah bin Masoud, Othman, and Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Muti` ibn al-Aswad recommended to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: He recommended to Abdullah ibn Al-Zubayr"
"31554","(31554) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He was a guardian of a man."
"31555","(315??5) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: A cousin of mine recommended a will to me. He said: I thought about that, so I asked A lifetime? So he ordered me to accept it. He said: Ibn Sirin used to accept the will."
"31556","(31556) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Ubaid crossed the Euphrates and recommended to Umar ibn Al-Khattab"
"31557","(31557) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: Abraham was sent to me and he recommended to me."
"31558","(31558) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of his father: He said: He fell ill with an illness that he recovered. From him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought him his oud and said: O Messenger of God, I have a lot of wealth, but not He inherits from me except my son. Should I give two-thirds in charity? He said: No. He said: So the half? He said: No, I said: So a third? He said: A third is a lot.\n(Bukhari 6733 and Muslim 1252)"
"31559","(31559) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I wished that people would ignore a third to A quarter, because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A third is a lot. (Bukhari 2743. Muslim 1253)"
"31560","(31560) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Al-Zubayr bequeathed a third of it."
"31561","(31561) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He was mentioned at the age of one-third in The will, he said: A third is moderate, neither understated nor overstated."
"31562","(31562) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul: that Muadh bin Jabal said: God has given you in charity a third of Your wealth will increase your life. Meaning: the will."
"31563","(31563) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Ezza, he said: Abu Bakr said: It was taken from What is the matter with what God took of the spoils and commanded a fifth?"
"31564","(31564) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Abu Bakr and Ali recommended the fifth."
"31565","(31565) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Bakr: that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman said: I would not accept The will of a man who bequeaths a third and has a son."
"31566","(31566) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The third is good and it is permissible."
"31567","(31567) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Bashir ibn Uqba, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Shakhir, who said: There was a mutarrif who saw the five Good commandment."
"31568","(31568) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say that the one who enjoins the five is better. Who recommends a quarter, and the one who recommends a quarter is better than the one who recommends a third?"
"31569","(31569) Ali and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: They used to bequeath only a fifth and a quarter. The third is the utmost part of the untamed, and Ibn Numayr said: the utmost part of the untamed."
"31570","(31570) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Because I bequeath the five is more beloved to me than That I bequeath a quarter, and that I bequeath a quarter is more beloved to me than that I bequeath a third, and whoever bequeaths will not leave you."
"31571","(31571) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Mandal narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel said: A third is weak and a quarter is weak."
"31572","(31572) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Abbas, he said: A quarter is bad and a third is bad."
"31573","(31573) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Ibrahim said: It used to be said: A sixth is better than The third in the will."
"31574","(31574) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: They used to prefer to leave behind One-third"
"31575","(31575) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Qutham, the client of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali said: My will is to Akbar. My son is not stabbed in either the stomach or the vagina."
"31576","(31576) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: It is not right for a Muslim to stay for two nights and have anything to bequeath to him, unless his will is written with him.\n(Muslim 1249. Abu Dawud 2854)"
"31577","(31577) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer, who said: Whoever leaves a will will not be harmed by it nor will he be harmed. No one will have the same reward as if he gave it in charity during his life or in his health."
"31578","(31578) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The harmful person in a will is from major sins, then he recited {not harmful, a commandment from God}"
"31579","(31579) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, who said: Al-Hakam and I went to Sa’id bin Jubayr. So I asked him about his saying: “And those who should fear, if they leave behind them weak offspring, they will fear for them” to his saying {rightly} He said: He is the one who is attended by death, and those attending it say to him: Fear Allah, and grant them, may God bless them, even if they are dead. Those who are commanded to make a bequest love to spend on their children.\n So we came with an oath and asked him? He said: What did Saeed say? So we said: Such and such. He said: No, but it is a man who is approached by death and it is said to him: Fear God and keep your money. For there is no one more deserving of your wealth than your child, and if the one making a bequest were a relative, they would love for it to be made to them."
"31580","(31580) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Amr, who said: My father complained, so I met him. Thumama bin Hazan Al-Qushayri, and he said to me: Did your father make a will? I said: No. He said: If you are able to make a will, then let him make a will, for it will complete what was detracted from his zakat. (Tabarani 69)"
"31581","(31581) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Dharaar is in The commandment is one of the major sins. Then he recited: {And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger and transgresses His limits - He will admit him to the Fire to abide therein}."
"31582","(31582) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ibrahim bin Misra told me that he heard a peacock. He says: No Muslim who is certain of a will dies without making a will except his family who are entitled to make a will on his behalf."
"31583","(31583) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, he said: Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were only They hate for a man to die before making a will, before inheritances are sent down."
"31584","(31584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha, who said: I said to Ibn Abi Awfa: The Messenger of God recommended May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: No, I said: How do people command the will? He said: He recommended the Book of God.\n(Bukhari 2740, Muslim 1256)"
"31585","(31585) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He did not leave The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bequeathed neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor did he bequeath anything. (Muslim 1256. Ibn Majah 2695)"
"31586","(31586) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Arqam bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died without leaving a will. (Ahmad 343. Abu Ali 2553)"
"31587","(31587) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: They mentioned with Aisha that Ali was a guardian, so she said: When was he appointed guardian? I was propping him on my lap, and he became effeminate and died. When was a will given to him?!\n(Bukhari 2741, Ahmed 32)"
"31588","(31588) Ibn Juraij narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the dead person leaves behind seven hundred dirhams, then no He advises you.\n(Saeed bin Mansour 250)"
"31589","(31589) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers {If he leaves behind the best, he will make a bequest} He said: The best of wealth, it was It is said: A thousand dirhams or more."
"31590","(31590) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father: that Ali entered upon a man from Banu Hashim ‘Awdah. So he wanted to make a will, but he forbade him and said: God says: {If he leaves good} and if you do not leave any money, then leave it for your family."
"31591","(۳۱۵۹۱) حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو مُعَاوِیَۃَ ، عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ شَرِیکٍ ، عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِی مُلَیْکَۃَ ، عَنْ عَائِشَۃَ ، قَالَ : قَالَ She had a man: I want to make a will. She said: How much money do you have? He said: Three thousand. She said: How many children do you have? قَالَ : أَرْبَعَۃٌ ، قَالَتْ : فَإِنَّ اللَّہَ یَقُولُ : {إنْ تَرَکَ خَیْرًا} وَإِنَّہُ شَیْئٌ یَسِیرٌ ، فَدَعْہُ لِعِیَالِکَ فَإِنَّہُ I prefer"
"31592","(31592) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibrahim: In his saying {a will for their wives} he said: It has been abrogated."
"31593","(۳۱۵۹۳) حَدَّثَنَا وَکِیعٌ ، عَنْ سُفْیَانَ ، عَنِ الْجَہْضَمِ ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللہِ بْنِ بَدْرٍ ، عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ {إنْ تَرَکَ خَیْرًا The will}, he said: It was abrogated by the verse of inheritance."
"31594","(۳۱۵۹۴) حَدَّثَنَا ابْنُ فُضَیْلٍ، عَنْ أَشْعَثَ، عَنِ الْحَسَنِ قَالَ: نَسَخَتْہَا آیَۃُ الْفَرَائِضِ، وَتَرَکَ الأَقْرَبُونَ مِمَّنْ لاَ He inherits"
"31595","(31595) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The will is not based on its content, but rather It is in the same position as debt in a man’s wealth."
"31596","(31596) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus: It was He sees the will as guaranteed."
"31597","(31597) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man makes a will to a man who is absent, then he presents So he acknowledged the will, then he denied it, so he has no right to do so."
"31598","(31598) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us that he read to Fudayl bin Misra, on the authority of Abu Hariz, on the authority of Al-Hakam, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar, he said: When two men and a woman meet, labor strikes her, it is not permissible for them to take possession of what is in their wealth except a third."
"31599","(31599) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who gives pleasure in traveling on the water and riding on the sea. And about the plague and the pregnant woman, he said: Whatever they are given is permissible, it should not be part of a third."
"31600","(31600) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whatever a pregnant woman does during her month is from a third."
"31601","(31601) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: A man has tuberculosis and fever, and he comes. And he goes, saying: Whatever he does is from all the wealth, except that he is the most miserable on his bed."
"31602","(31602) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whatever a pregnant woman does, she is her guardian."
"31603","(31603) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The bearer is his will."
"31604","(31604) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The pregnant woman is his guardian."
"31605","(31605) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, who said: Your wife gave me a gift, and Pregnant, so she said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and he said: It is from all the wealth.\n Hammad said: Yahya said: We say: It is from all wealth as long as it is not lost by divorce."
"31606","(31606) Waki’ told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The bearer is his will."
"31607","(31607) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Iyas bin Muawiyah was detained on suspicion, so they sent me, and he said: Go to... Al-Hasan, so ask him: What is my condition regarding what I took of my wealth in this condition? He said: So I went to Al-Hassan and said to him: Your brother Ayas is greeting you and saying: What is the matter with me on this day? Al-Hasan said: His condition is the same as that of a sick person, only a third is permissible for him."
"31608","(31608) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: When he put His foot is in stitches, so whatever he has bequeathed is from a third."
"31609","(31609) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: When he puts his foot in The stitches, whatever he spoke of, is one-third of it."
"31610","(31610) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ash-Shu’biy, on the authority of Masruq, that he said: If A man put his foot in stitches saying: If he travels, then whatever he bequeaths to him is from a third."
"31611","(31611) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a prisoner in the hands of the enemy: if he gives a gift, or If he makes a bee, or bequeaths a third of it, it is permissible."
"31612","(31612) Ma’an bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A prisoner is not permitted to take his property except One-third"
"31613","(31613) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The sale of a successor is permissible."
"31614","(31614) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The custodian of his house Father"
"31615","(31615) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Hamza, on the authority of Abu Wahhab, who said: The guardian’s order is permissible except in The quarter, and if he sold it, he would not say anything."
"31616","(31616) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The guardian of the orphan looks as he sees For the orphan, he works for the orphan."
"31617","(31617) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: The custodian of his residence. The father"
"31618","(31618) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq: that Shurayh used to approve the witnesses of the guardians."
"31619","(31619) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"31620","(31620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is not permissible, he is an opponent."
"31621","(31621) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Omar bequeathed four thousand to the mothers of his children, Four thousand"
"31622","(31622) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Imran bin Husayn made a will for his mothers. His children"
"31623","(31623) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Burqan, who said: I said to Maymun bin Mihran: Does a man make a will for the mother of his children? He said: It is permissible."
"31624","(31624) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Al-Sha’bi made a will for the mother of his two children."
"31625","(31625) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham: Concerning a man who gives in love to the mother of his children. He said: He permissible"
"31626","(31626) Mu’tamir told us, he said: I said to Yunus: A man gave something to the mother of his children and then he died? He said: Al-Hasan used to say: “Layla”"
"31627","(31627) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the mother of the child achieves something in her life, If her master dies, then he is hers and she is freed. If the deceased took away something before he died, or bequeathed something From what she achieved in her life: He can do with it whatever he wants."
"31628","(31628) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin Rafi’, who said: A man in irrigation died and left behind money and slaves, and he said: My servant is so-and-so for so-and-so, and My servant is so-and-so for so-and-so, and his will did not amount to a third. When he took the slave to Kufa, some of them died. The slave of the heirs, and the slave of the one he bequeathed to them had not died, so I asked Abraham? He said: He gives to those who make a will what his companion has bequeathed to him."
"31629","(31629) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who made his will to be written to him, and he said: The letters written: I have spent my correspondence on the families of my master, and he said: He will give charity, and that is permissible, and there is no harm in him making a bequest to his servant. If the servant says: I have written myself down, or I have sold myself, that is not permissible."
"31630","(31630) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked about a man who recommended that Banu Hashim enter. Are your friends with them? He said: No."
"31631","(31631) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: that Saad bin Abbad divided his wealth among his heirs. On the Book of God, and his wife had given birth to a man, so Abu Bakr and Omar sent for Qais bin Saad to go out for this. The boy fulfilled his rights. He said: He said, “As for something that Sa’d did, I will not take it back, but my share is his.” So accept that from him."
"31632","(31632) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Wabara, who said: A man bought a sister of his who had been taken captive in The pre-Islamic man bought her and a son for her, and it is not known who his father was. He grew up and acquired wealth, then he died. They went to Omar and told the story about him. The story, so he said: Take his inheritance and put it in the treasury. I do not see him leaving my guardian any blessings, nor do I see it as obligatory for you. This reached Ibn Masoud, and he said: May he die, until he met him, and he met him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, your aide and guardian. Yes, he said: Such and such? He said: Yes, so he gave him the money."
"31633","(31633) Yahya bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: A man came to Omar and said to him: : I had a prostitute’s sister, and she died and left behind a boy, and he died and left behind a group of camels. Omar said: I don’t see any difference between you and him. By lineage, bring her and put her among the camels of charity. He said: Then he came to Ibn Masoud and mentioned that to him, so Abdullah got up and went to Omar. He said: What do you say, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I do not see any relationship between him and him. He said: Isn’t he his maternal uncle and the guardian of his blessings? He said: What do you see? He said: I think he has more right to his money, so Omar returned it to him."
"31634","(31634) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Awan, who said: Hammad was asked about a man who bequeathed money to the poor? He said: He saw nothing wrong with giving preference to some over others according to the need."
"31635","(31635) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: Is it more correct for the bees to settle the children on a letter? God? He said: Yes, and we have been informed of that on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Have you made your children equal? I said: About Al-Numan? He said: And others, they claimed."
"31636","(31636) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir say: My father gave me Atiya, and the mother of Amr bin Rawahi said: I will not be satisfied until you bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, you gave the son of Amr a gift, so you commanded me to I thank you, so he said: Did you give each of your children the like of this? He said: No. He said: Fear God and be just among your children. He said: So he returned and returned your gift.\n(Bukhari 2587, Muslim 1242)"
"31637","(31637) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Nu’man, on the authority of His father: That his father gave him a boy, and that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to testify to him, and he said: Your son has eaten. I gave him something like this. He said: No. He said: So return it to him. (Muslim 1242. Tirmidhi 1367)"
"31638","(31638) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: Go with my father. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bear witness to the gift he gave you. He said: You have others. He said: Yes. He said: Did you give them all the same as you gave them? He said: No, he said: I do not bear witness to injustice. (Bukhari 2650, Ahmed 268)"
"31639","(31639) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: When Tawus was asked about it, he would recite: {Is the most correct? The ignorant ones seek."
"31640","(31640) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Urwah said: It repels from the cruelty of a living thing what it repels from the cruelty of it. The dead"
"31641","(31641) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Masma’ ibn Thabit, on the authority of Ikrimah: He hated it."
"31642","(31642) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to prefer A man is fair between his two children, even in kissing."
"31643","(31643) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam: He disliked a man preferring some of his children over others, and he was He rewards him in judgment."
"31644","(31644) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, that he said: There is no harm in a man giving preference. Some of his children are superior to others."
"31645","(31645) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abi Hayyan, he said: My father told me, he said: A neighbor attended Shurayh had children, so he divided his wealth among them, not wanting to be just. Then he called Shurayh and he came and said: O father of my unlettered people. I divided my wealth between my children and my family, and I have given you testimony. So Shurayh said: God’s division is more fair than yours, so return them to me. The arrows of God and His obligations, and let me bear witness. Otherwise, do not let me bear witness, for I do not bear witness to injustice."
"31646","(31646) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of?? Masruq: He brought a man to give instructions, and he gave orders to do things that were not appropriate. Masruq said: Indeed, God has made an apportionment among you, and it is good. And whoever desires his opinion from the opinion of God will go astray. Make a bequest to your relatives from those who do not desire it, then leave the money to those who May God bless him."
"31647","(31647) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Ash-Shu’bi: Concerning a man who had leprosy, and he said: My brother is my partner in my wealth, and he said: If the witnesses bear witness, he enjoined it before his pain befalls him, so share it with him."
"31648","(31648) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hikam and Al-Hasan, who said: If some of the heirs acknowledge a debt The deceased will be rewarded for his share."
"31649","(31649) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning an heir who acknowledged a debt, he said: It is upon him for his share. With his share, he said: Then he said after that: It will be deducted from his share."
"31650","(31650) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He has his share according to his share."
"31651","(31651) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Amir: Concerning a man who died and left behind two sons, and left two hundred A dinar. Then one of the two sons confirmed that his father owed fifty dinars. He said: It will be taken from this one’s share and given to the other. His share"
"31652","(31652) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: If some of the heirs acknowledge a debt owed by The dead person will be rewarded with his share."
"31653","(31653) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If two or three of the heirs testify, then they only acknowledge it. themselves"
"31654","(31654) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible for the heirs to take account of what they inherited."
"31655","(31655) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Whatever witnesses from among the Muslims are valid, their testimony is permissible. All the heirs."
"31656","(31656) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If two of the heirs testify, it is permissible It is permissible for them both in their shares, and the ruling said: It is permissible for them all."
"31657","(31657) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: If two of the heirs of a man testify With a religion he was given his religion."
"31658","(31658) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If one of the heirs testifies, it is permissible for all of them."
"31659","(31659) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He was asked about a man. He said: If it happened to me Something happened and my servant was free, so he needed it. Should he sell it to him? He said: Yes."
"31660","(31660) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir: Concerning a man who said to his servant: If he dies in this illness, So you are free. He said: He does not have the right to sell it until he dies."
"31661","(31661) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad: They both disliked that the trustee be bought from Inheritance is something."
"31662","(31662) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: It is not permissible for a governor to buy from His guardian\n He said: Mujahid said: Do not buy one hand from the other."
"31663","(31663) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah ibn Zufar, who said: He was with Abdullah and a man came to him. On the horse Ablaq, and he said: Do you command me to buy this? He said: What is the matter with him? He said: A man bequeathed to me and left him, so I set him in the market for a price. He said: Do not buy him, and do not borrow from his money.\n Abu Ishaq said: I heard it from his prayer sixty years ago."
"31664","(31644) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sinan bin Harun Al-Barjami narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, they said: Concerning a man who bequeathed a third to his servant. They said: That is from his slave, if the third was more than the eighth of it. He freed them and paid to them what remained, even if it was less than an eighth of it. He freed them and gave them what remained, even if he bequeathed to them a dirham. If the heirs wish, they may permit it, and if they wish, they may not permit it."
"31665","(31665) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir: That It was said to him in his will upon death: If only you freed your servant! So he recited these verses: {And those who had left behind them weak offspring should fear for themselves}"
"31666","(31646) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir: When death approached him and he had a boy, it was said to him: If only you freed this one? He said: Indeed, I have left no one for my children except him. He said: So they repeated to him: If he freed him, then he recited these verses: {And let him fear those If they had left behind them weak offspring, they would have feared for them."
"31667","(31667) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, who said: A man said to Ar-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym: Give me a will. With your Qur’an, he said: Then he looked at a young son of his and said: {And the relatives are closer to each other in the Book of God}"
"31668","(31668) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Al-Aaliyah fell ill, so he freed a slave. They mentioned to him that he was from beyond the Daylight. Then he said: If he is alive, then I will not free him, but if he is dead, then he will be freed. And he mentioned these verses: {And he has descendants. Weak}"
"31669","(31669) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Al-Ashja’i, he heard Sufyan say: Concerning a man who bequeathed a third to two men. Then one of them was found dead. He said: It will be for the other. Meaning: a full third.\n Yahya said: This is the saying."
"31670","(31670) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who made a will for the successor of his children. So-and-so said: The woman is not the heel."
"31671","(31671) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: A man’s successor means his children, and his children. His children are male."
"31672","(31672) Abu Asama told us, he said: Waddah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a man who died and left behind three sons. And he said: A third of my wealth is for my youngest son. The eldest said: I do not allow it, and the middle one said: I do allow it, so he said: Make it nine times. Arrows: Three arrows are raised, and he has his arrow and the arrow of the one who permitted him.\n Hammad said: The arrow will be returned to all of them.\n Amer said: The one who responded only responded to himself."
"31673","(31673) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, who said: Al-Zuhri was asked about a woman who bequeathed a third of What does she have to do with her husband for the sake of God? He said: It is not permissible unless you say: For the sake of God, for my husband, he may place him wherever he wishes."
"31674","(31674) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: I was with Dawud bin Abi Hind, when two or more men from the family of Anas bin Among them was Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, and they brought with them a letter in a document that they mentioned was the will of Anas. Ibn Malik, and her chest was opened: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Anas Ibn Malik wrote in this document. Concerning his will, I am enjoining on whomever I leave behind all of your family to fear God, thank Him, and hold fast to your rope. And faith in His promise, and He enjoined upon them peace of mind, compassion, righteousness, and piety. Then He enjoined, if He died, that a third He has no right to do so unless he changes his will before joining God. A thousand in the way of God if it is the matter of the mothers on that day. All together, and in the slaves and the relatives, and whoever for whom emancipation from his slave was named on the day he returned from me and emancipation overtook him, then it is The guardian of my will shall evaluate it for a third, without any objection or dispute."
"31675","(31675) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There were some among them who inherited the silent one, and some among them did not. He inherits it."
"31676","(31676) Abdullah bin Musa told us, saying: Sufyan said: It is not permissible to make a will for people of war."
"31677","(31677) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib: That a man commanded that two slaves be freed for a price. He named it, but for that price there were no two slaves found, so I asked Ata’, and he said: Buy one slave and free him for it."
"31678","(31678) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hisham bin Hassan told us: His first will was Muhammad bin Sirin: This is what Muhammad ibn Abi Amr recommended, that he bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is his servant. and His Messenger, and he commanded his children and his family to {Fear God and make peace between you, and obey God and His Messenger. You are believers.} And I enjoin upon you what Abraham enjoined upon his sons and Jacob: {O my sons, indeed, God has chosen for you the religion So do not die unless you are Muslims.} He claimed that it was the first commandment of Anas bin Malik."
"31679","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(31679) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever learns the Qur’an So let him learn the obligatory duties, and not be like a man who is met by a Bedouin and says to him: Are you an immigrant, Abdullah? And he says: Yes. So he says: Some of my family died and left behind such-and-such, and if he knew it, it was knowledge that God gave him, and if he did not He does well and says: Why do you prefer us, O Muhajireen? (Bayhaqi 209)"
"31680","(31680) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, In the same way"
"31681","(31681) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar said: Learn the religious duties, for they are among the Your religion"
"31682","(31682) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Example He who recites the Qur’an and does not do the religious duties well is like two hands without a head."
"31683","(31683) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Whoever reads Surah An-Nasa’, then learns what is hidden from what is not hidden from him, knowledge of the religious duties."
"31684","(31684) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq: It was said to him: Was she Aisha? You do the obligatory duties well, so he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have seen the sheikhs of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. The great ones ask us about the religious duties?"
"31685","(31685) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: I have not seen anyone more knowledgeable about the obligatory prayer, nor do I know. With jurisprudence or poetry: from Aisha."
"31686","(31686) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali bin Rabah narrated to us, on the authority of his father: Omar addressed the people with the tax collector. He thanked God and praised Him, then said: Whoever would like to be asked about the Qur’an, let him come to Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and whoever would like to He asks about the obligatory duties, so let Zayd bin Thabit come."
"31687","(31687) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: Learn the Qur’an. And the obligatory duties, for it is likely that a man will lack the knowledge he used to know, or he will remain among a people who do not know him."
"31688","(31688) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Uqaili narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salma Al-Homsi, on the authority of Sulaiman Bin Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever nullifies an inheritance, may God be pleased with it in His Book, God has nullified it. An inheritance from Paradise. (Saeed bin Mansour 285)"
"31689","(31689) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, He said: Whenever they disagreed about an obligation, they would go to Aisha and she would inform them about it."
"31690","(31690) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to your scholars: Teach me the religious duties. He said: Come Your neighbors"
"31691","(31691) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, who said: Omar said: Learn the melody, the obligatory prayers, and the Sunnah as you learn. The Qur’an."
"31692","(31692) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ma’bud al-Jinni, on the authority of Mu’awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever God desires good for, He will make him understand the religion. (Bukhari 711, Muslim 718)"
"31693","(31693) Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan delivers a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying, “On these sticks, O God, do not prevent me.” You have given, and there is no giver of what you have withheld. Whoever God intends good, He will make you understand the religion. (Ahmad 950 Malik 900)"
"31694","(31694) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: Whomever God desires good, He will make him understand the religion."
"31695","(31695) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: If God wants a servant He is a good man who taught the religion and inspired him with guidance."
"31696","(31696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: If God intends good for a servant, He taught me the religion, increased it in this world, and saw its defects. So whoever is given them has been given the best of the world. And the Hereafter"
"31697","(31697) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab: that Uthman was asked about her, He said: The woman gets a quarter, and the mother gets a third of what remains, and the rest of that goes to the father."
"31698","(31698) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab: that Zayd ibn Thabit He was asked about a woman and two parents, so he gave the woman a quarter, the mother a third of what was left, and what was left went to the father."
"31699","(31699) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a woman and two fathers, He said: A quarter, and a third of what remains."
"31700","(31700) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah was brought about a woman and two fathers, and he said: : When Omar took a road we took it, we found it easy, and there came a woman and two parents, and he made her of Four, so he gave the woman a quarter, and the mother a third of what was left, and he gave the father the rest of that."
"31701","(31701) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Omar, with something similar."
"31702","(31702) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a woman and two fathers: The woman gets a quarter, the mother gets a third of what’s left, and whatever’s left goes to the father."
"31703","(31703) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Omar, With the same, except that he said: He came with a woman and two fathers."
"31704","(31704) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah: He said: It was Omar, when he took a road and we took it, we found him wandering. He was asked about his two wives and his parents, and he said: To the wife is a quarter, and to the mother. A third of what remains, and what remains belongs to the father."
"31705","(31705) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Abbas disagreed with the people of prayer. Concerning a woman, parents, and a husband, he said: The mother gets a third of all the wealth. (Abdul Razzaq 19018, Bayhaqi 228)"
"31706","(31706) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: What prevents them from making it among Twelve shares, so they give three shares to the wife, four shares to the mother, and five shares to the father."
"31707","(31707) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: Abdullah said: What God would have seen me as preferable to a mother over a father."
"31708","(31708) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah said: When Omar walked A path, which we took and found easy, and that there came a woman and two fathers, so he assigned to the woman a quarter, and to the mother a third. What remains, and what remains belongs to the father."
"31709","(31709) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi: Concerning a woman and two fathers: for a woman. A quarter, and the mother gets a third of what remains.\n Abu Bakr said: This is one of four shares: the woman gets one share, which is a quarter, and the mother gets a third of what remains, which is one share. And the father has two shares."
"31710","(31710) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asbaani, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas sent me to Zayd ibn Thabit to ask him about a husband and parents. Zayd said: The husband gets half, and the mother gets a third. What remained was one-sixth, so Ibn Abbas sent to him: In the Book of God can you find this? He said: I hate to prefer a mother over a father. Ibn Abbas used to give the mother a third of all wealth."
"31711","(31711) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Suleiman, who said: Abraham used to impose it as Zayd agreed."
"31712","(31712) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah: Concerning a husband and two parents: for the husband The half, a third of what remains goes to the mother, and whatever remains goes to the father."
"31713","(31713) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Mandal narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali and Zayd bin Thabit. : Concerning a woman and two parents and a husband and two parents. He said: He said: The mother gets a third of what is left."
"31714","(31714) Abdă told us, on the authority of Al-Amash: That Ibn Abbas sent to Zaid to ask him about a husband and parents? Zaid said: The husband gets half, and the mother gets a third of what is left. Ibn Abbas said: Can you find for her in the Book of God a third of what is left? Zaid said: This is my opinion, and God knows best.\n Abu Bakr said: These are six shares: the husband gets three shares, the mother gets one share, and two shares gets the father."
"31715","(31715) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: Muadh made a ruling. In Yemen, there are a son and a sister from a father and a mother: half to the sister, and half to the son."
"31716","(31716) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Muadh, similar to that."
"31717","(31717) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Bura ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, He said: Ibn al-Zubayr did not give anything to the sister and son until she told him that Muadh had decreed an oath for his son and sister. For father and mother: half to the son and half to the sister. He said: You are my messenger to Ibn Utbah, so tell him about that."
"31718","(31718) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I narrated to Ibn Al-Zubayr with the words of Muadh, and he said: You are my messenger to Ibn Utba, so inform him of that."
"31719","(31719) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Masry narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Abi narrated to us. Habib, on the authority of Abu Salama: Omar divided the money between the son and the sister in half."
"31720","(31720) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah: In His son and sister. He said: half and half."
"31721","(31721) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Ibn Al-Zubayr had To prevent sisters and daughters from inheriting, so I told him that Mu’adh had decided it among us: He inherited a son and a sister."
"31722","(31722) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ali, Ibn Masoud, and Muadh used to say about His son and sister: half and a half, and this is the saying of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for Ibn al-Zubair and Ibn Abbas."
"31723","(31723) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah bin He admonished him and he ordered me to reconcile the inheritance between the son and the sister, and Ibn al-Zubayr had ordered him not to inherit. There is nothing between the sister and the son, and I will reconcile between them when Al-Aswad ibn Yazid comes and says: I saw Mu’adh In Yemen, the money was divided between the son and the sister, and I went to Ibn al-Zubayr and informed him of that, so he ordered me to come to you. So I will inform you of that so that you may judge it and write it down to him. Then he said: O Aswad, you are with us attested, so go to him and inform him. That is what he should decide.\n Abu Bakr said: And this is from two arrows: a share for the son and a share for the sister."
"31724","(31724) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl bin Shurahbil, who said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman bin Rabi’a asked them about his son, his son’s son, and his father’s and mother’s sister? They said: Half is for the son, and what is left is for the sister. Go to Ibn Masoud and ask him, for he will follow us. He said: So the man came to Ibn Masoud asked him and told him what they said, so he said: I have gone astray, and I am not of those who are guided, but I will judge by what the Messenger of God has judged. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: half is for the son, and for the son’s son is one-sixth, you complete two-thirds, and what remains is for the sister."
"31725","(31725) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He decided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his son, his son’s son, and a sister: he gave him half to the daughter, and to his son’s son a sixth. You complete the two-thirds, and take the remainder.\n Abu Bakr said: These are of six shares: three shares are for the son, one share is for the son’s son, and one share is for the sister. Saman"
"31726","(31726) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: That it was He allocates two-thirds to the sisters and daughters, and allocates what remains to the males and not the females, and Aisha shared among them, So it made what remained after the thirty {for the male the equivalent of the portion of two females}"
"31727","(31727) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jabir, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit: He said about it: This is from the decree of the pre-Islamic people: men inherit, not women."
"31728","(31728) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: He used to take the words of Abdullah In terms of maternal and paternal sisters, and paternal brothers and sisters, he made what was left over two-thirds for males, not females, so he went out as a kharaj. To Medina, he said: Then he came with the intention of sharing among them, he said: Then Alqamah said to him: What has refuted you from the statement of Abd? God? Have you met anyone more steadfast in yourself than him? He said: He said: No, but I met Zayd bin Thabit and found him to be one of those well-established in knowledge."
"31729","(31729) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: He came and Alqamiya said to him: What Was Ibn Masoud steadfast? Masruq said to him: No, but I saw Zayd bin Thabit and the people of Medina associating with you."
"31730","(31730) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: To his two sisters, to his father and mother. two-thirds, and to his brothers to his father and to his sisters whatever remains. {For the male is the equivalent of the share of two females} in the words of Ali and Zaid, And in the words of Abdullah: Two-thirds are for his sisters, for his father and his mother, and what remains is for the males of his brothers, not their females.\n Abu Bakr said: And this in both statements is a total of three shares: for sisters and daughters, two-thirds, and the remaining third So it is between brothers and sisters, or between his son’s daughters and his son’s sons, for the male the equivalent of the share of two females."
"31731","(31731) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his two daughters and his son, his son. And the son of a son lower than her: for his two-thirds daughters, and whatever is left over for his son’s son, he shall return to those above him and to those with him of the daughters. In the saying of Ali and Zayd: {For the male is the equivalent of the portion of two females} and it is not to be referred to whoever is lower than him, and in the saying of Abdullah: For his two-third daughters, and for his son’s son as long as he remains, he has no objection to his sister, nor to those above him, because he Complete two-thirds.\n Abu Bakr said: This is out of nine, according to the statement of Ali and Zayd: So two-thirds will go to the two daughters: And three will remain. Two shares: The son’s son has two shares, and his sister has two shares, and in Abdullah’s statement: Of three shares: two-thirds are for the two daughters. Two shares, and to the son’s son as long as he remains a sharer."
"31732","(31732) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Abdullah used to say about his son, and his son is a son And the sons of a son, and the sons of a paternal sister and mother, and a paternal sister and brothers: that Ibn Masoud used to give him half of his money, then Consider, if the males divide their shares more than one-sixth, he does not add to them the sixth, and if their shares are less than He divided one-sixth with it, and no harm affected it, and others among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: For this half. And whatever remains, the male gets the share of two females.\n Abu Bakr said: This is the origin of six shares."
"31733","(31733) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ali and Zayd used to say about someone’s cousins. A maternal brother: He gives him one-sixth, and whatever remains between him and his cousins, and Abdullah used to give him all the money."
"31734","(31734) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He was brought among the cousins. One of them was a maternal brother, and Ibn Masoud gave him all the money, so Ali said: May God have mercy on Abu Abdul Rahman, if he For a jurist, if I were me, I would give him a sixth, and he was their partner."
"31735","(31735) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha`, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: It was Judgment is made among the cousins, one of whom is a maternal brother, according to the ruling of Abdullah."
"31736","(31736) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her cousins. One of them is her maternal brother. He said: Then Omar, Ali, and Zaid decided on her: Her maternal brother has a sixth, and he is He has yet to partner with them in the money, and Abdullah has decided that the money is his and not his cousins.\n Abu Bakr said: According to the words of Omar, Ali and Zayd: It is from six arrows, and according to the words of Abdullah and Shurayh: From one share, which is all the money."
"31737","(31737) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Aws, on the authority of Hakim bin Aqal, who said: Ali was brought about two cousins. One of them is a husband, and the other is a maternal brother. So he said to Shuraih: Say about her. Shuraih said: Half goes to the husband, and what’s left goes to the brother. He said: Laha Ali: opinion? He said: I thought so, so Ali gave the husband half, and the brother a sixth, and divided what remained between them."
"31738","(31738) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning A woman left behind three cousins, one of whom was her husband, and the other was her maternal brother. Ali and Zaid said: The husband gets half. The maternal brother gets a sixth, and whatever remains is shared between them. Ibn Masoud said: The husband gets half, and whatever remains goes to the maternal brother.\n Abu Bakr said: And this is in the statement of Ali and Zayd from six: The husband gets three half, and the brother gets a sixth from the mother, and what remains is Two shares, so it is between them, and in the words of Ibn Masoud from two shares: The husband gets half, and what remains goes to the mother’s brother."
"31739","(31739) Yahya bin Zakariya told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left Her mother’s two brothers, one of them is her cousin. Ali and Zayd said: The third is between them, and what is left goes to her cousin. He said Ibn Masoud: The money is between them.\n Abu Bakr said: This is according to the statement of Ali and Zayd from three arrows, and according to Ibn Masoud it is from two arrows."
"31740","(31740) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, saying: I asked Sa`id bin Jubayr about his sons. And two cousins, one of whom is a maternal brother? He said: Half is for the son, and what is left is for the cousin who is not a maternal brother, and a maternal brother does not inherit with a child. He said: So I asked Ata: He said: Saeed made a mistake. The son gets half, and what remains between them is two halves.\n He said: Abu Bakr: This is in the words of Sa’id bin Jubayr from Samin: For the half son and for the cousin who is not With one half of the mother’s brother, and in the word “giving” of four: two shares for the son, and two shares between them."
"31741","(31741) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left one of her paternal uncles behind. Her mother’s two brothers, and Ali and Zaid decided on her: Her mother’s brother has a sixth, then he is your partner after that in the money. Ibn Masoud ruled regarding it: All the money is his, and this is a lineage that is in polytheism, then its family is safe after it.\n Abu Bakr said: This, according to Ali and Zayd, is from six arrows, and according to Abdullah, it is from one arrow. Because it is all money."
"31742","(31742) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her brothers to her mother. Men and women, and they are her cousins in the clan. He said: They divide a third among them: men and women alike. The remaining two-thirds are exclusively for the males, excluding the women, in the ruling of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them.\n And this is in their statement, all of three shares."
"31743","(31743) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his two daughters and his sons. His sons, both men and women: two-thirds are for his daughters, and whatever is left is for the males, not the females. Abdullah did not increase the sisters. And the daughters are two-thirds, and Ali and Zaid used to share among them, so what remained {for the male is like a portion The two females}"
"31744","(31744) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Simak ibn al-Fadl, he said: I heard Wahhab speaking, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Masoud said: I witnessed Omar sharing a third with the brothers from the father and mother with the brothers from the mother, so a man said to him: You have made a judgment about it. This is the first year other than this. He said: How did you make up your case? He said: You made it for the maternal brothers, and you did not make anything for the brothers from the father and mother. He said: That is according to what we have decreed, and this is according to what we have decreed. What we have undone (Abdul Razzaq 19005)"
"31745","(31745) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: that Omar, Zaid, and Ibn Masoud were They associate in marriage a mother and brothers by a mother and a father and sisters by a mother. They associate brothers on the father’s side and a mother with brothers. For the mother in share, and they used to say: The father only increased their closeness, and they made their males and females equal in it."
"31746","(31746) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her husband. And her mother and her sisters are to her father, and her mother and her brothers are to her mother: her husband gets half, three shares, and her mother gets one-sixth. One share, and one-third to her sisters for her mother, and he did not give her sisters to her father or mother any of the inheritance. Ali was judged, and he shared among them Omar, Abdullah, and Zayd bin Thabit: between brothers on the father and mother, with the mother’s sons in a third. whom they inherited, except that they shared in it their males and their females alike."
"31747","(31747) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz: that Uthman was a partner among them."
"31748","(31748) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Shuraih and Masruq: They joined the brothers on the father’s side. And the mother with her maternal brothers."
"31749","(31749) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, in the same way, he said: What The father increased their closeness."
"31750","(31750) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he said: For her mother is one-sixth, Her husband gets half, and a third between the brothers on the mother and the brothers on the father and mother."
"31751","(31751) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, he said: His son died. By Al-Hasan bin Al-Hasan, and she left her wife, her mother, her brothers to her mother, and her sisters to her father and mother, so they rose to Omar. Ibn Abdul Aziz, so he gave the husband half, and the mother a sixth, and he shared between the brothers from the mother and the brothers from the father and mother, and he said For the husband: Hold back from your relatives. Will another arrow join them until it can be seen whether she is pregnant or not?"
"31752","(31752) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah and Omar were polytheists. He said: And they Ali does not associate partners with You.\n Abu Bakr said: This is out of six shares: the husband gets the half, three shares, the mother gets a sixth, and the brothers from the mother get the sixth. A third is two shares."
"31753","(31753) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali: He was He does not associate you with anything."
"31754","(31754) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali: He was not He associates you with Him."
"31755","(31755) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ali did not associate partners with you."
"31756","(31756) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah: He was not He associates you with polytheism and says: The arrows have ceased."
"31757","(31757) Mu’ashar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ali: He did not associate partners among them."
"31758","(31758) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit: He was not He associates you with Him."
"31759","(31759) Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: That Ali, the father of Musa, and my father They did not associate partners with you. Waki’ said: There is not one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but they differed from him regarding partnership. Except for Ali, for he did not associate partners with you."
"31760","(31760) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Omar: He divided the money between his paternal and maternal uncles."
"31761","(31761) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ziyad, who said: I know what Omar did. He made the blind In the position of the father, and the maternal uncle in the position of the mother."
"31762","(31762) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, who said: For the two paternal uncles, and for the paternal uncles. One-third"
"31763","(31763) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suleiman al-Absi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali: He used to say about The paternal aunt and paternal aunt, according to the saying of Omar: two-thirds for the paternal aunt, and one-third for the maternal paternal aunt."
"31764","(31764) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, that he used to lodge the paternal uncle in the same place as his father. The maternal aunt is in the same position as the mother."
"31765","(31765) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar and Abdullah used to inherit the aunt and uncle. If there is no other than them.\n Ibrahim said: They used to place the paternal aunt in the position of the father, and the maternal aunt in the position of the mother."
"31766","(31766) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Bashir al-Hamdani, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he used to say Concerning the paternal aunt and paternal aunt: one-third is for the paternal aunt, and one-third is for the maternal paternal aunt."
"31767","(31767) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to inherit as much as Have mercy on them"
"31768","(31768) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: that Omar inherited the maternal aunt and paternal uncle, so he inherited the paternal uncle. Two-thirds, and the empty third."
"31769","(31769) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Masoud said: For the paternal aunt, one-third, and for the maternal uncle, one-third."
"31770","(31770) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was called. Peace be upon him, and he was led to the funeral of a man from the Ansar. Then he came to Ali on a donkey and said: What did he leave behind? They said: He left behind his uncle and maternal uncle. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man died and left behind his paternal uncle and maternal uncle, then he walked away, then He said: A man died and left behind a paternal uncle and a maternal uncle. Then he said: I did not find anything of them. (Abu Dawud 361, Saeed bin Mansour 163)"
"31771","(31771) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr, who said: Omar said: It is strange that the paternal aunt is inherited. And you do not inherit."
"31772","(31772) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked May God bless him and grant him peace on the inheritance of his paternal aunt and maternal aunt while he was riding, so he remained silent, then he walked away, then he said: Tell me. Gabriel, that they have no inheritance."
"31773","(31773) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to think that the inheritance should go to the male relatives, not the paternal uncles. And the aunt"
"31774","(31774) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ al-Zarqi. On the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hanif Al Ansari, on the authority of Abu Imamah bin Sahl bin Hanif: A man threw stones. A man with an arrow killed him, and he had no heir except a maternal uncle, so Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah wrote to Umar about that, so he wrote to him. Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God and His Messenger are the masters of those who have no masters, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heirs. No (Tirmidhi 2103 and Ibn Majah 2737)"
"31775","(31775) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar’s maternal uncle inherited all the money. He said: He was a maternal uncle. And his lord."
"31776","(31776) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr: Omar inherited a maternal uncle. And a master of his master."
"31777","(31777) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: Badil bin Misra al-Uqaili told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Hawzani, on the authority of Al-Miqdam, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A maternal uncle is the heir of someone who has no heir. (Abu Dawud 2891, Ibn Hibban 6035)"
"31778","(31778) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: Masruq was asked about a man who died and had no heir except His maternal uncle and nephew? He said: The maternal uncle has the share of his sister, and the brother’s son has the share of her father."
"31779","(31779) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi’ ibn Hibban said: Ibn Dahdahah perished, and he had an opinion about them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Asim bin Adiy. He said: Did he have any lineage among you? He said: No, he said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave his inheritance to his sister’s son, Abu Lubab bin Abdul-Mundhir. (Abdul Razzaq 19120)"
"31780","(31780) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: They attached the duties to their families, and whatever remains is for those closest to them. (Bukhari 6732, Muslim 1233)"
"31781","(31781) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban. On the authority of his uncle, Wasi’ ibn Hibban, he said: Thabit ibn al-Dahdah was a man who came - meaning: suddenly - and he was with Banu Anif, or Among the children of Al-Ajlan, he died and left no heir except his sister’s son, Abu Lubab bin Abdul-Mundhir, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abdul Razza, 19120)"
"31782","(31782) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: Do you know how much of Hamza’s son is from Mona? My mother’s sister freed a man and he died and his inheritance was divided between her daughter and her. He said: : In the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Saeed bin Mansour 173)"
"31783","(31783) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, On the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of his son Hamza - Muhammad said: And she is Ibn Shaddad’s maternal sister - she said: A servant of mine died and left him. His daughter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided his wealth between him and his daughter, giving him half and half to her."
"31784","(31784) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He gave his son Hamza half and his daughter half."
"31785","(31785) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Burda : That a man died and left behind his daughter and his masters who freed him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him half of his daughter. And his servants are half. (Abu Dawud 363. Bayhaqi 241)"
"31786","(31786) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shams Al-Kindiyah, she said: I sued to Ali regarding my father: He died and left no one but me and his master, so he gave me half and his master half."
"31787","(31787) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shamoos, on the authority of Ali, with something similar."
"31788","(31788) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Al-Kanood, on the authority of Ali: He made a ruling regarding his son and his male servant, giving the daughter half, and the male master half."
"31789","(31789) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That a servant of his son Hamza died and left behind his daughter and son. Hamza, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave his son Hamza half, and his daughter half."
"31790","(31790) Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I disputed until Shurayh had a servant of ours who died and left behind his two daughters and his servants, so Shurayh gave two-thirds to his daughters, and he gave His master is one-third."
"31791","(31791) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The hadith of his son Hamza was mentioned to him: that the Prophet prayed God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her half, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed her his own taste."
"31792","(31792) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad: He was a servant of his son Hamza died and left behind his daughter and his two sons, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave his daughter half, and his son Hamza The half\n Abu Bakr said: This is from two shares: half for the daughter and half for the master. (Tahawi 401, Bayhaqi 241)"
"31793","(31793) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. On the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: That Ali used to say regarding the kings and the People of the Book: They should not veil themselves, nor should they They inherit."
"31794","(31794) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, who said: They do not block And they will not inherit."
"31795","(31795) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said, Omar said: It is not withheld from one who does not inherit."
"31796","(31796) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kail, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Ali, who said: The possessed do not inherit, nor do they withhold."
"31797","(31797) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kail, on the authority of Abu Sadiq: That a man asked Ali about A woman died and left behind her sister and mother as mamluks? Ali said: Does the sixth circle around her neck? He said: No, so he said: We will leave it for the rest of the day."
"31798","(31798) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, on the authority of Shuraih, that He gave the inheritance of a man - his brother Mamlouk - to his brother's free children."
"31799","(31799) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The free sons of his brother will inherit it."
"31800","(31800) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father: Concerning a man who died and left his mother a slave, and she found him free. He said: Money is for the grandfather."
"31801","(31801) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali and Zaid: The Mamluks and the polytheists, they said: They shall not withhold, nor shall they inherit."
"31802","(31802) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: He used to be veiled by the Mamluks and the People of the Book, And he does not inherit from them."
"31803","(31803) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: If a man dies and leaves behind his father or brother, Or his son is a slave and leaves no heir, then he is bought, freed, and then inherited."
"31804","(31804) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: Concerning a man who died and left behind his father. A slave. He said: It is bought from his wealth and set free, then it is inherited. He said: And Al-Hasan used to say it."
"31805","(31805) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, with something similar."
"31806","(31806) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar and Abdullah were given The inheritance is with the relatives. Fudail said: So I said to Ibrahim: Is it ok for me? He said: He was the most severe of them in that: to give to relatives."
"31807","(31807) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, Omar, Ali, and Abdullah, with a similar story."
"31808","(31808) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyya - Abu Bakr said: I think so, On the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr - he said: I was sitting with Abu Al-Darda’ - he was a judge - when a man came to him and said: My sister’s son died. He did not leave an heir, so what do you think of his wealth? He said: Go and catch him."
"31809","(31809) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hayyan al-Ju`fi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla: that Ali had a son. And a woman and a client, so he gave the son half, and the woman the eighth, and returned what remained to the son, but he did not give the client Something"
"31810","(31810) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Ibrahim: He denied the hadith of his son. Hamza, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed her only his taste."
"31811","(31811) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: A servant of Alqamiya made a will for the family of He gave him a third, and his nephew gave his mother two-thirds."
"31812","(31812) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim, who said: Ali was brought about a man who left his grandmother and his companions. So he gave the grandfather the money but not the slave."
"31813","(31813) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I was walking with him when a woman overtook him. At the companion's house, she said: Your mistress has died, so take her inheritance. He said: It is yours, and she said: May God bless you with it. He said: If it had been mine, I would not have left it for you, and at that time he would be in need of a fortune to obtain from her inheritance, from Five dirhams, so I said to him: What is this? He said: Her mother’s sister’s son."
"31814","(31814) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: Ibn Masoud was brought on the authority of a mother and brothers. For a mother, so the brothers gave the mother a third, and he gave the mother the rest of the money, and he said: The mother is a kinsman of someone who has no ancestors."
"31815","(31815) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah was brought There is a mother and his brothers by mother, so he gave the mother a sixth and the brothers a third, and returned what remained to the mother, and said: The mother is a supporter of the one who is not a supporter. His, and Ibn Masoud did not reject a father's sister with a paternal and maternal sister, nor did he reject his son's son with his two sons being descendants."
"31816","(31816) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah and Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: that Ali used to respond to everyone. A person with a share, except the husband and the wife."
"31817","(31817) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ali that he used to respond to every A person with a share, except the husband and the wife."
"31818","(31818) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: That Ali used to respond to the people of Arrows from people of wombs."
"31819","(31819) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: It was mentioned that he had a case that Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah: He gave his son or sister all the money, and Al-Sha’bi said: This is Abdullah’s ruling."
"31820","(31820) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abdullah: He was responding to his son and sister. And the mother, if she is not a married woman, and Zaid does not give them anything except her share."
"31821","(31821) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah did not respond to six things: to a husband, Nor a woman, nor a grandfather, nor against paternal sisters with paternal and maternal sisters, nor against a son’s daughters with lineal daughters, nor against a sister. To a mother with a mother. Ibrahim said: So I said to your mother, “He responds to the maternal brothers with the grandparents.” He said: “If you wish.” He said: “And it was Ali.” He responds to all of them except the husband and the wife."
"31822","(31822) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah did not respond to six things: He would not respond. Not against a husband, not against a wife, not against a grandfather, not against a father’s sister with a father’s sister and a mother, not against a mother’s sister with a mother, not against his son. A son was crucified with his son."
"31823","(31823) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Salem, the servant of Abu Hudhayfy, was martyred. He said: So Abu Bakr gave his daughter half and gave the other half for the sake of God."
"31824","(31824) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, who said: Ibrahim said: There was no one among The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would respond to a woman or a husband with something. He said: And Zaid used to give him everything. He fulfilled his due obligation, and whatever remained, he put it in the treasury."
"31825","(31825) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah would not respond to a paternal sister with a paternal and maternal sister. He does not return anything to the son of a son with his son, nor does he return anything to the brothers of a mother with a mother, nor to a husband, or a woman."
"31826","(31826) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah and Al-A’mash, who said: No one would respond to a grandfather unless it was someone else."
"31827","(31827) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about blindness: Is he more deserving of inheritance, or Your brother's son? He said: He said to me: And you do not know that. He said: I said: The brother’s son has more right than the paternal uncle. Abu Ishaq said: And Amer witnessed it. It is stolen that he said: Place them in the positions of their fathers."
"31828","(31828) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Bring down the relatives. The homes of their fathers."
"31829","(31829) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi: Concerning two nephews and an uncle. He said: Money. To his brother's son."
"31830","(31830) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Money is for the blind."
"31831","(31831) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah and Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to inherit as much as Have mercy on them"
"31832","(31832) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Al-Shu’bi about the two sons of a brother and two uncles, which of them has more right? By inheritance? He said: The brother’s son. He said: Place them in the positions of their fathers."
"31833","(31833) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Ibrahim said: Ali said: He does not strike anyone who does not. He inherits"
"31834","(31834) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: The one with the arrow has more right. Of those who have no shares"
"31835","(31835) Waki’ said: And other than Sufyan said, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who died and left behind two paternal sisters. And two sisters from a father and a mother. He said: It used to be said: The one with shares has more right than one who has no shares."
"31836","(31836) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a Muslim woman who left her husband. If she is a Muslim, and her mother’s siblings are Muslims, and she has a son who is Christian, Jewish, or an infidel, then her husband gets half. Three shares, and to her sisters, one-third is to her mother, and whatever remains is to the descendant, according to the words of Ali and Zayd, and no A Jew, nor a Christian, can inherit from a Muslim. Abdullah ruled that the husband is entitled to a quarter because she has an infidel son. And they are blocked, according to the statement of Abdullah, and they do not inherit, and according to the statement of Ali and Zaid: They are not blocked, nor are they inherited. He said Abu Bakr: According to Ali and Zayd, this is six arrows, and according to Abdullah bin Masoud, it is four."
"31837","(31837) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said about a Muslim woman who left Her mother is a Muslim and she has brothers who are Christians, Jews, or infidels, so Abdullah ruled: She has a sixth with them, and he made them They are blocked and do not inherit, and all the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that they are not blocked or inherited. They inherit.\n Abu Bakr said: As for the rest of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, other than Abdullah, of four shares. It is for Dhu al-Asbah, and in the case of Abdullah: out of five shares, it is for Dhu al-Asbah by mercy.\n Abu Bakr said: Then this is in their statement, “a total of six shares,” if it is in Abdullah’s statement: “The mother gets one-sixth.” And there are five remaining, and if it is according to the saying of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The mother gets a third, which is two shares. And four for the rest of the gang."
"31838","(31838) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said: Concerning a woman who left her husband Her brothers from her mother are free, and she has a son who is a slave: her husband gets half, three shares, and her brothers gets a third from her mother. Two shares, and the remaining one-sixth belongs to the clan, and her owned son does not inherit anything in Ali’s case.\n Abdullah ruled regarding her: that her husband is entitled to a quarter and a half of a share, and that her son is entitled to the rights of brothers from the mother if he is Owned, and her son does not inherit anything and the husband is excluded from it, and the remaining three-quarters are for the clan.\n Zayd ruled regarding her: that her half is entitled to three shares, and that her brothers are entitled to her mother, one-third is two shares, and what remains is So he is in the treasury if he has no loyalty or kinship.\n Abu Bakr said: This, according to Ali and Zayd, is six arrows, and according to Abdullah bin Masoud, it is four. Names"
"31839","(31839) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The obligatory duties do not count."
"31840","(31840) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid: They neglected the obligation."
"31841","(31841) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: There are two paternal sisters. And a mother, and two maternal sisters, and a husband, and a mother. He said: out of ten, for the two sisters from the father and the mother four, and for the two sisters from the mother. Two shares, three shares for the husband, and one share for the mother.\n Waki` said: The people are on this, and this is what Ibn Al-Faroukh swore."
"31842","(31842) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: My sons’ children will block me instead of my brothers, and I will not block them instead of their brothers."
"31843","(31843) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her sister to her mother. As for her mother, and she has no descendants, her sister from her mother gets a sixth, and her mother gets five-sixths, according to the ruling of Abdullah, and he ruled There is Zaid in her: her sister from her mother gets a sixth, and her mother gets a third, and he puts the rest of it in the treasury, and he made up for it. Ali: They have the money according to what they inherited, so he allocated one-third to the maternal sister and two-thirds to the mother-in-law.\n Abu Bakr said: This, according to Ali, is three lions, and according to Abdullah and Zayd, it is six."
"31844","(31844) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Ibrahim said about a woman who left her sister To her father, to her mother, and to her sister from her father, and there is no descendant to her other than them: so to her sister to her father and to her mother is three. Quarters, and her sister from her father gets a quarter in Ali’s ruling, and Abdullah’s ruling: The sister from her father and mother gets five shares. The paternal sister gets a sixth, and Zaid ruled on it: The paternal and maternal sister gets three shares, and the paternal sister gets a sixth, etc. It remains for the treasury if there is no loyalty or fanaticism.\n Abu Bakr said: This is according to the statement of Ali from three arrows, and according to the statement of Abdullah and Zayd it is from six arrows."
"31845","(31845) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said about a woman who left her daughter And her son’s son and her mother’s son, and she has no descendants: three-fifths to her daughter’s son, one-fifth to her son’s son, and one-fifths to her mother’s son. One-fifth, according to Ali’s ruling, and Abdullah’s ruling regarding it: It is out of twenty-four shares: from that one-sixth is to his son’s son. Four shares, for the mother a quarter of the remaining five shares, and for the son three quarters of twenty: fifteen shares, And Zaid decided on it: The son gets the half, the son gets the sixth, and the mother gets the sixth, and whatever remains is in the treasury if it is not there. Loyalty and fanaticism."
"31846","(31846) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, who said: Abraham said: He inherits from six women. Your wives: the son, the son’s son, the mother, the grandmother, the sister, and the wife. Women inherit from the men in seven groups: they inherit. Her father, her son, her son’s son, her brother, her husband, and her grandfather, and she shall inherit one-sixth from her daughter’s son unless they are He has another nerve."
"31847","(31847) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, he said: A man inherits six Your wives: your daughter, your son’s son, your mother, your grandmother, your sister, and your wife. Seven people inherit from a woman: Her son, her son’s son, her father, her grandfather, her husband, and her brother, and she inherits one-sixth from her daughter’s son, and no He inherits something from her in the words of all of them."
"31848","(31848) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, who said: I asked Ibn Umar on the authority of Ibn Ibnu: Have you seen a man? He left behind his daughter's son. Should he inherit it? He said: No."
"31849","(31849) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Mandal, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In the words of Ali and Zayd. : The son of the son refers to those below him and those above him. For the male, it is like the portion of two females. And in Abdullah’s statement: When he completes The two-thirds do not belong to the son’s daughters."
"31850","(31850) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Mandal narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said regarding Abdullah’s statement: Half is for the son, and what remains is for the son’s sons and the son’s daughters: for the male is the share of two females, unless they increase the son’s daughters. On the sixth"
"31851","(31851) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Brothers do not inherit from the mother. With a son, nor a son, male or female, nor with a father, nor with a grandfather."
"31852","(31852) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, who said: I have not seen a man who was more wise than Ali was asked about two daughters, two fathers, and a woman, and he said: Their price became nine times.\n Abu Bakr said: This is out of twenty-seven shares: sixteen for the two daughters, and eight for the parents. And for the woman three."
"31853","(31853) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: that Abu Bakr used to see the grandfather Father"
"31854","(31854) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Kurdos bin Abbas Al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Abu Musa: Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father."
"31855","(31855) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaiki, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: The one who said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I had taken a friend, I would have taken him as a friend who made the grandfather a father. Meaning: Abu Bakr.\n(Bukhari 3658, Ahmed 4)"
"31856","(31856) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Furat al-Qazzaz, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr wrote To Abdullah bin Utba: Abu Bakr used to make grandfather a father. (Ahmad 4. Abu Ali 6772)"
"31857","(31857) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khalid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Maqil, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas, a man asked him about grandfather? Ibn Abbas said to him: Which father do you have the greatest? The man did not know what to say, so I said: Adam. Ibn Abbas said: God says: O children of Adam."
"31858","(31858) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Bakr, Ibn Abbas, and Uthman: They made grandfather Father"
"31859","(31859) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He made him a father."
"31860","(31860) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaisah Ibn Dhu’ib: That Omar was It is obligatory for the grandfather for whom people do obligatory prayers today. I said to him: What does it mean: the saying of Zayd ibn Thabit? He said: Yes."
"31861","(31861) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who said: The grandfather is in the same position as the father as long as he is not A father is inferior to him, and the son’s son is in the same position as the son, unless there is a son inferior to him."
"31862","(31862) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, who said: A man said to Abu Wa’il: Abu Burda It is claimed that Abu Bakr made the grandfather a father? He said: He lied. If he had made him a father, Omar would not have disagreed with him."
"31863","(31863) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My son’s son died, so what do I have of his inheritance? He said: You have one-sixth. When he returned, he called for it. He said: You have another sixth. When he returned, he called for it. He said: The other sixth is bait.\n(Abu Dawud 2888, Ahmed 428)"
"31864","(31864) Shababi told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Maqil bin Yassar Al-Muzani said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, an obligatory portion of which he was very obligatory, so he gave him a third or One-sixth (Ibn Majah 6722. Tabarani 536)"
"31865","(31865) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Omar said: Who knows the case of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him? He said: Maqil bin Yassar Al-Muzani: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judged about us. He said: What is that? He said: One-sixth. He said: With whom? He said, “I don’t know.” He said, “I don’t know. So what’s the point?”"
"31866","(31866) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: We were We will inherit it from the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It means: seriousness. (Abu Ali 1090)"
"31867","(31867) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ali was no more serious. With the child on one-sixth."
"31868","(31868) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nadhilah, he said: Omar and Abdul God diligently divides what is between Him with the brothers, and the sixth is better for Him than dividing with them. Then Omar wrote To Abdullah: I do not think that we have been unjust in our seriousness. So when this letter of mine comes to you, share it with your brothers. He explained that the third would be better for him than sharing with them, so Abdullah took it."
"31869","(31869) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Abu Al Ala, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: Abdullah used to associate The grandfather is with his brothers, and when they increase, a third of them die. When Alqamiya died, I went to Ubaidah, and they told me that Ibn Masoud He used to share the grandfather with his brothers, and when they were many, he would give him a sixth, so I returned from him and I was silent.\n So I passed by Ubaid bin Nudhaylah, and he said: Why do I see you choking? He said: I said: How can I not be a treacherous person? So I told him, and he said: Both of them are truthful to you. I said: For God’s sake, your father is truthful to me. Both of them, he said: It was Abdullah’s opinion and oath that he should share it with his brothers, so if they increased, he paid a sixth, then He came to Omar and found him sharing it with his brothers. When they increased, a third of them died, so he abandoned his opinion and continued with Omar."
"31870","(31870) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali: He was diligently dividing brotherhood up to one-sixth."
"31871","(31871) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: He came among his six brothers. He found it, so he gave the grandfather a sixth."
"31872","(31872) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ibn Abbas wrote to Ali. He asked him about his six brothers and grandfather? So he wrote to her: Make him like one of them, and erase his letter."
"31873","(31873) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: that Zaid used to share with his brothers what Between it and a third."
"31874","(31874) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar and Abdullah: They used to share the grandfather with Brotherhood is what is between him and a third."
"31875","(31875) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim: That Ali used to share his grandfather’s money with his brothers. One-sixth"
"31876","(31876) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar wrote to Abdullah bin Masoud: We feared that we had been unfair to him, so I will give him a third along with his brothers."
"31877","(31877) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: that Zaid used to say: The grandfather is divided with one person. And the two, if they were three, he would have a third of all the money, and if he had obligatory duties, it would be taken into account, but if it was a third I give him what is good for him, and if the share is good for him, he divides it, and he does not detract from one-sixth of all the money."
"31878","(31878) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah and Zayd were They give a third to the grandfather and two-thirds to the brothers, and in a man who left behind four brothers, his father, his mother, and his two sisters. To his father, his mother, and his grandfather. He said: Ali used to make them sixth shares, for the grandfather a sixth. Ali did not make For the grandfather, it is less than a sixth with the brothers, and whatever remains is for the male, like the share of two females. And Abdullah and Zaid used to give A male’s one-third grandfather and thirty brothers are equal to the share of two females. He said, “In five brothers and a grandfather.” He said: “Then the grandfather in Saying: Ali is one-sixth, and five-sixths is for the brothers, and Abdullah and Zayd used to give the grandfather a third, and the brothers Two-thirds"
"31879","(31879) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Ibn Masoud had no more The grandfather received the sixth with the brothers. He said: So I said to him: I witnessed Omar ibn al-Khattab give him a third with the brothers, so he gave him a third."
"31880","(31880) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Ghanam, who said: The first grandfather In Islam, he inherited: Omar bin Al-Khattab, so he wanted to keep the money, so I said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, they are trees below you. Meaning: build your building.\n Abu Bakr said: This is according to the words of Omar, Abdullah and Zaid out of three shares, so the grandfather gets a third, and whatever remains It is for the brothers, and in the saying of Ali, out of six shares: for the grandfather, one-sixth of the shares, and for the brothers, five shares."
"31881","(31881) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah: In Akhat and Jid: half and half."
"31882","(31882) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his grandfather and his brother to his father. And his mother: the grandfather gets half and his brother gets the half, according to the words of Ali, Abdullah and Zayd. They said about a man who left behind his grandfather and his brothers."
"31883","(31883) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his grandfather and his brother’s son. To his father and mother: the grandfather has the property in the case of Ali, Abdullah and Zayd.\n This is from one share, and it is all money."
"31884","(31884) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his grandfather and his brother to his father. And his mother and his brother to his father: the grandfather gets half, and his brother gets half to his father and his mother according to the saying of Ali and Abdullah, and it was Zaid gives the grandfather a third, and the brother through the father and mother two-thirds. He divides the brother through the father with the brother through the father and mother, and he does not inherit. Something"
"31885","(31885) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah Qasim was very serious. siblings to a third, and he gives each owner his share, and the maternal siblings do not inherit with the grandfather, and he does not share By paternal siblings, paternal and maternal siblings, along with the grandfather, and if she is a paternal and maternal sister and a paternal sister and a grandfather, he gives the paternal sister. The mother is half, and the grandfather is half.\n Ali used to divide the inheritance from the grandfather to the brothers up to one-sixth, and he would give each owner of an obligatory inheritance his due, and he would not inherit from the brothers The mother is with the grandfather, and the grandfather with the child does not exceed one-sixth unless there is no one else, so if she is a paternal and maternal sister, and a brother And a paternal sister, and a grandfather. He gave the half to the paternal sister and the mother, and divided between the brother and the grandfather’s sister.\n Abu Bakr said: This, according to Ali and Abdullah, is from two arrows, and according to Zayd, it is three arrows."
"31886","(31886) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad wanted to inherit The maternal sister along with the grandfather, and he said: Omar inherited the sister with him, so Abdullah bin Utbah said: I am neither a Saba’i nor a Haroori. So follow the trail, for you will not make a mistake on the road as long as you follow the trail."
"31887","(31887) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: None of the Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, inherited. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, his maternal brothers and grandfather."
"31888","(31888) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Zaid did not A maternal brother does not inherit anything, nor does a maternal sister inherit anything from a grandfather."
"31889","(31889) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ali and Abdullah were not The maternal brothers and grandfather inherit something.\n Abu Bakr said: This is from one share, because all the money belongs to the grandfather."
"31890","(31890) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to make the staff of Eight: Three for the husband, three for the sister, one share for the mother, and one share for the grandfather. He said: Ali used to make it out of nine: three for the husband, three for the sister, two shares for the mother, and one share for the grandfather. Zaid used to make it out of nine: three for the husband, three for the sister, two shares for the mother, one share for the grandfather, then He multiplies it by three, and it becomes twenty-seven, so he gives the husband nine, and the mother six, leaving twelve. He gives the grandfather eight, and he gives the sister four."
"31891","(31891) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid, in a similar way. The hadith of Abu Muawiyah, and he added to it: And I was informed on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he used to make the grandfather the father, and the brothers would not inherit. He has something with him, and he gives the husband half, a sixth to the grandfather: two shares, and a third to the mother: two shares."
"31892","(31892) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah and Zaid, Like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"31893","(31893) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I said to Al-Amash: Why was it called Al-Akdriyah? He said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan presented it to a man called al-Akdar. He was looking into the religious duties, but he made a mistake in them. So he called it Al-Akdriyya.\n Waki` said: We were listening before Sufyan explained it, but it was called Al-Akdriyah, because Zaid’s statement was confusing about it. He did not explain what he said."
"31894","(31894) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Ismail bin Raji, on the authority of Ibrahim. And on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Ash-Sha’bi say about a mother, a paternal and maternal sister, and a grandfather: Zayd ibn Thabit said: Out of nine shares: The mother gets three, the grandfather gets four, and the sister gets three. And Ali said: For the sister, the half is three shares, and for the mother a third: two shares, and what remains is for the grandfather, which is one share. Ibn Masoud said: The sister gets half: three shares, and the mother gets a sixth: one share, and whatever remains goes to the grandfather, and he is two shares. Othman said: Three times: a third for the mother, a third for the sister, and a third for the grandfather. Ibn Abbas said: A third is for the mother, and whatever remains is for the grandfather.\n Waki’ said: Al-Sha’bi said: Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf asked me about her? So I informed him of their sayings, and he was amazed at what Ali said, so he said: Whose saying is this? So I said: Abu Turab’s statement. Then Al-Hajjaj understood and said: We did not blame Ali for his judgment, we only blamed such-and-such and such-and-such."
"31895","(31895) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her sister to her father. And her mother, her grandfather, and her mother, so to her sister is to her father and to her mother half, to her mother is a third, and to the grandfather is a sixth, according to the saying Ali\n Abdullah used to say: The mother gets a sixth, the grandfather gets a third, and the sister gets the half. Abdullah used to say: God was not there. To see that I prefer a mother to a grandfather in this obligatory prayer and in no other punishment.\n Zayd used to give the mother a third, and the sister a third of what was left. Zayd divided it into nine shares: for the mother, the third was three. shares, and the sister gets a third of the remaining shares, and the grandfather gets four shares.\n Othman used to divide it into thirds among them: a third for the mother, a third for the sister, and a third for the grandfather.\n Ibn Abbas used to say: The grandfather is in the same position as the father."
"31896","(31896) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: Abdullah used to say about a sister, mother, and grandfather: The sister gets half, and the remaining half goes between the grandfather and mother."
"31897","(31897) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar: Concerning a sister, a mother, and a grandfather. He said: for the sister. Half, one-sixth goes to the mother, and whatever remains goes to the grandfather.\n Abu Bakr said: This, according to the statement of Ali and Abdullah, is from six arrows, and according to the statement of Zaid bin Thabit, it is from nine. Names"
"31898","(31898) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah: He said about his son, sister, and grandfather: He gave the son half, and made what was left between the grandfather and the sister, half to him, and to her half.\n He was asked about his son, two sisters, and a grandfather, so he gave the daughter half, and made what was left between the grandfather and the two sisters, as his half. And they have half.\n He was asked about his son, three sisters, and a grandfather, so he gave the daughter half, and gave the grandfather a fifth of what was left, and he gave the sisters a fifth. Five."
"31899","(31899) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah: Concerning a son, a sister, and a grandfather. He said: Who Four shares: two shares for the daughter, one share for the grandfather, and one share for the sister. I said to him: What if they were both sisters? He said: His servants made it out of four: two shares for the daughter, one share for the grandfather, and one share for the two sisters. I said to him: If they are Three sisters? He said: He made it stolen from ten: the daughter gets five shares, the grandfather gets two shares, and each one of them gets one share."
"31900","(31900) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq: There is a daughter and three sisters. And grandfather, he said: out of ten: the half-daughter gets five shares, the grandfather gets two shares, and each sister gets one share."
"31901","(31901) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah: Concerning his son and a sister. And grandfather, he said: Of the four shares: half for the son, one share for the grandfather, and one share for the sister."
"31902","(31902) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq: Concerning his two sons and two sisters. And grandfather, he said: Of the eight shares: half are for the daughter, four, for the grandfather are two shares, and for each sister is one share."
"31903","(31903) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who left his daughter and sister. To his father, mother and grandparents, the half goes to his daughter, the sixth goes to his grandfather, and whatever remains goes to his sister. According to Ali’s statement, it was not The grandfather with the son adds something to the sixth, and according to what Abdullah said to his daughter, it is half, and whatever remains is between the sister and the grandfather.\n If they are sisters, then what is left between the grandfather and the two sisters, according to the statement of Abdullah and Zaid, and in the statement of Ali: the grandfather gets a sixth, And to the two sisters what is left, and if there are three sisters with the son and the grandfather, then to the son half and to the grandfather a fifth of what is left, and to the sisters Three-fifths according to the statement of Abdullah and Zayd.\n Abu Bakr said: This is in the statement of Ali from six arrows, and in the statement of Abdullah and Zaid from ten arrows: Five shares for the daughter, two shares for the grandfather, and one share for the sisters."
"31904","(31904) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: How can Ali say something about his son, sister, and grandfather? He said: Of the four. He said: I said: This is only in the words of Abdullah."
"31905","(31905) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said about a woman who left her husband And her mother, her paternal brother, and her grandfather: the husband gets half, three shares, the mother gets a third, two shares, and the grandfather gets one share. The saying of Ali and Zaid, and in the saying of Abdullah: The husband gets half, the mother gets a third of what remains, the grandfather gets a share, and the brother gets a share. A share, and if they are brothers or more than that: the husband gets half, the mother gets a share, the grandfather gets a share, and the rest of the shares And it is for his brothers in the words of Ali, Zayd, and Abdullah."
"31906","(31906) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We came to Shurayh and asked him about a husband. A mother, a brother, a grandfather? He said: The husband gets half, and the mother gets a third, then he remained silent, then the one over his head said: He should not say anything about the grandfather. He said: So we came to `Ubaidah and he divided it into six, according to the words of Abdullah. He gave the husband three, the mother one share, and the grandfather one share. And brother Sahama.\n This is what they say, all of six of them."
"31907","(31907) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who left her sister to her father. And her mother and grandfather, so her sister gets half to her father and mother, according to the statement of Ali and Abdullah, and Zaid used to give him the sister. The third and the grandfather are two-thirds.\nAbu Bakr said: This, according to Ali and Abdullah, is from two arrows, and according to Zayd, it is from three arrows."
"31908","(31908) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said: Concerning a man who left behind his grandfather and his sister. To his father and mother, and to his brother to his father, so to the grandfather in the case of Zayd two-fifths out of ten, four shares, and to his sister From his father and mother, half, five, and to his father’s brother, a share. The mother had three-fifths of the money, so you were given half because three-fifths is more than the half, and not to the sister. One, even if he divides it by more than half.\n Ibn Masoud used to give the paternal sister and mother half, and the grandfather half, and he did not count the paternal brothers along with the paternal brothers. And the mother.\n Ali used to give half to the sister from the father and mother, and divide the remaining half between the brothers and the grandfather, the grandfather as one of them. Unless the grandfather’s share is less than one-sixth, if he is one brother, then the half that remains between them, even if they are brothers. Half is between them, and if there are three of them, then the sixth goes to the grandfather, and whatever remains is to the brothers.\n Abu Bakr said: This is in Zayd’s statement “from ten shares,” and in Abdullah’s statement: “from two shares,” and it was Ali makes it one of six if there are many brothers."
"31909","(31909) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said: Concerning a woman who left her mother, And her sister to her father and mother, and her brother to her father, and her grandfather. Zayd ruled concerning her: The mother gets a sixth, and the grandfather gets a fifth. What remained, and the sister got three-fifths of what remained. The brother returned to his sister and did not inherit anything, and Abdullah ruled that: The sister gets three shares, the mother gets one share, and the grandfather gets one share, and Ali decided on it: The sister from the father and mother gets three shares. Shares, and the mother gets shares, and the rest of the shares: the grandfather gets shares, and the brother gets shares.\n This, according to Ali and Zayd, is six arrows, and according to Abdullah, it is five."
"31910","(31910) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said about a woman who left her husband, And her mother, and four sisters she had from her father and mother, and her grandfather. Zaid ruled for her: The husband has three A share, and a share for the mother, and a share for the grandfather, and a share for the sisters, and Ali and Abdullah decided on it for nine shares: The husband gets three shares, the mother gets one share, the grandfather gets one share, and the sisters get four shares.\n Abu Bakr said: So in the statement of Zayd it is six arrows, and in the statement of Ali and Abdullah it is nine arrows."
"31911","(31911) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Salem told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: There is a maternal sister, a father, a brother, and a sister. For a father and a grandfather, in Ali’s saying: The sister from the father and mother gets half, and what remains is divided between the grandfather, the sister and the brother from the father in fifths: The grandfather gets two fifths, and the sister gets five. And in the words of Abdullah: The sister from the father and mother gets half, and the grandfather gets what remains, and the brother and sister from the father have nothing. And in the words of Zayd: Of eighteen shares: for the grandfather, one-third is six, for the brother on the father’s side, six, and for the sister on the father’s side, three.\n The sister from the father and mother gets three shares, then the sister and the brother from the father return six shares to the sister from the father and mother, so it was completed. The half is ninety, and three shares remain for them: for brother Saman and sister Saham.\n And there are two sisters on the father’s side and a mother, and a brother on the father’s side, and a grandfather, according to Ali’s saying: The two sisters on the father’s side and the mother’s two-thirds, and what remains is between the grandfather. And the brother, and in the words of Abdullah: The two sisters from the father and the mother have two-thirds, and the grandfather gets what remains, and the brother from the father has nothing. And in the words of Zaid: There are three shares: one share for the grandfather, one share for the brother, and one share for the two sisters, then the brother returns one share. The father has shares over the two sisters from the father and the mother.So they complete the two-thirds, and nothing is left for him.\n And there are two sisters from a father and a mother, and a sister from a father, and a grandfather, in\n The saying of Ali and Abdullah: The two sisters get two-thirds from the father and the mother, and what’s left goes to the grandfather, and the sister from the father has nothing. And in the saying Zayd: Of five shares: two shares for the grandfather, two shares for the two sisters from the father and mother, and two shares for the paternal sister, then it is returned. The sister from the father has shares over the two sisters from the father and the mother, and nothing is left for her.\n And there are two sisters on the father’s side and a mother, and a brother and a sister on the father’s side, and a grandfather, according to Ali’s statement: The two sisters on the father’s side and the mother’s account are two-thirds, and the grandfather is given a sixth. And whatever remains, between the sister and the brother, from the father to the male, is equal to the share of two females. And in the words of Abdullah: For two sisters from the father and the mother. Two-thirds, and whatever remains belongs to the grandfather, but the paternal brother and sister do not have anything. And in Zayd’s statement: Of fifteen shares: the grandfather has a third. Five shares, and for the brother from the father four shares, and for the sister from the father two shares, and for the two sisters from the father and mother four shares, then The brother and sister from the father return to the two sisters from the father and mother their share. They complete the two-thirds, and there is nothing left for them. Something\n And there are two sisters from a father and a mother, and two sisters from a father,It is found in the saying of Ali and Abdullah: Two-thirds belong to the two sisters from the father and the mother, and to the grandfather what remains, but not to the two sisters from the father. Something And in the words of Zayd: Of six shares: two shares for the grandfather, two shares for the two sisters from the father and the mother, and two shares for the two sisters from the father. Two shares, then the two sisters from the father are returned to the two sisters from the father and the mother, so they complete the two-thirds, and nothing remains They have nothing to do with it.\n And there is a sister on the father’s side and a mother, and three sisters on the father’s side, and his grandfather: according to the statement of Ali and Abdullah: The sister on the father’s side and the mother’s side gets half. For the sisters on the father’s side, one-sixth completes the two-thirds, and for the grandfather what remains, and in Zayd’s statement: eighteen shares: for the grandfather, one-third. Six, and the sister from the father and mother gets three shares, and the sisters from the father get nine shares, then the sisters from the father return to Ali. The sister from the father and mother received six shares, so she completed the ninety-half share, and one share remained for her.\n And there are two sisters from the father and mother, and a brother, and two sisters from the father, and a grandfather: in Ali’s statement: for the two sisters from the father and mother are two-thirds, and for the grandfather. One-sixth, and whatever remains, between the brother and the two sisters, from the father to the male, is equal to the share of two females. And in Abdullah’s statement: for the two sisters. From the father and mother, two-thirds, and the remainder belongs to the grandfather.The brother and two sisters from the father have nothing.\n And there is a mother, a sister, and a grandfather in Ali’s saying: The sister gets half, the mother gets a third of what’s left, and the grandfather gets what’s left.\n And in the words of Zayd: Of the nine shares: for the mother a third is three, for the grandfather four, and for the sister two shares. He made it with them both. In the same position as a brother, and in the saying of Uthman: To the mother a third, to the grandfather a third, and to the sister a third, and in the saying of Ibn Abbas: To the mother a third, As for the grandfather, as long as he remains, the sister has nothing. A brother and sister with a grandfather do not inherit anything."
"31912","(31912) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Zaid was The grandfather shares up to a third with his brothers and sisters, and when he reaches one-third, he gives him a third, and the brothers and sisters have what He remains, and neither the maternal brother nor the maternal sister has anything with a grandfather, and the paternal brothers are divided among the paternal brothers, and he does not inherit from them. If he was a brother on the father’s side, a mother’s side, and a grandfather, he gave the grandfather half, and if they were brothers, he gave him a third. If they added He gave him a third, and what was left was for the brothers, and if it was a sister, he gave him, along with the sister, the third, and for the sister a third. And if they are two sisters, he gives them half, and he has half as long as the sharing is good for him, and if the duties of a woman and a mother are fulfilled And a husband who gave the people of the obligatory duties his due duties, and what was left was divided among the brothers and sisters, so if a third of what was left was better for him. Of the share, he gives him a third of what remains, and if the share is good for him, he gives him the share, even if it is a sixth of all If the money is better for him than sharing it, he gives him a sixth, and if the sharing is better for him than a sixth of all the money, he gives him The share"
"31913","(31913) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar and Abdullah: They did not give preference to either mother. Very seriously"
"31914","(31914) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ubaidah, He said: I find it difficult to be serious about two hundred cases."
"31915","(31915) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: I memorized it from Omar. Hundreds of different cases in Al-Jadd."
"31916","(31916) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Amr Al-Kharifi: That a man asked Ali from an obligation? He said: Bring it if there is no grandfather in it."
"31917","(31917) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of a man from Murad, who said: I heard Ali say: Whoever wants to encounter the germs of Hell, let him make a dispute between grandfather and brotherhood."
"31918","(31918) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We came to Shurayh and asked him? Then the one on his head said: He does not say anything about the grandfather."
"31919","(31919) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Take seriously what the people have agreed upon. Meaning: the saying of Zaid."
"31920","(31920) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id: That Umar wrote about the matter of seriousness and distress in Then he began to ask his Lord for help. When he was stabbed, he called for the shoulder and erased it. Then he said: Indeed, I had written a letter in the grave. And Al-Kalala, and I decided to restore you to what you were upon, but they did not know what was on your shoulder."
"31921","(31921) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed, who said: A man from Murad narrated to me, on the authority of Ali, who said: He who loves To be plunged into the germs of Hell, to judge between brothers and grandfathers."
"31922","(31922) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qabisya, who said: The grandfather came with the mother and the son’s son after The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Abu Bakr, and she said: My son’s son and my daughter’s son have died, and I have been informed that I have a right. Abu Bakr said: I do not find any truth in you in the Book of God, and I have not heard anything about you from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And I will ask the people. He said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba testified that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a sixth, so he said: Who? Is he witnessing with you? He said: Muhammad bin Muslim, so he testified and gave her a sixth, and the grandmother who disagreed with her came to Omar, so he gave her a sixth, and he said : If you meet, it is between you.\n Muammar added: And whichever of you is alone with it, it is for her. (Tirmidhi 2100)"
"31923","(31923) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he gave the grandfather a sixth. (Ibn Majah 2725. Saeed bin Mansour 83)"
"31924","(31924) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Munib Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, he said: Ibn Buraidah narrated to me, On the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed the grandfather with a sixth if it had no son. (Abu Dawud 2887, Darqutni 74)"
"31925","(31925) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Umair told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The grandfather. In the same position as the mother, she inherits what the mother inherits."
"31926","(31926) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He fed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted three grandmothers and said: I said to Abraham: Who? He said: His paternal grandmothers: his mother’s mother, and his father’s mother, and his maternal grandmother.\n(Abu Dawud 3550 Darmi 2935)"
"31927","(31927) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Three grandmothers inherit from the grandmothers, and the most numerous grandmothers in lineage. I am entitled to one-sixth."
"31928","(31928) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer, who said: If four grandmothers come together, the maternal father’s mother will not inherit."
"31929","(31929) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Three grandmothers inherit: two grandmothers from From the mother's side, his grandfather from the father's side."
"31930","(31930) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Grandmothers inherit All four."
"31931","(31931) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Sahm Al-Faraidi, he said: Jabir bin Zayd used to inherit four grandmothers."
"31932","(31932) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about four grandmothers? He said: Three of them will inherit, and my father’s mother will be cancelled."
"31933","(31933) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to leave nine grandmothers as an inheritor, and he said: If one Grandmothers are closer, so they are closer to her."
"31934","(31934) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to leave three grandmothers as an inheritor, and he would say: I am sure of them. She was closer, so he is hers rather than the other, so if they are level, then he is between them."
"31935","(31935) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Ibrahim said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made He said hello to his two grandfathers on his mother’s side, and two grandmothers on his father’s side, one-sixth. Za’idah said: I said to Mansour: The one from before His father: His father’s mother, and his mother’s mother? He said: Yes."
"31936","(31936) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Ibrahim said: If the grandmothers are of the same type One, some of them are closer to the maximum fall."
"31937","(31937) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said: Grandmothers inherit one-sixth, so if they are One, two, or three, and between them there is an arrow, according to the saying of Ali and Zaid, and if they come together, they are three grandmothers. The deceased is prescribed equally. He said: Between them is a share that is the maternal grandfather, and the paternal grandfather: the mother of his father, and the mother of his mother, and in the saying Abdullah: If three grandmothers come together, they are one-sixth, and if some of them are closer in lineage, some of them are not. Some mothers."
"31938","(31938) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Four grandmothers came. They go back and forth until Masruq inherited three, and subtracted his mother’s father’s mother."
"31939","(31939) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab: Two grandmothers came A share, so he divided a sixth between them."
"31940","(31940) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abdullah used to inherit grandmothers, even if they were Ten, and he says: It was only arrows that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed them. (Abdul Razzaq 19093)"
"31941","(31941) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Four grandmothers who lived together came to Masruq, and he inherited. Three, and he subtracted one: the mother’s father’s mother."
"31942","(31942) Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: A man died and left behind his two grandmothers: his mother’s mother, and his mother’s mother. His father, so Abu Bakr inherited from his mother’s mother, and left the other. A man from the Ansar said: I have left behind a woman, even if The two grandmothers died and their son is still alive. He did not inherit anything from the woman she inherited from him, and he inherited what she left behind: his father’s mother! So Abu Bakr inherited it, so he divided between them the sixth. (Saeed bin Mansour 82)"
"31943","(31943) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad: I heard from Kharijiya bin Zayd, Sulayman bin Yasar, and Talha bin Abd. Allah ibn Awf say: If the maternal grandmother is closer, then he has more right to it."
"31944","(31944) Waki’ told us, he said: Bashir told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Zayd, he said: So The maternal grandmother was more crippled than the paternal grandmother, and she had one-sixth of her inheritance. If the grandmother was from the father, The weaker than the grandmother by the mother, there was a sixth between them."
"31945","(31945) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, on the authority of Kharijiyah Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit said: If the grandmother on the mother’s side is more crippled than the grandmother on the father’s side, she gets one-sixth, and if The grandmother on the father's side was more crippled than the grandmother on the mother's side, the sixth being between them."
"31946","(31946) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Zaid, who said regarding grandmothers: Arrows are for those with The closest to them."
"31947","(31947) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The two grandmothers: whichever is closer, gets the inheritance."
"31948","(31948) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ammar, the client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit: Grandmothers: If the grandmother is closer, then she is more deserving."
"31949","(31949) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: He said: Abdullah: Grandmothers are not veiled except the mother."
"31950","(31950) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab heard that Omar inherited his grandfather. A man from Thaqif with her son."
"31951","(31951) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abi Amr Al-Shaybani, he said: He was a servant God will make the grandmother inherit with her son and her son are alive."
"31952","(31952) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salama Ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dama’i, he said Imran bin Husayn said: The grandmother inherits while her son is alive."
"31953","(31953) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He fed his grandfather a sixth of her children, so she was the first grandmother to inherit inheritance in Islam. (Abdul Razzaq 19093)q"
"31954","(31954) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Humaid bin Abdul Rahman al-Himyari, On the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Lahsaka al-Hanzali died and he left Haskaa and mothered Hasaka, so Abu Musa wrote to Omar about her. Ibn Al-Khattab, so Omar wrote to him saying that he inherited her with her son, one-sixth."
"31955","(31955) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama and Hammam, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: He inherited a grandfather with Her son\n(Abdul Razzaq 19095)"
"31956","(31956) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to inherit the grandfather while her son was alive."
"31957","(31957) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to inherit the grandfather along with her son, and her son. Alive"
"31958","(31958) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he said: The first kid who was fed a sixth-sixth in Islam was a kid. She fed him while her son was alive."
"31959","(31959) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih: He inherited two grandmothers: A mother's mother, a father's mother, and both of their sons are alive."
"31960","(31960) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father: He used to inherit The grandmother and her son are alive."
"31961","(31961) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: Her son denied her the inheritance."
"31962","(31962) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: that Uthman did not inherit from the father’s maternal grandmother and her son. Al-Zuhri said: Ibn Al-Zubayr died and did not leave any heirs."
"31963","(31963) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Abraham said: The grandfather does not inherit with her son if He was alive, according to Ali and Zaid.\n Abu Bakr said: I heard someone saying: People are like this."
"31964","(31964) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: None of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, inherited Peace be upon him, the grandmother and her son, except for Ibn Masoud."
"31965","(31965) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: that Zayd He did not give the grandmother an inheritance along with her son."
"31966","(31966) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Zayd: They were not made The grandmother has an inheritance with her son."
"31967","(31967) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Ibn Al-Mul’anah, his mother will inherit his inheritance. All of it"
"31968","(31968) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: The cursed woman has the entire inheritance of her children."
"31969","(31969) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said about a son The cursed: His entire inheritance goes to his mother, and if he does not have a mother, then it belongs to his concubine.\n And Abraham said: His entire inheritance is for his mother, and her intercourse with her will be free from her, and likewise the child of fornication and the child of a Christian woman and his mother. Muslim"
"31970","(31970) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah: Concerning Ibn Al-Mula’an: an inheritance To his mother. If his mother dies, he inherits from her and her heirs."
"31971","(31971) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ibn Al-Mul’an inherits. His mother. If he dies, whoever inherits his mother inherits from him."
"31972","(31972) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The inheritance of Ibn Al-Mul’an. For his mother"
"31973","(31973) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali and Zaid: Concerning Ibn al-Mula’an, they said: A third goes to his mother, and whatever remains is in the treasury."
"31974","(31974) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: She shall inherit her inheritance, and I will keep it in her inheritance. The treasury"
"31975","(31975) Ma’an bin Issa narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Urwa: Concerning Ibn al-Mul’ana and the child of adultery, if he dies: she inherits from him. His mother has her rights in the Book of God, and his brothers have their rights to his mother, and what remains is for the Muslims."
"31976","(31976) Issa told us, on the authority of Malik, that he reported something similar to that on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar."
"31977","(31977) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: What did Ibrahim bin Zayd think about Ibn What is the cursed one? So I said: He will join his mother, and Ibrahim said: He will join his father. So we came to Abdullah bin Hurmuz, and he wrote to us. Medina to the People of the House among whom this happened, and the answer came from their book: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him. He joined his mother.\n(Abdul Razzaq 12486)"
"31978","(31978) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair. He said: I wrote to a brother of mine in Banu Zurayq: To whom did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, make a ruling concerning Ibn al-Mul’anayn? So he wrote to me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judged him for his mother, in the same position as his father and in the same position. His mother\n(Abu Dawud 362; Abd al-Razzaq 12477)"
"31979","(31979) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, that they said in Ibn Al-Mala’an: His companionship is the support of his mother."
"31980","(31980) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Al-Mul’ana’ is asabtah. His mother’s descendants inherit from them and they inherit from you."
"31981","(31981) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ibn al-Mul```anah is a sect. His mother’s descendants, they inherit it and take care of it."
"31982","(31982) Asbat told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The person closest to his mother will inherit it."
"31983","(31983) Shababah told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, they said: Ibn Al-Mul’anain will inherit from whomever inherits it. His mother"
"31984","(31984) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hamza al-Zayat narrated to us, on the authority of a man called: Omar, on the authority of al-Sha`bi: Concerning Ibn Mala’an."
"31985","(31985) Waki’ told us, he said: Hamza said: Ibn Abi Layla used to say: For the paternal uncle two-thirds and for the maternal aunt one-third."
"31986","(31986) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Sha’bi say: Concerning Ibn Mula’naan. He died and left behind Ibn His brother, his maternal grandfather, said: The money is for the brother’s son."
"31987","(31987) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, that they said about Ibn Mala’an. He died and left his mother and brother to his mother. He said: Ali used to say: To the mother a third, and to the brother a sixth, and he would return what was left over to them. Two-thirds and a third, and Ibn Masoud used to say: The mother gets a third, and the brother gets a sixth, and he returns what remains to the mother.\n Abu Bakr said: So these words of all of them are made up of six."
"31988","(31988) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Manyal, on the authority of Iyas ibn Abd, Al-Muzani: He was asked About people on whom a house fell and they all died? So some of them inherited from others."
"31989","(31989) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Qatn ibn Abdullah al-Dhabi informed me: A woman rode Euphrates, and with her a son of hers, so they both drowned, and it is not known which of them died before its companion. So we brought Shurayh and informed us. Thus, he said: Each one of them inherited from its owner, and do not return to any of them anything that he inherited from its owner."
"31990","(31990) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, Amr bin Amr Al-Jashmi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba - who was a judge for Ibn Al-Zubayr - said that he inherited from the drowned people one from another."
"31991","(31991) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Omar, that he inherited a people who drowned, some of them From some"
"31992","(31992) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn: Some people drowned on the Manbij bridge, so Omar inherited Some of them from one another. Sufyan said to Abu Husayn: I heard it from Al-Sha’bi. He said: Yes."
"31993","(31993) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali: That the people of the House drowned. In a ship, Ali bequeathed some of them from others."
"31994","(31994) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ubaydī: A group of people fell upon them. A house, or they died of a plague, so the inheritance of one of them was inherited from another."
"31995","(31995) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Haris al-Bajlili, on the authority of his father: That a man and his son - or Two brothers - they were all killed on the day of Siffin. It is not known which of them was killed first. He said: So Ali bequeathed to each one of them. His companion\n(Abdul Razzaq 19152, Darami 3048)"
"31996","(31996) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Dhu’ib: A plague occurred in the Levant, and the entire family of the Prophet was dying, so Omar decreed that the highest inherit from the lowest, and if not... They will be like that. He inherited this from that, and that from that.\n Saeed said: Higher than lower: The dead among them would die and have placed his hand on another beside him."
"31997","(31997) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, the same."
"31998","(31998) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, Abraham said: Among the people they die without knowing Which of them died before? He said: Some of them inherit from others.\n Mansour said: It does not matter which of them you started if you inherited some of them from others."
"31999","(31999) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: The living would inherit from the dead, and the shipwrecked did not inherit from one another."
"32000","(32000) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, he said: It was in the letter of Omar bin Abd al-Aziz: He inherits every A human being and his heir from among the people."
"32001","(32001) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A woman came to him and said: My brother and my brother’s son went out in They built two ships and sank, so he left them nothing as an inheritance."
"32002","(32002) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Neither of them shall inherit from what He inherited something from his owner."
"32003","(32003) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, regarding all those who die, and it is not known which of them died. Before its companion, he said: They do not inherit from one another."
"32004","(32004) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jamm, on the authority of Ibrahim: that Ali inherited three who were shipwrecked. one of them from another while their mother was alive, so he inherited to their mother a sixth of the loins of each one of them, then they inherited to her a third of what he inherited. Each one of his companions, and he left what was left for the clan."
"32005","(32005) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi: He heard them explain They said: They inherit from one another. They said: If one of them dies and leaves behind money, and the other leaves nothing behind, he inherits and he inherits it. The one who did not leave anything behind the inheritance of the owner of the money, and the heirs of the owner of the money did not have anything."
"32006","(32006) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The inheritance of a foundling is equal to the inheritance of a foundling."
"32007","(32007) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Hasira, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, he said: When Ali stoned the woman, He said to her: This is your son, you shall inherit from him, and he shall inherit from you, but if he commits a crime, it is your responsibility."
"32008","(32008) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah: Concerning Ibn Al-Mula’an: His mother is his wife, her wife is his wife, and the child of adultery is in the same position as you."
"32009","(32009) Abbad told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The entire inheritance is for his mother - meaning: son The cursed one - and her intercourse with her will be removed from her, and likewise the child of adultery, and the child of a Christian woman whose mother is Muslim."
"32010","(32010) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The child of a cursed person and the child of adultery: they are inherited from the mother."
"32011","(32011) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The son of fornication was born in the same position as Ibn Al-Mul’naynah, or Ibn Al-Mul’nain is in his position. The child of adultery"
"32012","(32012) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Hisham bin Hubaira wrote to Shurayh. He asks him about the inheritance of the child of adultery? So he wrote to her: “Raise him to the ruler, for this is a night of sorrow and difficulty.”"
"32013","(32013) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The child of fornication and the child of those who curse each other. Their mother and maternal uncles inherit from them."
"32014","(32014) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: Concerning the hermaphrodite, he said: It is inherited from Before he cares"
"32015","(32015) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Katheer Al-Ahmasi narrated to us, on the authority of his father: That Mu’awiyah was brought in He sent them to Ali, and he said: He will inherit from where he urinates."
"32016","(32016) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd and Al-Hasan: Concerning the hermaphrodite, they said: He inherits from his wealth.\n Qatada said: So I mentioned that to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: Yes, and if he urinated on both of them, then it is from whichever of the above."
"32017","(32017) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Bashir al-Hamdani narrated to us, on the authority of al-Sha`bi: Concerning a newborn child who has no property. For the male, or for the female, he urinates from his navel! He said: He has half the share of a female and half the share of a male."
"32018","(32018) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Adni, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: In a hermaphrodite, inheritance is given. From his intestines, and if he ingests both of them, then from whichever of them came before."
"32019","(32019) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman did not inherit Al-Hamil"
"32020","(32020) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Talaq, on the authority of his father, he said: I met the Companions in the time of Ali and Uthman, no. They inherit."
"32021","(32021) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: The lamb does not inherit except with a clear proof."
"32022","(32022) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Thawban: Omar wrote that polytheism should not be inherited from his children."
"32023","(32023) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It was written to Shurayh that no descendant would inherit except With what we have shown."
"32024","(32024) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, who said: It was mentioned to Muhammad that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about The Companions: They do not inherit except with the testimony of witnesses. He said: Then Muhammad said: The Muhajireen and Ansar inherited inheritance according to their lineage, which was In the pre-Islamic era, I deny that Umar wrote about this."
"32025","(32025) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to inherit each other through the ties of kinship that they continue. With it"
"32026","(32026) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Iyas bin Abbas, on the authority of a sheikh of his people: that Abu Sulayman, a brother of his, drowned. It was said to him: Rashid, so Banu Zubaid and Banu Asad disputed over him, so they rose to Masruq, and he said: Masruq to Banu Asad: Do you bear witness that he used to deprive himself of what a brother deprives of his sister? They testified to that, so he gave it to Abu Suleiman. His inheritance"
"32027","(32027) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash, he said: My father was a pregnant woman, and his brother died, so he inherited it stolen from him."
"32028","(32028) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: Every lineage is connected In Islam, he is an inheritor."
"32029","(32029) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he is of known lineage, he is connected and heirs. It means: the pregnant woman."
"32030","(32030) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`baa, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about al-Hamil? They said: He does not inherit except with clear evidence."
"32031","(32031) Abdul Rahim bin Abdul Rahman Al Muharbi narrated to us, saying: Zaydah bin Qadamah narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us. Ibn Abi Al-Sha’tha’i said: A woman from a Muharib Jalaib acknowledged the lineage of her brother, a Julaib, so Abdul Rahman bin Utba inherited from him. Her sister"
"32032","(32032) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Atiyya told us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about the Lamb who evaluates the evidence. He is his brother. He said: He will inherit it according to the Book of God."
"32033","(32033) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Juma’, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If The apostate is an apostate and his children inherit him."
"32034","(32034) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali: He brought an imported Al-Ijli had apostatized, and he offered to convert to Islam, but he refused, so he killed him and placed his inheritance among his Muslim heirs.\n(Abdul Razzaq 1929. Dharmi 3075)"
"32035","(32035) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali: Concerning the inheritance of the apostate: to his heirs from Muslims"
"32036","(32036) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: Concerning the inheritance of the apostate, It is for his Muslim heirs, not for his family. Something"
"32037","(32037) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will be killed, and his inheritance will go to his heirs from Muslims"
"32038","(32038) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The inheritance of the apostate is made for his heirs."
"32039","(32039) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, who said: I asked Sa`id bin al-Musayyab about The inheritance of the apostate, will it be transferred? He said: What is connected? I said: His sons will inherit it. He said: We will inherit them, not ours."
"32040","(32040) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Mas`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Sabbah Musa bin Abi Kathir, he said: I heard Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab says: We will inherit the apostates from them, but they will not inherit from us."
"32041","(32041) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi and al-Hakam, who said: His inheritance shall be divided between His wife and his Muslim heirs."
"32042","(32042) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: If he joins Dar al-Harb and then returns before his inheritance is divided Or the ruler frees the mothers of his children and his wife, and he has more right to them."
"32043","(32043) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Muslims used to perfume their people. The apostate inherits his inheritance. Meaning: if he is killed."
"32044","(32044) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib: That his commander - a man from Banu Mudlij He killed his son, so Omar ibn al-Khattab took with him a hundred camels: thirty camels, thirty jadis, and forty camels. And he said to my father who was killed: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: A murderer has no inheritance. (Ibn Majah 2446. Malik 867)"
"32045","(32045) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: The murderer does not inherit."
"32046","(32046) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar said: The one who kills intentionally or by mistake does not inherit."
"32047","(32047) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: A man killed his brother. He made a mistake, so Ibn Abbas was asked about that? He did not inherit anything from him, and he said: No murderer inherits anything."
"32048","(32048) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Prophet’s prayers and peace be upon him decided May God bless him and grant him peace: A murderer does not inherit any of the blood money from the one who kills his relative, intentionally or accidentally.\n Al-Zuhri said: The murderer does not inherit anything from the blood money of the one he kills, even if it is a son or parent, but he inherits from his wealth, because God knows that people kill one another, and it is not appropriate for anyone to sever the inheritances that He has appointed."
"32049","(32049) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Abdi, on the authority of Ali, who said: He does not inherit. The killer"
"32050","(32050) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: The murderer does not inherit anything from the blood money of the one who kills."
"32051","(32051) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The murderer does not inherit from the blood money nor from the wealth. Something"
"32052","(32052) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to not leave the murderer as heirs, and he thought that He blocks it."
"32053","(32053) Hammad bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I asked Ibn Shihab about a murderer inheriting something? He said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: The Sunnah has passed that the murderer does not inherit anything."
"32054","(32054) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Abi Aoun, who said: Muhammad said: Ibn Jubayr: The one who kills intentionally does not inherit anything from the blood money or anything else, and the one who kills by mistake does not inherit anything from the blood money. And he inherits from someone else, if so."
"32055","(32055) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of Urwa, he said: The murderer does not inherit."
"32056","(32056) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: A murderer does not inherit anything."
"32057","(32057) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If a man kills his son or brother, he does not He inherits it, and the closest people after him inherit it."
"32058","(32058) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he killed him by mistake, he inherited from his wealth, and he did not He inherits from his blood money, and if he kills him intentionally, he does not inherit from his wealth or from his blood money."
"32059","(32059) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he kills his guardian by mistake and inherits from his wealth, and does not inherit Of his blood money, and if he kills him intentionally, he does not inherit from his wealth or from his blood money."
"32060","(32060) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ali: Concerning A man killed his mother. He said: If it was a mistake, he inherits, and if it was intentional, he does not inherit.\n Waki` said: A man who kills intentionally or by mistake will not inherit from the blood money or from the wealth."
"32061","(32061) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The murderer does not inherit."
"32062","(32062) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The murderer does not inherit anything of his blood money, nor Of his money"
"32063","(32063) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The murderer does not inherit."
"32064","(32064) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The murderer does not inherit."
